{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_49","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/pwsh -NoProfile -Command \"pwsh.exe -NoProfile -NonInteractive -File './docs/receipts/hv/hv-r1-acquire.ps1' -Stage Primary\"","aggregated_output":"{\"Method\":\"workflow.sessionlog.updateTurn\",\"Name\":\"startup-audit\",\"ExitCode\":0,\"Receipt\":\"hv-r1-store-startup-audit.txt\",\"OutputCharacters\":464}\n{\"Method\":\"workflow.todo.get\",\"Name\":\"PLAN-HVPIPELINE-001\",\"ExitCode\":0,\"Receipt\":\"hv-r1-store-PLAN-HVPIPELINE-001.txt\",\"OutputCharacters\":16628}\n{\"Method\":\"workflow.todo.get\",\"Name\":\"REMED-HVPIPELINE-001\",\"ExitCode\":0,\"Receipt\":\"hv-r1-store-REMED-HVPIPELINE-001.txt\",\"OutputCharacters\":19282}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_52","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/pwsh -NoProfile -Command \"pwsh.exe -NoProfile -NonInteractive -File './docs/receipts/hv/hv-r1-inspect.ps1' -Task Read -Path './docs/architecture/SessionTurn-Review-AgentContext-Architecture-Amendment-1-Durable-HV.md' -Start 301 -Count 200\"","aggregated_output":"SOURCE ./docs/architecture/SessionTurn-Review-AgentContext-Architecture-Amendment-1-Durable-HV.md totalLines=2785\n301: - W-06 Crash or failure inside the finalization transaction: it rolls back; the request stays `Finalizing` and the sweep runs finalization again.\n302: - W-07 Crash after the finalization commit, before any stream delivers its notification: the notification row is durable; streams and pollers replay it by sequence (R-16).\n303: - W-08 Crash after an incident row commits, before triage filing: the incident stays `Pending`; the sweep files it (FileHvIncidentCommand).\n304: - W-09 Crash after triage accepts a filing, before the report id is recorded: the retry files again under the same `dedupeKey`, which joins the same triage group (L-03).\n305: - W-10 Cancel racing finalization, claim, or close: all of them change the request row inside SerializableWrite, so one commits first and the other sees the committed state (R-28).\n306: - W-11 Two workers claiming one request: the claim is a conditional update on the request's state and version inside SerializableWrite; exactly one claim commits.\n307: - W-12 The audit ledger becomes unavailable during a run: AppendHvRunOutputCommand refuses with 503 `audit_unavailable` and writes nothing; the worker stops the reviewer process (a hard stop, S-29), cannot record the failure while the ledger is down, and the lease expiry later queues a new attempt; nothing is ever reported complete without its audit rows.\n308: \n309: ## 10. Configuration: `HostileValidationOptions`\n310: \n311: Section `Mcp:HostileValidation`, declared under the canonical root as `QBrainAi: HostileValidation:` in `appsettings.yaml` and projected onto `Mcp:` by `CanonicalSectionProjectionProvider`, as foundation section 6.2 declares `AgentContext`; class `HostileValidationOptions` in `src/QBrainAi.Services/HostileValidation/HostileValidationOptions.cs` with `SectionName = \"Mcp:HostileValidation\"`, `Validate()`, and `ValidateOnStart()`; per instance through `McpInstanceResolver`.\n312: \n313: - `Reviewers` (list): exactly one entry for each of `Cline`, `Copilot`, `Claude`, `Codex`, and `Grok` (S-02); each entry has `Enabled` (default true), `ExecutionStrategy` (an existing strategy name, `src/QBrainAi.Services/Services/IAgentExecutionStrategy.cs:6-46`), `AgentPath` (the CLI to launch), `Model` (null means the CLI's default model, recorded from the runtime provenance; Copilot needs a configured model, because its default `auto` routes each prompt to a model of its own choosing, which two probe prompts of 2026-10-16 showed by landing on `mai-code-1.1-flash` and `gpt-6-luna`, and it refuses `--reasoning-effort` without an explicit model, so V-7 could not hold, VI-02), `Effort` (null means the highest effort the reviewer's CLI accepts, verified on 2026-10-16 (VI-08): Codex `max` (its rollout recorded `effort` `max`), Claude `max` (its transcript recorded `effort` `max`), Cline `xhigh` (the highest `--thinking` level), Grok `xhigh` (Grok 1.0.60 refuses `max`: \"unknown effort level 'max'; use one of: xhigh, high, medium, low\"), and Copilot `max` (the highest `--reasoning-effort` value, which the configured model's NONCE proves); develop's one-shot constants at `OneShotCliAgentExecutionStrategy.cs:23-26` differ for Codex (`xhigh`) and Grok (`max`, which Grok refuses), problem P9), and `MaxConcurrentRuns` (default 1, 1..8).\n314: - `MaxTurnsPerRequest` (default 200, 1..2000).\n315: - `MaxAttemptsPerRequest` (default 3, 1..10).\n316: - `LeaseDuration` (default 5 minutes) and `HeartbeatInterval` (default 60 seconds; must be less than half of `LeaseDuration`).\n317: - `OutputFlushInterval` (default 250 milliseconds, 50..5000) and `OutputFlushBytes` (default 65536, 1024..4194304); the default interval is kept only after its storage cost is measured (VI-05).\n318: - `PollInterval` (default 2 seconds) and `WorkerEnabled` (default true).\n319: - There is no execution timeout and no output size limit (R-11, S-22: \"Output should be captured live and streamed\").\n320: - Startup validation fails on an unknown or duplicate reviewer id, a missing one of the five, an unknown execution strategy, an enabled Copilot entry without a configured `Model`, or a value outside its range.\n321: - Seeding: at startup each reviewer entry is inserted as an `HvReviewer` row when the workspace has none for its id (readiness `Unverified`); an existing row is never overwritten, because UpdateHvReviewerCommand is the real-time management surface (S-02), the pattern develop uses for agent definitions seeded per workspace (`SeedWorkspaceAgentsAsync`, `src/QBrainAi.Services/Services/IAgentPoolService.cs:83`).\n322: \n323: ## 11. Shared components (new, each defined once)\n324: \n325: The foundation's shared components (foundation section 3.5) are reused unchanged: SerializableWrite, IdempotentCreate with PayloadFingerprint, ReadableKeyAllocator, PagedQuery with PageBounds, ClassifiedErrorException with ErrorCodes, SecretRedactor, ContentHasher, TurnLocator, TurnWritePipeline, ScoreLexeme, ScoreVerdict, and WorkspaceResolutionBehavior. The components below are new; each has one implementation, one test class named for it, and one diagram here, and every unit that uses one draws it as a single call node.\n326: \n327: ### 11.1 FencedLease (namespace `QBrainAi.Support.Mcp.Storage.Leases`)\n328: \n329: Claims, renews, and takes over the lease of one row, and guards every fenced write, following develop's handoff-ingestion pattern (`HandoffIngestionService.cs:724-735,782-807`). Operations: `Claim(row, owner, duration)` (only when the row has no lease or an expired one; the fence token increments), `Renew(row, owner, fence, duration)`, `Guard(row, owner, fence)` (the precondition of every fenced write), `Release(row, owner, fence)`. Each runs inside the caller's SerializableWrite. Used by ClaimHvRunCommand, RecordHvRunHeartbeatCommand, AppendHvRunOutputCommand, CloseHvRunOutputCommand, FailHvRunCommand, and ExpireHvRunLeasesCommand.\n330: \n331: ```mermaid\n332: flowchart TD\n333:     S([\"FencedLease: operation, row, owner, fence\"]) --> OP{\"Operation?\"}\n334:     OP -->|Claim| CL{\"Lease absent or expired?\"}\n335:     CL -->|no| E1([\"held: another owner holds a live lease\"])\n336:     CL -->|yes| CT[\"Set owner and expiry, increment the fence token\"]\n337:     CT --> OK1([\"claimed: the new fence token\"])\n338:     OP -->|\"Renew, Guard, or Release\"| G{\"Owner and fence equal the stored ones?\"}\n339:     G -->|no| E2([\"stale_fence: nothing changed\"])\n340:     G -->|yes| W{\"Operation?\"}\n341:     W -->|Renew| RN[\"Extend the expiry\"]\n342:     RN --> OK2([\"renewed\"])\n343:     W -->|Guard| OK3([\"guarded: the caller's write proceeds\"])\n344:     W -->|Release| RL[\"Clear owner and expiry\"]\n345:     RL --> OK4([\"released\"])\n346: ```\n347: \n348: ### 11.2 GzipCodec (namespace `QBrainAi.Support.Mcp.Storage.Compression`)\n349: \n350: `Compress(bytes)` returns one GZIP member; `Decompress(bytes)` returns the original bytes; `RoundTrip(original, compressed)` decompresses and compares length and SHA-256 (through ContentHasher's hex form over raw bytes) and fails with `evidence_corrupt` on any difference, so no compressed blob is stored unverified. It follows `DataAuditLogEntity`'s encode and decode (`DataAuditLogEntity.cs:119-147`); that entity's private copy is context, not work. Used by SubmitHvRequestCommand (request evidence), AppendHvRunOutputCommand (chunks), FinalizeHvRequestCommand (result document, chunk verification), and GetHvEvidenceQuery and OrderedEventReplay (reads).\n351: \n352: ```mermaid\n353: flowchart TD\n354:     S([\"GzipCodec: operation, bytes\"]) --> OP{\"Operation?\"}\n355:     OP -->|Compress| C[\"Write one GZIP member at the configured level\"]\n356:     C --> RT[[\"GzipCodec RoundTrip on the result\"]]\n357:     RT -->|equal| OK1([\"compressed bytes\"])\n358:     RT -->|different| E1([\"evidence_corrupt\"])\n359:     OP -->|Decompress| D{\"Valid GZIP member?\"}\n360:     D -->|no| E2([\"evidence_corrupt\"])\n361:     D -->|yes| OK2([\"original bytes\"])\n362:     OP -->|RoundTrip| R[\"Decompress, compare length and SHA-256 with the original\"]\n363:     R -->|equal| OK3([\"equal\"])\n364:     R -->|different| E3([\"evidence_corrupt\"])\n365: ```\n366: \n367: ### 11.3 AuditLedgerGuard (namespace `QBrainAi.Support.Mcp.Storage.Auditing`)\n368: \n369: `EnsureAvailable()` checks, inside the caller's transaction, that the `DataAuditLogs` table is writable and refuses with 503 `audit_unavailable` (`retryable: true`) when it is not, closing for HV the skip of `McpDbContext.AppendAuditRows` (`McpDbContext.cs:1507-1538`); `RecordRead(entityKind, entityKey, actor)` adds one ledger row with action `read` for an evidence access (R-19). Every HV unit calls `EnsureAvailable()` before any other step that writes; GetHvEvidenceQuery, GetHvResultQuery, and the output stream call `RecordRead` before returning bytes.\n370: \n371: ```mermaid\n372: flowchart TD\n373:     S([\"AuditLedgerGuard: operation\"]) --> A{\"DataAuditLogs writable in this transaction?\"}\n374:     A -->|no| E([\"503 audit_unavailable, retryable: nothing written\"])\n375:     A -->|yes| OP{\"Operation?\"}\n376:     OP -->|EnsureAvailable| OK1([\"available\"])\n377:     OP -->|RecordRead| R[\"Add one ledger row: action read, entity kind and key, actor, request id\"]\n378:     R --> OK2([\"read recorded with the caller's commit\"])\n379: ```\n380: \n381: ### 11.4 AgentIdentity (namespace `QBrainAi.Client.Agents`)\n382: \n383: `Normalize(name)` returns the reviewer id (`Cline`, `Copilot`, `Claude`, `Codex`, `Grok`) of a known alias, case-insensitively and with separators removed, or `Unknown` with the input's PascalCase form; `IsSameReviewer(a, b)` compares normalized ids. The alias table is R-08's; the PowerShell core's copy is kept equal by the golden contract `docs/context/agent-identity-contract.json` (`AgentIdentityGoldenContractTests` in C# and Pester), the foundation's language-boundary rule (foundation section 3.5.4).\n384: \n385: ```mermaid\n386: flowchart TD\n387:     S([\"AgentIdentity.Normalize: name\"]) --> B{\"Blank?\"}\n388:     B -->|yes| U([\"Unknown\"])\n389:     B -->|no| N[\"Lower-case, remove separators\"]\n390:     N --> K{\"In the alias table?\"}\n391:     K -->|yes| R([\"Reviewer id: Cline, Copilot, Claude, Codex, or Grok\"])\n392:     K -->|no| U2([\"Unknown, with the PascalCase form\"])\n393: ```\n394: \n395: ### 11.5 TurnSnapshotBuilder (namespace `QBrainAi.Support.Mcp.HostileValidation`)\n396: \n397: Builds the canonical review snapshot of one turn: its turn key, status, `requestClass`, query title and text, interpretation, response, actions, design decisions, files modified, requirements discovered, blockers, tags, context list, and processing dialog, in stored order, with `agentReview` and `hostileReview` left out (R-21), every text through SecretRedactor, serialized as canonical JSON, and hashed through ContentHasher. Used by SubmitHvRequestCommand (the snapshot and its hash on each `HvRequestTurn`) and FinalizeHvRequestCommand (V-2 re-hash).\n398: \n399: ```mermaid\n400: flowchart TD\n401:     S([\"TurnSnapshotBuilder: turn\"]) --> P[\"Project the listed fields in stored order; omit agentReview and hostileReview\"]\n402:     P --> R[[\"SecretRedactor on every text field\"]]\n403:     R --> J[\"Serialize as canonical JSON\"]\n404:     J --> H[[\"ContentHasher: SHA-256 of the stored normal form\"]]\n405:     H --> OK([\"snapshot JSON and snapshotSha256\"])\n406: ```\n407: \n408: ### 11.6 RequirementReferenceExtractor (namespace `QBrainAi.Support.Mcp.Requirements`)\n409: \n410: Extracts the requirement and use-case references of R-23 from the submitted context, in order of first appearance and without duplicates, and resolves each against the workspace's effective requirements (`client.Requirements.GetEffectiveRequirementsAsync`, the marker's requirements visibility rule) and use cases (by store id or exact title). Returns each reference with `kind`, `id`, `resolved`, and, when resolved, its title and the SHA-256 of its effective record. Used by SubmitHvRequestCommand.\n411: \n412: ```mermaid\n413: flowchart TD\n414:     S([\"RequirementReferenceExtractor: context text\"]) --> X[\"Scan for FR, TR, TEST ids, acceptance-criterion forms, and use-case references; keep first appearances\"]\n415:     X --> L{\"Any reference found?\"}\n416:     L -->|no| E([\"empty list\"])\n417:     L -->|yes| R[\"Resolve each against the effective requirements and the use cases\"]\n418:     R --> OK([\"ordered list: kind, id, resolved, title, sha256\"])\n419: ```\n420: \n421: ### 11.7 NotificationOutbox (namespace `QBrainAi.Support.Mcp.HostileValidation`)\n422: \n423: `Append(kind, hvRequestId, reviewerId, runId, payload)` runs inside the caller's SerializableWrite: it increments the workspace's `HvWorkspaceState.NextNotificationSequence`, inserts the `HvNotification` row with that sequence, and registers a post-commit wake-up on `IChangeEventBus` (R-16). Used by every unit whose change a caller observes.\n424: \n425: ```mermaid\n426: flowchart TD\n427:     S([\"NotificationOutbox.Append in the caller's transaction\"]) --> Q[\"Read and increment HvWorkspaceState.NextNotificationSequence\"]\n428:     Q --> I[\"Insert HvNotification with the sequence, kind, ids, and payload\"]\n429:     I --> W[\"Register the post-commit wake-up on IChangeEventBus\"]\n430:     W --> OK([\"appended: sequence; visible only when the caller commits\"])\n431: ```\n432: \n433: ### 11.8 OrderedEventReplay (namespace `QBrainAi.Support.Mcp.Streaming`)\n434: \n435: Serves a Server-Sent Events stream from durable ordered rows: parses `Last-Event-ID` (absent means from the beginning of the requested stream, a malformed value is 400 `validation_error` with `details.field` `Last-Event-ID`), sends every stored event after it in order with its `id:`, then waits on the `IChangeEventBus` wake-up (or a poll interval) and sends new rows; it sends a comment line every 15 seconds while idle so proxies keep the connection, and ends when the caller disconnects or the stream's source reaches a terminal event. Develop's event stream has no replay and no event ids (`src/QBrainAi.Support.Mcp/Controllers/EventStreamController.cs:27-92`); this component adds both without changing that controller. Used by StreamHvRunOutputQuery and StreamHvNotificationsQuery.\n436: \n437: ```mermaid\n438: flowchart TD\n439:     S([\"OrderedEventReplay: source, Last-Event-ID\"]) --> P{\"Last-Event-ID valid or absent?\"}\n440:     P -->|malformed| E([\"400 validation_error, details.field Last-Event-ID\"])\n441:     P -->|yes| RD[\"Read stored events after the position, in order\"]\n442:     RD --> SND[\"Send each event with its id\"]\n443:     SND --> T{\"Source terminal and all events sent?\"}\n444:     T -->|yes| END([\"stream ended with the terminal event\"])\n445:     T -->|no| WT[\"Wait for a wake-up or the poll interval; send a comment every 15 seconds while idle\"]\n446:     WT --> DC{\"Caller disconnected?\"}\n447:     DC -->|yes| END2([\"stream closed\"])\n448:     DC -->|no| RD\n449: ```\n450: \n451: ## 12. Data model (namespace `QBrainAi.Support.Mcp.Storage.Entities.HostileValidation`)\n452: \n453: Every entity is new, in `src/QBrainAi.Storage/Entities/HostileValidation/`, keyed by `WorkspaceId` first (every read is workspace-scoped and no read crosses workspaces, foundation section 3), soft-deleted through `IsDeleted` so that `McpDbContext` writes its audit ledger rows for it (R-19), and carries the root ids of every parent it hangs from (foundation section 3.1, \"Root ids\"). Lengths are the foundation's: an agent 64, a session id or request id 256, a readable key 128. Scores are `decimal` with precision 29 and scale 28, written and read as exact lexemes (ScoreLexeme). Every timestamp is UTC with offset, and the identifiers that carry a time use the UTC form `yyyyMMddTHHmmssZ` (D-08). Diagrams are in Addendum B.\n454: \n455: `HvWorkspaceState` (table `HvWorkspaceStates`, key `WorkspaceId`): one row per workspace, created on first use. `LastAssignedReviewerId` (16, null before the first assignment; the round-robin cursor, R-07), `NextNotificationSequence` (long, starts at 1, R-16), `StateVersion` (int).\n456: \n457: `HvReviewer` (table `HvReviewers`, key (`WorkspaceId`, `ReviewerId`)):\n458: \n459: - `ReviewerId` (16): `Cline`, `Copilot`, `Claude`, `Codex`, or `Grok`.\n460: - `Enabled` (bool), `ExecutionStrategy` (32), `AgentPath` (512), `ConfiguredModel` (128, null means the CLI default), `ConfiguredEffort` (32, null means the highest effort of section 10), `MaxConcurrentRuns` (int).\n461: - `ResolvedModel` (128) and `ResolvedEffort` (32): the runtime model and effort the last passing NONCE recorded from the reviewer's own provenance (P-04); null until a NONCE passes.\n462: - `Readiness` (16: `Unverified`, `Online`, `Offline`), `ReadinessReason` (64: the failure code that made it `Offline`, or the change that made it `Unverified`), `ReadinessChangedUtc`, `LastProbeRunId` (128), `OpenIncidentId` (128, the incident that made it `Offline`).\n463: - `ProbeRequestedUtc`: set when a NONCE is requested and cleared when ClaimHvRunCommand creates its probe run; a requested probe waits here, so a NONCE survives a restart before it is claimed.\n464: - `StateVersion` (int: optimistic concurrency for UpdateHvReviewerCommand), `CreatedUtc`, `UpdatedUtc`.\n465: \n466: `HvRequest` (table `HvRequests`, key (`WorkspaceId`, `HvRequestId`), `HvRequestId` = `hvr-<sessionId>-<yyyyMMddTHHmmssZ>`, `-<nn>` from the second key of one second, ReadableKeyAllocator):\n467: \n468: - Scope: `ScopeKind` (16: `Turn`, `Range`, `Session`), `Agent` (64) and `SessionId` (256) of the reviewed MCP session, `FromRequestId` and `ToRequestId` (256; equal for `Turn`, null for `Session`), `ExcludedSubmittingTurn` (bool: a session scope left the submitting turn out, R-05).\n469: - Submitter: `SubmitterKind` (16: `Agent`, `Operator`), the submitting turn key `SubmitterAgent` (64), `SubmitterSessionId` (256), `SubmitterRequestId` (256) (null for `Operator`), `SubmitterReviewerId` (16, AgentIdentity of `SubmitterAgent`, `Unknown` allowed), `OperatorName` (128, `Operator` only), `AuthorReviewerId` (16, AgentIdentity of the reviewed session's `Agent`, `Unknown` allowed; R-08).\n470: - Context: `Context` (text, as submitted; read surfaces redact it through SecretRedactor), `ContextFormat` (16: `Markdown`, `Yaml`, `Text`).\n471: - Idempotency: `IdempotencyKey` (128, unique with `WorkspaceId`), `PayloadSha256` (64, PayloadFingerprint of the client inputs: scope, submitter, context, context format).\n472: - State: `Status` (16: `Queued`, `Running`, `CancelRequested`, `Finalizing`, `Completed`, `Failed`, `Canceled`), `AssignedReviewerId` (16), `AttemptCount` (int), `FailureCode` (64), `CancelRequestedUtc`, `CreatedUtc`, `StartedUtc`, `CompletedUtc`, `StateVersion` (int).\n473: - Result (set only by FinalizeHvRequestCommand): `FinalizedRunId` (128), `HolisticCorrectness`, `HolisticCompleteness`, `HolisticVerdict` (16: `AGREE`, `DISAGREE`), `HolisticSummary` (text), `OverallVerdict` (16), `ThresholdCorrectness` and `ThresholdCompleteness` (the values in force, R-31), `ResultSha256` (64).\n474: - Indexes: (`WorkspaceId`, `Status`, `CreatedUtc`) for the claim order and the running query; (`WorkspaceId`, `Agent`, `SessionId`).\n475: \n476: `HvRequestTurn` (table `HvRequestTurns`, `long Id`): `WorkspaceId`, `HvRequestId` (FK (`WorkspaceId`, `HvRequestId`)), `Ordinal` (unique with the request; the turn's position in the session's turn order), the turn key `Agent`, `SessionId`, `RequestId` (root ids), `SnapshotSha256` (64, TurnSnapshotBuilder), `SnapshotBytes` (int), `RequestClassAtAdmission` (16), `HostileStatusAtAdmission` (16: shows an included `Unnecessary` turn, S-09), `Disposition` (16: `Pending`, `Reviewed`, `Released`). Unique filtered index (`WorkspaceId`, `Agent`, `SessionId`, `RequestId`) where `Disposition` is `Pending` (I-01).\n477: \n478: `HvRequestRequirementRef` (table `HvRequestRequirementRefs`, `long Id`): `WorkspaceId`, `HvRequestId` (FK), `Ordinal` (unique with the request), `Kind` (8: `FR`, `TR`, `TEST`, `AC`, `UC`), `RefId` (256), `Resolved` (bool), `Title` (512), `RecordSha256` (64).\n479: \n480: `HvRequestResponse` (table `HvRequestResponses`, `long Id`; replaces `AgentContextHvRequestItem`, A-04): `WorkspaceId`, `HvRequestId` (FK), `ResponseId` (128, FK (`WorkspaceId`, `ResponseId`) to `AgentResponses`), `PackageId` (128) and the response's turn key `Agent`, `SessionId`, `RequestId` (root ids; always a member turn), `Ordinal`, `Disposition` (16: `Pending`, `Graded`, `Closed`, `NotGraded`), `ClosedReason` (32: `rejected` or `superseded` when the response left the review through ResponseStatusTransition, `request_ended` when the request ended `Canceled` or `Failed`), `NotGradedReason` (32: `agent_context_disabled`), `GradeId` (128). Unique (`WorkspaceId`, `HvRequestId`, `ResponseId`); unique filtered (`WorkspaceId`, `ResponseId`) where `Disposition` is `Pending`.\n481: \n482: `HvRun` (table `HvRuns`, key (`WorkspaceId`, `RunId`); `RunId` = `hvrun-<hvRequestId>-<nn>` for a review, `hvprobe-<reviewerId>-<yyyyMMddTHHmmssZ>` with `-<nn>` from the second key of one second for a probe):\n483: \n484: - `Kind` (8: `Review`, `Probe`), `HvRequestId` (128, FK; null for `Probe`), `ReviewerId` (16), `Attempt` (int), `ExpectedModel` (128), `ExpectedEffort` (32), `ProbeNonce` (64, `Probe` only).\n485: - Ownership: `LeaseOwner` (256), `LeaseExpiresUtc`, `FenceToken` (long, FencedLease).\n486: - `Status` (16: `Claimed`, `Running`, `OutputClosed`, `Succeeded`, `Failed`, `Abandoned`, `Canceled`), `ProcessId`, `ClaimedUtc`, `StartedUtc`, `LastHeartbeatUtc`, `LastOutputUtc`, `EndedUtc`, `ExitCode`, `FailureCode` (64), `FailureDetail` (text, sanitized).\n487: - Output manifest: `OutputChunkCount` (int), `OutputLineCount` (long), `OutputBytes` (long, decompressed), `OutputChainSha256` (64: the chain hash after the last chunk, defined here once; for chunk n, SHA-256 over the previous chain value followed by chunk n's SHA-256, both lower-case hex, with the empty string before chunk 1).\n488: - Progress (R-18): `ProgressPercent` (decimal), `ProgressEtaSeconds` (int), `ProgressReportedUtc`.\n489: - Provenance: `RuntimeModel` (128), `RuntimeEffort` (32), and the reviewer's own turn `ReviewerAgent` (64), `ReviewerSessionId` (256), `ReviewerRequestId` (256), `VerdictRecordSha256` (64).\n490: - `StateVersion` (int). Unique filtered (`WorkspaceId`, `HvRequestId`) where `Status` is `Claimed`, `Running`, or `OutputClosed`: one live run per request.\n491: \n492: `HvRunOutputChunk` (table `HvRunOutputChunks`, `long Id`): `WorkspaceId`, `RunId` (FK), `HvRequestId` and `ReviewerId` (root ids), `Sequence` (unique with `RunId`, from 1 without gaps), `Payload` (bytes: one GZIP member of the batch's UTF-8 JSONL lines; null after removal), `LineCount` (int), `ByteCount` (int, decompressed), `Sha256` (64, decompressed bytes), `ChainSha256` (64), `FenceToken` (long, the fence the append held), `CreatedUtc`, `RemovedUtc`.\n493: \n494: `HvEvidence` (table `HvEvidence`, `long Id`): `WorkspaceId`, `HvRequestId` (FK), `Kind` (16: `Request`, the complete accepted request of section 13.3 written at admission; `Result`, the result document of section 13.4 without its embedded log, written at finalization; unique with the request), `Payload` (bytes, one GZIP member; null after removal), `ByteCount`, `CompressedBytes`, `Sha256` (64, decompressed), `ContentType` (64), `CreatedUtc`, `RemovedUtc`, `RemovedBy` (128), `RemovalReason` (2048).\n495: \n496: `HvTurnAssessment` (table `HvTurnAssessments`, `long Id`): `WorkspaceId`, `HvRequestId` (FK), `RunId` (128), `Ordinal` (the `HvRequestTurn` ordinal; unique with the request), the turn key (root ids), `Correctness`, `Completeness`, `Verdict` (16: `AGREE`, `DISAGREE`), `MappedReviewStatus` (16: the `hostileReview` status policy HvVerdictMapping stored: `Pass`, `Fail`, or `Other`), `Summary` (text).\n497: \n498: `HvFinding` (table `HvFindings`, `long Id`): `WorkspaceId`, `HvRequestId` (FK), `RunId`, `Ordinal` (unique with the request), `Scope` (16: `Turn`, `Holistic`), `TurnOrdinal` and the turn key (null for `Holistic`), `Outcome` (16: `FAIL`, `UNKNOWN`), `Category` (32: `defect`, `risk`, `missing-tests`, `unclear-requirements`, `insufficient-disclosure`, `out-of-scope`, `uncertainty`, the categories of develop's hostile-review findings, `src/QBrainAi.Services/Services/HostileReviewService.cs:19-22`), `Location` (2048), `RequirementRef` (256), `ClaimId` (64), `Evidence` (text), `Remediation` (text, required: S-13 \"adequest description to remediate\").\n499: \n500: `HvNotification` (table `HvNotifications`, key (`WorkspaceId`, `Sequence`)): `Kind` (32: `hv_queued`, `hv_started`, `hv_cancel_requested`, `hv_finalizing`, `hv_completed`, `hv_failed`, `hv_canceled`, `reviewer_online`, `reviewer_offline`, `reviewer_unverified`, `incident_filed`), `HvRequestId`, `ReviewerId`, `RunId`, `PayloadJson` (text), `CreatedUtc`.\nEXIT_CODE=0\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_51","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/pwsh -NoProfile -Command \"pwsh.exe -NoProfile -NonInteractive -File './docs/receipts/hv/hv-r1-inspect.ps1' -Task Read -Path '/home/sharpninja/.codex/plugins/cache/mcpserver-codex-plugin/mcpserver/1.120.0/skills/requirements/SKILL.md' -Start 171 -Count 400\"","aggregated_output":"SOURCE /home/sharpninja/.codex/plugins/cache/mcpserver-codex-plugin/mcpserver/1.120.0/skills/requirements/SKILL.md totalLines=548\n171: ```yaml\n172: method: workflow.requirements.createFr\n173: params:\n174:   id: FR-MCP-XXX-001\n175:   title: Acceptance criteria example\n176:   description: Requirement records preserve structured pass/fail criteria.\n177:   priority: high\n178:   area: MCP\n179:   acceptanceCriteria:\n180:     - id: ac-1\n181:       text: Round-trip preserves criterion text\n182:       isSatisfied: false\n183:     - id: ac-2\n184:       text: Evidence is retained when supplied\n185:       isSatisfied: true\n186:       evidence: tests/Services/RequirementAcceptanceCriteriaTests.cs\n187: ```\n188: \n189: To copy criteria from an execution TODO onto a requirement, call `workflow.requirements.copyAcceptanceCriteriaFromTodo`:\n190: \n191: ```yaml\n192: method: workflow.requirements.copyAcceptanceCriteriaFromTodo\n193: params:\n194:   kind: fr\n195:   id: FR-MCP-XXX-001\n196:   todoId: PLAN-MCP-001\n197: ```\n198: \n199: This maps to `POST /mcpserver/requirements/{kind}/{id}/acceptance-criteria/copy-from-todo` with body `{ \"todoId\": \"PLAN-MCP-001\" }`.\n200: \n201: ### Batch Create Or Update\n202: \n203: When creating or updating multiple records, prefer the atomic batch commands instead of Markdown ingestion. Batch commands accept YAML `records:` arrays and fail all records if any record is invalid, conflicts, or is missing during update.\n204: \n205: Use per-kind commands when every record is the same type:\n206: \n207: ```yaml\n208: type: request\n209: payload:\n210:   requestId: req-20260409T120002Z-createfr-batch-001\n211:   method: workflow.requirements.createFrBatch\n212:   params:\n213:     records:\n214:       - id: FR-MCP-004\n215:         title: Batch requirements\n216:         description: The system must accept multiple requirement records in one request.\n217:         priority: high\n218:       - id: FR-MCP-005\n219:         title: Atomic validation\n220:         description: The system must reject the whole batch when one record is invalid.\n221:         priority: high\n222: ```\n223: \n224: Use `workflow.requirements.updateFrBatch`, `createTrBatch`, `updateTrBatch`, `createTestBatch`, and `updateTestBatch` for per-kind batches. For mixed FR/TR/TEST arrays, use `workflow.requirements.createBatch` or `workflow.requirements.updateBatch` and include `kind: fr|tr|test` on each record.\n225: \n226: ### Updating an FR\n227: \n228: To modify an existing FR:\n229: \n230: ```yaml\n231: type: request\n232: payload:\n233:   requestId: req-20260409T120003Z-updatefr-001\n234:   method: workflow.requirements.updateFr\n235:   params:\n236:     id: FR-MCP-003\n237:     status: completed\n238:     notes: Implemented with HybridSearchService using all-MiniLM-L6-v2 embeddings\n239: ```\n240: \n241: ### Deleting an FR\n242: \n243: ```yaml\n244: type: request\n245: payload:\n246:   requestId: req-20260409T120004Z-deletefr-001\n247:   method: workflow.requirements.deleteFr\n248:   params:\n249:     id: FR-MCP-003\n250: ```\n251: \n252: ## Technical Requirements (TR)\n253: \n254: TR IDs require both `area` and `subarea` segments. The full ID format is `TR-<AREA>-<SUBAREA>-###`.\n255: \n256: ### Listing TRs\n257: \n258: ```yaml\n259: type: request\n260: payload:\n261:   requestId: req-20260409T120005Z-listtr-001\n262:   method: workflow.requirements.listTr\n263:   params:\n264:     area: MCP\n265:     subarea: PERF\n266: ```\n267: \n268: ### Creating a TR\n269: \n270: ```yaml\n271: type: request\n272: payload:\n273:   requestId: req-20260409T120006Z-createtr-001\n274:   method: workflow.requirements.createTr\n275:   params:\n276:     id: TR-MCP-PERF-001\n277:     title: API response time SLA\n278:     description: All API endpoints must respond within 500ms at p99\n279:     priority: high\n280:     area: MCP\n281:     subarea: PERF\n282:     notes: Measured at gateway, excluding network transit time\n283: ```\n284: \n285: ### Updating a TR\n286: \n287: ```yaml\n288: type: request\n289: payload:\n290:   requestId: req-20260409T120007Z-updatetr-001\n291:   method: workflow.requirements.updateTr\n292:   params:\n293:     id: TR-MCP-PERF-001\n294:     status: in_progress\n295:     notes: Baseline established at 320ms p99 under load test\n296: ```\n297: \n298: ### Deleting a TR\n299: \n300: ```yaml\n301: type: request\n302: payload:\n303:   requestId: req-20260409T120008Z-deletetr-001\n304:   method: workflow.requirements.deleteTr\n305:   params:\n306:     id: TR-MCP-PERF-001\n307: ```\n308: \n309: ## Test Requirements (TEST)\n310: \n311: ### Listing TEST Requirements\n312: \n313: ```yaml\n314: type: request\n315: payload:\n316:   requestId: req-20260409T120009Z-listtest-001\n317:   method: workflow.requirements.listTest\n318:   params:\n319:     area: MCP\n320: ```\n321: \n322: ### Creating a TEST Requirement\n323: \n324: ```yaml\n325: type: request\n326: payload:\n327:   requestId: req-20260409T120010Z-createtest-001\n328:   method: workflow.requirements.createTest\n329:   params:\n330:     id: TEST-MCP-001\n331:     title: Agent authentication unit test\n332:     description: Verify API key authentication rejects invalid tokens with 401\n333:     priority: critical\n334:     area: MCP\n335:     notes: Uses in-memory EF provider with CustomWebApplicationFactory\n336: ```\n337: \n338: ### Updating and Deleting TEST Requirements\n339: \n340: Follow the same pattern as FR: use `workflow.requirements.updateTest` and `workflow.requirements.deleteTest` with the same parameter shapes.\n341: \n342: ## Requirement Mappings\n343: \n344: Mappings link an FR to one or more TRs and TEST IDs in the current workspace, forming the traceability matrix.\n345: \n346: ### Listing Mappings\n347: \n348: ```yaml\n349: type: request\n350: payload:\n351:   requestId: req-20260409T120011Z-listmap-001\n352:   method: workflow.requirements.listMappings\n353:   params:\n354:     frId: FR-MCP-001\n355: ```\n356: \n357: ### Creating a Mapping\n358: \n359: ```yaml\n360: type: request\n361: payload:\n362:   requestId: req-20260409T120012Z-createmap-001\n363:   method: workflow.requirements.createMapping\n364:   params:\n365:     frId: FR-MCP-001\n366:     trIds:\n367:       - TR-MCP-ARCH-001\n368:     testIds:\n369:       - TEST-MCP-001\n370:     notes: Core authentication flow covered by ARCH constraint and unit test\n371: ```\n372: \n373: Legacy single-link `trId` and `testId` inputs are accepted for compatibility. Prefer `trIds` and `testIds` for all new calls.\n374: \n375: The result confirms the stored mapping:\n376: \n377: ```yaml\n378: type: result\n379: payload:\n380:   requestId: req-20260409T120012Z-createmap-001\n381:   result:\n382:     item:\n383:       frId: FR-MCP-001\n384:       trId: TR-MCP-ARCH-001\n385:       testId: TEST-MCP-001\n386:       createdAt: 2026-04-09T12:00:12Z\n387:       notes: Core authentication flow covered by ARCH constraint and unit test\n388: ```\n389: \n390: ### Deleting a Mapping\n391: \n392: ```yaml\n393: type: request\n394: payload:\n395:   requestId: req-20260409T120013Z-deletemap-001\n396:   method: workflow.requirements.deleteMapping\n397:   params:\n398:     frId: FR-MCP-001\n399:     trId: TR-MCP-ARCH-001\n400: ```\n401: \n402: ## Document Generation\n403: \n404: To generate formatted requirements documents from the current workspace database slice:\n405: \n406: ```yaml\n407: type: request\n408: payload:\n409:   requestId: req-20260409T120014Z-gendoc-001\n410:   method: workflow.requirements.generateDocument\n411:   params:\n412:     format: markdown\n413:     docType: matrix\n414: ```\n415: \n416: Valid `docType` values:\n417: \n418: - `functional` - numbered list of all FR entries with status and description\n419: - `technical` - numbered list of all TR entries grouped by area/subarea\n420: - `testing` - numbered list of all TEST entries with linked FR IDs\n421: - `matrix` - traceability matrix table: FR × TR × TEST × status\n422: - `all` - complete export package\n423: \n424: ```yaml\n425: type: result\n426: payload:\n427:   requestId: req-20260409T120014Z-gendoc-001\n428:   result:\n429:     content: |\n430:       # Requirement Traceability Matrix\n431: \n432:       | FR ID      | TR ID           | TEST ID      | Status |\n433:       |------------|-----------------|--------------|--------|\n434:       | FR-MCP-001 | TR-MCP-ARCH-001 | TEST-MCP-001 | done   |\n435:       | FR-MCP-002 | TR-MCP-ARCH-002 | TEST-MCP-003 | open   |\n436:     format: markdown\n437:     docType: matrix\n438:     generatedAt: 2026-04-09T12:00:14Z\n439: ```\n440: \n441: ### Wiki Export\n442: \n443: Use `format: wiki` with `docType: all` to export wiki files directly into the workspace. The normal result returns metadata, not archive bytes. Files are written under `docs/Project/wiki/azure` and `docs/Project/wiki/github`. Each folder includes `.mcp-requirements-manifest.json`; Azure also includes `.order`; GitHub also includes `_Sidebar.md` and `_Footer.md`. When an older REPL cannot serialize the metadata result, the wrapper may return `contentBase64` with `contentType: application/json`; decode it to read the same export metadata.\n444: \n445: ```yaml\n446: type: request\n447: payload:\n448:   requestId: req-20260409T120014Z-gendoc-wiki-001\n449:   method: workflow.requirements.generateDocument\n450:   params:\n451:     format: wiki\n452:     docType: all\n453: ```\n454: \n455: ```yaml\n456: type: result\n457: payload:\n458:   requestId: req-20260409T120014Z-gendoc-wiki-001\n459:   result:\n460:     format: wiki\n461:     docType: all\n462:     generatedAtUtc: 2026-04-09T12:00:14Z\n463:     outputRoot: F:\\GitHub\\McpServer\\docs\\Project\\wiki\n464:     files:\n465:       - relativePath: azure/Home.md\n466:         fullPath: F:\\GitHub\\McpServer\\docs\\Project\\wiki\\azure\\Home.md\n467:         contentType: text/markdown\n468:         lastModifiedUtc: 2026-04-09T12:00:14Z\n469: ```\n470: \n471: ## Bulk Ingestion\n472: \n473: To import requirements from an existing Markdown document:\n474: \n475: ```yaml\n476: type: request\n477: payload:\n478:   requestId: req-20260409T120015Z-ingest-001\n479:   method: workflow.requirements.ingestDocument\n480:   params:\n481:     content: |\n482:       ## FR-MCP-010: GraphRAG ingestion\n483:       The system must support ingestion of raw text into the GraphRAG corpus.\n484:       Priority: high | Area: MCP | Status: pending\n485: \n486:       ## TR-MCP-GRAPH-001: Chunked text embedding\n487:       Ingested text must be split into chunks and embedded using all-MiniLM-L6-v2.\n488:       Priority: high | Area: MCP | Subarea: GRAPH | Status: pending\n489:     format: markdown\n490: ```\n491: \n492: To import wiki documents, pass a path-keyed `documents` map and include `lastModifiedUtc` per entry when available. Use `sourceFormat: auto` or `wiki`; set `preferredWikiFormat: azure|github` only when the Azure and GitHub timestamp checks disagree. The server compares both `.mcp-requirements-manifest.json` `generatedAtUtc` values and the latest `lastModifiedUtc` per platform. If both checks agree, the newer platform is selected. If they disagree and no preference is supplied, import fails. The selected platform folder is authoritative: missing records are deleted, changed records are updated, new records are created, and identical records are ignored.\n493: \n494: ```yaml\n495: type: request\n496: payload:\n497:   requestId: req-20260409T120015Z-ingest-wiki-001\n498:   method: workflow.requirements.ingestDocument\n499:   params:\n500:     format: wiki\n501:     sourceFormat: wiki\n502:     preferredWikiFormat: github\n503:     documents:\n504:       github/.mcp-requirements-manifest.json:\n505:         content: '{\"generatedAtUtc\":\"2026-04-09T12:00:14Z\"}'\n506:         lastModifiedUtc: 2026-04-09T12:00:14Z\n507:       github/Functional-Requirements.md:\n508:         content: |\n509:           # Functional Requirements (MCP Server)\n510:         lastModifiedUtc: 2026-04-09T12:00:15Z\n511: ```\n512: \n513: The server parses the document, creates, updates, deletes, or ignores matching FR/TR/TEST/mapping records, and returns a summary:\n514: \n515: ```yaml\n516: type: result\n517: payload:\n518:   requestId: req-20260409T120015Z-ingest-001\n519:   result:\n520:     created: 2\n521:     updated: 0\n522:     skipped: 0\n523:     errors: []\n524: ```\n525: \n526: ## Error Handling\n527: \n528: Common error codes:\n529: \n530: - `requirement_not_found` - no requirement with the given ID\n531: - `requirement_already_exists` - ID already in use; update instead of create\n532: - `invalid_requirement_id` - ID does not match the expected regex for its type\n533: - `mapping_not_found` - mapping between the specified FR and TR does not exist\n534: - `invalid_mapping` - mapping references a non-existent FR, TR, or TEST ID\n535: - `document_generation_error` - failed to render the requested document format\n536: - `document_ingestion_error` - could not parse or persist the ingested document\n537: \n538: ## Workflow Recommendations\n539: \n540: When discovering or agreeing on new requirements during a session:\n541: \n542: 1. Create the FR record immediately using `workflow.requirements.createFr`\n543: 2. Create the corresponding TR records using `workflow.requirements.createTr`\n544: 3. Create the TEST record using `workflow.requirements.createTest`\n545: 4. Link them with `workflow.requirements.createMapping`\n546: 5. Include the new IDs in the session log turn tags via `workflow.sessionlog.updateTurn`\n547: \n548: Capture requirements as they emerge; do not defer to end of session. Requirements traceability is validated in CI and build failures result from missing mappings.\nEXIT_CODE=0\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
