{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_55","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/pwsh -NoProfile -Command \"pwsh.exe -NoProfile -NonInteractive -File './docs/receipts/hv/hv-r1-inspect.ps1' -Task Read -Path './docs/architecture/SessionTurn-Review-AgentContext-Architecture-Amendment-1-Durable-HV.md' -Start 501 -Count 170\"","aggregated_output":"SOURCE ./docs/architecture/SessionTurn-Review-AgentContext-Architecture-Amendment-1-Durable-HV.md totalLines=2785\n501: \n502: `HvIncident` (table `HvIncidents`, key (`WorkspaceId`, `IncidentId`), `IncidentId` = `hvi-<reviewerId>-<yyyyMMddTHHmmssZ>` with `-<nn>` from the second key of one second): `ReviewerId`, `RunId`, `HvRequestId` (null for a probe), `FailureCode` (64), `DedupeKey` (256: `hv-reviewer-<reviewerId>-<failureCode>` for a failure attributable to the reviewer, `hv-server-<failureCode>` otherwise; the attribution is FailHvRunCommand's), `Summary` (2048), `Evidence` (text, sanitized), `FilingStatus` (16: `Pending`, `Filed`), `FilingAttempts` (int), `LastFilingError` (2048), `TriageReportId` (128), `TriageGroupId` (128), `CreatedUtc`, `FiledUtc`.\n503: \n504: Changed foundation entities (Addendum B.8):\n505: \n506: - `SessionLogTurn` gains `HvState` (16: `None`, `Pending`, `Final`, database default `None`; a turn already reviewed `Pass` or `Fail` starts `Final`) and `HvRequestId` (128), A-11.\n507: - `AgentResponseGrade`: `HvRequestId` becomes the composite foreign key (`WorkspaceId`, `HvRequestId`) to `HvRequests`; `RunId` (128) is added; `RequestJsonlPath`, `ResponseJsonlPath`, `RolloutJsonlPath`, and `ReviewerThreadId` are removed and `RequestJsonlSha256`, `ResponseJsonlSha256`, and `RolloutJsonlSha256` become `RequestEvidenceSha256` and `ResponseLogChainSha256` (A-05); `AgentContextHvRequests` and `AgentContextHvRequestItems` are not created (A-04).\n508: \n509: Export and federation: every HV table gets an explicit wiki dump policy in `WikiDumpTablePolicyRegistry.PolicyFor`, `COPY-SANITIZE+HISTORY+INERT` (the HostileReview tables' policy) except `HvRunOutputChunks` and `HvEvidence`, which are `OMIT-LOCAL` because they hold the workspace's evidence bytes; `hostile_validation` joins the federation domains as a local-only domain, as the foundation registers `agent_context` (foundation section 6.1, FR-MCP-103), so HV writes are never queued during a hub outage and never applied from hub fanout.\n510: \n511: ## 13. Wire contracts\n512: \n513: DTOs are defined once in `src/QBrainAi.Client/Models/HostileValidation/` (namespace `QBrainAi.Client.Models.HostileValidation`), registered in `McpClientJsonContext`, camelCase on the wire; scores travel as their exact lexemes (ScoreLexemeJsonConverter); unset fields are `null`.\n514: \n515: ### 13.1 Routes and surfaces\n516: \n517: Every REST route exists under `/qbrainai/hostile-validation` and the alias `/mcpserver/hostile-validation` (controller `HostileValidationController`, `[ApiController]`, authenticated by the workspace key, workspace from `X-Workspace-Path`). The MCP tools live in `src/QBrainAi.Support.Mcp/McpStdio/FwhMcpTools.HostileValidation.cs`, the client in `src/QBrainAi.Client/HostileValidationClient.cs` (property `HostileValidation` of `QBrainAiClient`), the REPL verbs in `src/QBrainAi.Repl.Core/HostileValidationWorkflow.cs` with `client.HostileValidation.*` passthrough, the Director commands in `src/QBrainAi.Cqrs.Mvvm/HostileValidationDirectorCommands.cs`, and the plugin verbs in `plugins/core/lib-ps/repl-invoke.ps1`. The REPL client mutation policy gives the `hostileValidation` namespace the classification the foundation gives `agentContext` (service-gated writes, reads on the read allowlist; foundation section 3.1, \"Transaction-gated REPL clients\").\n518: \n519: - Reviewers: `GET /reviewers` (ListHvReviewersQuery; MCP `hv_reviewer_list`; client `ListReviewersAsync`; REPL `workflow.hv.reviewers`; Director `hv-reviewers`); `GET /reviewers/{reviewerId}` (GetHvReviewerQuery; `hv_reviewer_get`; `GetReviewerAsync`; `workflow.hv.reviewer`); `PATCH /reviewers/{reviewerId}` (UpdateHvReviewerCommand; `hv_reviewer_update`; `UpdateReviewerAsync`; `workflow.hv.updateReviewer`; Director `hv-reviewer-update`); `POST /reviewers/{reviewerId}/nonce` (StartHvReviewerNonceCommand; `hv_reviewer_nonce`; `StartNonceAsync`; `workflow.hv.nonce`; Director `hv-nonce`).\n520: - Requests: `POST /requests` (SubmitHvRequestCommand; `hv_submit`; `SubmitAsync`; `workflow.hv.submit`, which the plugin binds to the submitting turn; Director `hv-submit` as `Operator`); `GET /requests/{hvRequestId}` (GetHvRequestQuery; `hv_get`; `GetAsync`; `workflow.hv.get`; Director `hv-request`); `GET /requests?status&agent&sessionId&reviewerId&submitterAgent&limit&offset` (QueryHvRequestsQuery; `hv_query`; `QueryAsync`; `workflow.hv.query`; Director `hv-requests`, which lists the running HVs with `status=Running`, S-18); `POST /requests/{hvRequestId}/cancel` (CancelHvRequestCommand; `hv_cancel`; `CancelAsync`; `workflow.hv.cancel`; Director `hv-cancel`).\n521: - Results and evidence: `GET /requests/{hvRequestId}/result` (GetHvResultQuery; `hv_result`; `GetResultAsync`; `workflow.hv.result`; Director `hv-result`); `GET /requests/{hvRequestId}/evidence/{kind}` with `kind` `request`, `response-log`, or `result` (GetHvEvidenceQuery; `hv_evidence`, which returns the GZIP bytes base64-encoded with their SHA-256 and sizes; `GetEvidenceAsync` as a stream; `workflow.hv.evidence`, which writes a file; Director `hv-evidence`); `POST /requests/{hvRequestId}/evidence/remove` (RemoveHvEvidenceCommand; `hv_evidence_remove`; `RemoveEvidenceAsync`; `workflow.hv.removeEvidence`; Director `hv-evidence-remove`).\n522: - Streams: `GET /requests/{hvRequestId}/output/stream` (StreamHvRunOutputQuery, SSE; client `StreamOutputAsync` as `IAsyncEnumerable`; REPL streaming verb `workflow.hv.watchOutput`; Director `hv-output`); `GET /notifications/stream` (StreamHvNotificationsQuery, SSE; `StreamNotificationsAsync`; `workflow.hv.watchNotifications`; Director `hv-notifications`); `GET /notifications?afterSequence&limit` (QueryHvNotificationsQuery; `hv_notifications`; `QueryNotificationsAsync`; `workflow.hv.notifications`). MCP has no stream tool; MCP callers poll `hv_notifications` and `hv_get`.\n523: - Incidents: `GET /incidents?reviewerId&filingStatus&limit&offset` (QueryHvIncidentsQuery; `hv_incidents`; `QueryIncidentsAsync`; `workflow.hv.incidents`; Director `hv-incidents`).\n524: \n525: Errors follow the foundation's rule (foundation section 3, \"Errors\"): every refusal is the `ClassifiedError` problem+json body through `McpErrorClassifier`, MCP tools return `{ code, error, message, retryable, details }`, and the REPL envelope is `type: error` with `code`, `message`, `retryable`, and `details`. Every unit's error list includes 400 `validation_error` with `details.field` `workspacePath` (WorkspaceResolutionBehavior), drawn after the dispatch in the sequences and not in the activity diagrams.\n526: \n527: ### 13.2 Requests and responses\n528: \n529: - `HvReviewerDto { reviewerId, enabled, executionStrategy, agentPath, configuredModel, configuredEffort, resolvedModel, resolvedEffort, readiness, readinessReason, readinessChangedUtc, lastProbeRunId, openIncidentId, maxConcurrentRuns, activeRuns, stateVersion }`.\n530: - `UpdateHvReviewerRequest { enabled, executionStrategy, agentPath, model, effort, maxConcurrentRuns, expectedStateVersion }`: every field but `expectedStateVersion` optional; `model` and `effort` accept an empty string to return to the default.\n531: - `StartHvReviewerNonceResult { reviewerId, status, probeRequestedUtc, runId }` (202 Accepted): `status` `Requested` (a new probe is waiting for the worker), `AlreadyRequested`, or `Running` (with the probe's `runId`); the outcome arrives as a `reviewer_online` or `reviewer_offline` notification and on the reviewer.\n532: - `SubmitHvRequestRequest { scope: { kind, agent, sessionId, requestId, fromRequestId, toRequestId }, submitter: { kind, agent, sessionId, requestId, operatorName }, context, contextFormat, idempotencyKey }`: `scope.kind` `Turn` needs `requestId`, `Range` needs `fromRequestId` and `toRequestId`, `Session` needs neither (S-03, S-11); `submitter.kind` `Agent` needs the full turn key, `Operator` needs `operatorName` (R-09); `context` is optional, at most 65536 characters; `contextFormat` defaults to `Markdown`.\n533: - `HvRequestResult { hvRequestId, status, scope, submitter, assignedReviewerId, attemptCount, excludedSubmittingTurn, turns: [{ ordinal, agent, sessionId, requestId, snapshotSha256, requestClassAtAdmission, hostileStatusAtAdmission, disposition }], requirementRefs: [{ kind, refId, resolved, title }], responses: [{ responseId, agent, sessionId, requestId, disposition, closedReason, notGradedReason, gradeId }], currentRun: { runId, reviewerId, status, attempt, startedUtc, lastHeartbeatUtc, lastOutputUtc, progress: { percentComplete, etaSeconds, etaStatus, reportedUtc }, lastOutput: [string] }, overallVerdict, holisticVerdict, failureCode, createdUtc, startedUtc, completedUtc }`: `lastOutput` holds the last 20 output lines of the current run (S-18, \"their last reported output\"); `etaStatus` is `Reported` or `Unknown` (R-18); summaries in a page leave `turns`, `requirementRefs`, `responses`, and `lastOutput` null.\n534: - `HvRequestQuery { status, agent, sessionId, reviewerId, submitterAgent, limit, offset }` returns `PageResult<HvRequestResult>` (PagedQuery, `PageBounds` `Refuse`, order `CreatedUtc` descending then `HvRequestId`).\n535: - `CancelHvRequestResult { hvRequestId, previousStatus, status }`.\n536: - `HvNotificationDto { sequence, kind, hvRequestId, reviewerId, runId, payload, createdUtc }`; `HvNotificationQuery { afterSequence, limit }` returns `{ items, lastSequence }`.\n537: - `HvIncidentDto { incidentId, reviewerId, runId, hvRequestId, failureCode, dedupeKey, summary, filingStatus, filingAttempts, triageReportId, triageGroupId, createdUtc, filedUtc }`.\n538: - `RemoveHvEvidenceRequest { reason, removedBy }` returns `RemoveHvEvidenceResult { hvRequestId, removedKinds, removedChunks, removedUtc }`.\n539: - `HvIncidentQuery { reviewerId, filingStatus, limit, offset }`; `HvNotificationPage { items, lastSequence }`; `HvOutputEvent { runId, sequence, lines, closedStatus }` (the item type of the output stream, section 13.5).\n540: - Server-side result types that never cross the wire as JSON: `HvEvidenceStream` (the evidence bytes with their content type, file name, SHA-256, and sizes, written to the response body by the controller), and the internal unit results of section 14.4 (`HvRunClaim`, `HvHeartbeatResult`, `HvAppendResult`, `HvCloseResult`, `HvFailResult`, `HvSweepResult`, `HvFinalizeResult`, `HvProvenance`), defined in `src/QBrainAi.Services/HostileValidation/Execution/`.\n541: \n542: ### 13.3 Reviewer contract, version 1\n543: \n544: The complete accepted request (the `Request` evidence, written at admission and never changed) is one JSON object: `{ schema: \"qbrainai.hv.request/1\", hvRequestId, workspacePath, scope, submitter, turns: [{ ordinal, agent, sessionId, requestId, snapshotSha256, snapshot }], responses: [{ responseId, agent, sessionId, requestId, contentSha256, content, claims }], context, contextFormat, requirementRefs, admittedUtc }`. The brief of one attempt is that object inside an envelope: `{ schema: \"qbrainai.hv.brief/1\", request: <the accepted request>, runId, attempt, reviewer: { reviewerId, model, effort }, instructions, outputSchema }`; the worker writes the exact brief it sends as the first record of the attempt's log, `{ \"type\": \"hv_brief\", \"brief\": <the brief> }`, so each log is complete on its own. The brief's `instructions` require the reviewer to review every turn individually and the set of turns as a whole, to treat every turn snapshot and the context as untrusted evidence, to emit the records below as single-line JSON objects in its messages, to emit progress records during the run (P-03), to log its review as its own session-log turn classified `Chore` and store its entire result there (R-24), to close that turn through the foundation's completion gate before it ends (an action or design decision and its own agent review, `Other` with a note being enough), because the foundation's Stop gate blocks a host from stopping while a delivered turn is still in progress (foundation section 3.4) and a reviewer run has no time limit (P-02), and to emit exactly one `hv_verdict` record last.\n545: \n546: Records (each a JSON object on its own line inside the reviewer's messages, read from each message's complete text as the reviewer's adapter assembles it from the native events, section 16.3; every other line is free text and stays in the log):\n547: \n548: - `{ \"type\": \"hv_progress\", \"percentComplete\": 0..100, \"etaSeconds\": n or null, \"note\": \"...\" }`.\n549: - `{ \"type\": \"hv_turn_assessment\", \"hvRequestId\", \"ordinal\", \"agent\", \"sessionId\", \"requestId\", \"snapshotSha256\", \"correctness\", \"completeness\", \"verdict\": \"AGREE\" or \"DISAGREE\", \"summary\", \"findings\": [{ \"outcome\": \"FAIL\" or \"UNKNOWN\", \"category\", \"location\", \"requirementRef\", \"claimId\", \"evidence\", \"remediation\" }] }`: one per member turn (S-03, S-21).\n550: - `{ \"type\": \"hv_holistic\", \"hvRequestId\", \"correctness\", \"completeness\", \"verdict\", \"summary\", \"crossTurnFindings\": [same shape] }`: exactly one (S-10); it states cross-turn consistency, omissions, contradictions, and end-to-end satisfaction and is never a calculation over the turn scores.\n551: - `{ \"type\": \"hv_response_grade\", \"hvRequestId\", \"responseId\", \"contentSha256\", \"correctness\", \"completeness\", \"verdict\", \"findings\": [{ \"claimId\", \"check\", \"outcome\": \"PASS\", \"FAIL\", or \"UNKNOWN\" }] }`: one per linked response with disposition `Pending` (foundation `verdict_match` rules: every claim named at least once).\n552: - `{ \"type\": \"hv_reviewer_turn\", \"agent\", \"sessionId\", \"requestId\" }`: the reviewer's own session-log turn (R-24).\n553: - `{ \"type\": \"hv_verdict\", \"hvRequestId\", \"runId\", \"overallVerdict\", \"turnCount\", \"responseGradeCount\", \"reviewer\": { \"reviewerId\", \"model\", \"effort\" } }`: exactly one, last.\n554: - `{ \"type\": \"hv_probe\", \"nonce\", \"model\", \"effort\" }`: the answer to a NONCE probe brief (R-10). A probe brief asks for this record and, as a review brief does, for the reviewer's own `Chore` turn and its `hv_reviewer_turn` record (R-24); policy ReadinessProbeVerdict reads both.\n555: \n556: The response log is the reviewer process's complete output as JSONL: the worker's `hv_brief` record first; then, when the adapter runs the CLI in a JSON streaming mode, each native event line as written, and otherwise each output line wrapped as `{ \"type\": \"hv_raw\", \"stream\": \"stdout\" or \"stderr\", \"line\": \"...\" }`; and, after the process exits, the adapter's provenance lines `{ \"type\": \"hv_provenance\", \"model\", \"effort\", \"source\", \"sourceSha256\" }`, which name the runtime receipt they were read from and its hash (P-04). The adapter extracts the reviewer's records from the agent message text of the native events (section 16.3). `hv_brief`, `hv_raw`, and `hv_provenance` are written only by the worker as top-level log lines and are never accepted from the reviewer's message text, so a reviewer cannot forge them.\n557: \n558: ### 13.4 Standard result document (S-13)\n559: \n560: `GET /requests/{hvRequestId}/result` returns `HvResultDocument`:\n561: \n562: `{ schema: \"qbrainai.hv.result/1\", hvRequestId, status, scope, submitter, reviewer: { reviewerId, expectedModel, expectedEffort, runtimeModel, runtimeEffort, runId, attempt, reviewerAgent, reviewerSessionId, reviewerRequestId }, request: <the complete accepted request of section 13.3>, responseLog: [<every JSONL record of the finalized run, in order, starting with its hv_brief record>], turnAssessments: [{ ordinal, agent, sessionId, requestId, correctness, completeness, verdict, mappedReviewStatus, summary, findings }], holistic: { correctness, completeness, verdict, summary, crossTurnFindings }, failures: [{ ordinal, scope, turnOrdinal, agent, sessionId, requestId, outcome, category, location, requirementRef, claimId, evidence, remediation }], responseGrades: [{ responseId, gradeId, verdict, correctness, completeness }], overallVerdict, thresholds: { correctness, completeness }, evidence: { request: { sha256, bytes, compressedBytes }, responseLog: { chainSha256, bytes, lines, chunks }, result: { sha256 } }, todoIds: [string], finalizedUtc }`.\n563: \n564: - `turnAssessments` lists every requested turn with its score (S-21); `failures` is the delineated list of every FAIL and UNKNOWN, each with its remediation (S-13); `request` and `responseLog` are complete (S-13); `todoIds` is information only (R-22).\n565: - With `Accept-Encoding: gzip` the document is sent compressed; the `responseLog` array is streamed from the chunks, so the server holds no uncompressed copy (R-14).\n566: - Before finalization the route answers 409 `hv_result_not_ready` with the request's status; after evidence removal it answers 410 `hv_evidence_removed` with the hashes and sizes it still holds.\n567: \n568: ### 13.5 Streams\n569: \n570: - Output stream: event `hv_output` with `id` `<runId>:<sequence>` and data `{ runId, sequence, lines: [string] }`, one event per stored chunk; event `hv_run_closed` with data `{ runId, status }` when the run ends; a new attempt starts a new run id in the same stream, so `Last-Event-ID` `<runId>:<sequence>` resumes after that chunk of that run. Per S-18 a caller attaches to \"any running hv\": the stream serves the request's runs in attempt order.\n571: - Notification stream: event `<kind>` with `id` `<sequence>` and data `HvNotificationDto`; `Last-Event-ID` `<sequence>` resumes after it. The stream is workspace-scoped (S-19: notifications of HV completion in the plugins).\n572: \n573: ### 13.6 Error codes\n574: \n575: New entries of the one `ErrorCodes` table (foundation section 3.5.2), each with its status and retryable flag:\n576: \n577: - `audit_unavailable` 503, retryable (AuditLedgerGuard).\n578: - `review_hostile_pipeline_only` 403 (A-06).\n579: - `turn_immutable` 409 with `details.reason` `hv_pending` or `hv_final` and `details.hvRequestId` (the code exists in the foundation's typed failures, C9; A-07 adds the reasons).\n580: - `hv_no_reviewer_available` 409 with `details.reviewers` (each reviewer's id, enabled flag, readiness, reason, and open incident) (S-16).\n581: - `hv_scope_invalid` 400 (`details.field`: an unknown kind, a missing or extra scope field, an unknown session, an endpoint turn not in the session, or a range whose start is after its end).\n582: - `hv_scope_too_large` 400 (`details.count`, `details.max`).\n583: - `hv_scope_includes_submitting_turn` 400.\n584: - `hv_scope_empty` 400 (a session scope with no turn left after the submitting turn's exclusion).\n585: - `hv_turns_not_terminal`, `hv_turns_pending`, `hv_turns_already_reviewed` 409, each with `details.turns` (and `details.hvRequestIds` for the second and third).\n586: - `hv_request_not_cancelable` 409 (`details.status`).\n587: - `hv_request_active` 409 (`details.status`: evidence removal of a request that is not `Completed`, `Failed`, or `Canceled`).\n588: - `hv_reviewer_disabled` 409 (a NONCE requested for a disabled reviewer).\n589: - `hv_result_not_ready` 409 (`details.status`).\n590: - `hv_evidence_not_available` 404 (a kind not produced yet) and `hv_evidence_removed` 410.\n591: - `conflict` 409: `retryable: false` for an idempotency key reused with other inputs or a reviewer update whose `expectedStateVersion` is stale (`details.field` `expectedStateVersion`), `retryable: true` when SerializableWrite or ReadableKeyAllocator is exhausted.\n592: - `not_found` 404 with `details.resource` `reviewer`, `hv_request`, or `run`.\n593: - `evidence_corrupt` 500: a GZIP round trip failed inside admission (SubmitHvRequestCommand) and nothing was saved; on runs it is also an internal failure code.\n594: - Internal codes, stored on runs and incidents and never returned by a public route: `stale_fence`, `evidence_corrupt`, `reviewer_launch_failed`, `reviewer_exited_nonzero`, `reviewer_output_invalid`, `reviewer_turn_unverified`, `reviewer_turn_logging_unsupported`, `runtime_identity_mismatch`, `verdict_binding_failed`, `reviewer_not_independent`, `snapshot_changed`, `probe_nonce_mismatch`, `lease_expired`, `attempts_exhausted`, `canceled`, `worker_shutdown`.\n595: \n596: ## 14. Units of work (CQRS handlers)\n597: \n598: Each unit is one command or query record and its handler, two files in the folders of section 4. WorkspaceResolutionBehavior runs after the dispatch and before every handler (foundation section 3.5.1); each unit lists its 400 `validation_error` with `details.field` `workspacePath` and does not draw it. Every command runs its checks and its save as one SerializableWrite delegate (foundation section 3.5.2) and calls AuditLedgerGuard first inside it (R-19), so each command lists 503 `audit_unavailable` and 409 `conflict` with `retryable: true` (attempts exhausted, nothing saved) and draws them once as the exits of its SerializableWrite call. Reviewer ids in routes and filters pass through AgentIdentity, so an alias addresses its reviewer.\n599: \n600: ### 14.1 Reviewer pool and readiness\n601: \n602: #### ListHvReviewersQuery: list the reviewer pool [FR-MCP-HVPIPE-001, -003]\n603: \n604: - Handler: `ListHvReviewersQuery(string WorkspacePath) : IQuery<IReadOnlyList<HvReviewerDto>>`.\n605: - Surfaces: section 13.1. Response 200: the five reviewers in pool order (Cline, Copilot, Claude, Codex, Grok), each with `activeRuns` (its runs in `Claimed` or `Running`).\n606: - Errors: 400 `validation_error` (`workspacePath`).\n607: \n608: ```mermaid\n609: flowchart TD\n610:     S([\"Handler runs: GET reviewers\"]) --> L[\"Load the workspace's HvReviewer rows in pool order\"]\n611:     L --> C[\"Count each reviewer's runs in Claimed or Running\"]\n612:     C --> R([\"200 the five HvReviewerDto\"])\n613: ```\n614: \n615: #### GetHvReviewerQuery: get one reviewer [FR-MCP-HVPIPE-001, -003]\n616: \n617: - Handler: `GetHvReviewerQuery(string WorkspacePath, string ReviewerId) : IQuery<HvReviewerDto>`.\n618: - Response 200 `HvReviewerDto`. Errors: 400 `validation_error` (`workspacePath`); 404 `not_found` (`details.resource` `reviewer`) for an id AgentIdentity does not map to a reviewer.\n619: \n620: ```mermaid\n621: flowchart TD\n622:     S([\"Handler runs: GET reviewers/{reviewerId}\"]) --> N[[\"AgentIdentity.Normalize\"]]\n623:     N -->|Unknown| E([\"404 not_found, details.resource reviewer\"])\n624:     N -->|reviewer id| L[\"Load the row and count its active runs\"]\n625:     L --> R([\"200 HvReviewerDto\"])\n626: ```\n627: \n628: #### UpdateHvReviewerCommand: manage a reviewer in real time [FR-MCP-HVPIPE-001]\n629: \n630: - Handler: `UpdateHvReviewerCommand(string WorkspacePath, string ReviewerId, UpdateHvReviewerRequest Request) : ICommand<HvReviewerDto>` (S-02).\n631: - Validation before the transaction: `expectedStateVersion` required; `executionStrategy`, when present, a supported strategy name; `maxConcurrentRuns` in 1..8; `model` at most 128 and `effort` at most 32 characters; any violation is 400 `validation_error` naming the field.\n632: - Delegate: AuditLedgerGuard; the reviewer row (404 when absent); `StateVersion` equal to `expectedStateVersion`, otherwise 409 `conflict` with `retryable: false` and `details.field` `expectedStateVersion`; apply the fields; when the strategy, agent path, model, or effort changed, set `Readiness` `Unverified` with reason `configuration_changed` and append `reviewer_unverified` (NotificationOutbox); increment `StateVersion`. After the commit the worker is woken, and it NONCEs an enabled `Unverified` reviewer (R-10).\n633: - A disabled reviewer stays assigned to the requests it holds until their next claim, which reassigns them (R-07); a run already running continues.\n634: - Response 200 `HvReviewerDto`. Errors: 400 `validation_error`; 404 `not_found` (`reviewer`); 409 `conflict` (`retryable: false` stale version, `retryable: true` exhausted); 503 `audit_unavailable`.\n635: \n636: ```mermaid\n637: flowchart TD\n638:     S([\"Handler runs: PATCH reviewers/{reviewerId}\"]) --> V{\"Fields valid and expectedStateVersion present?\"}\n639:     V -->|no| E1([\"400 validation_error, naming the field\"])\n640:     V -->|yes| N[[\"AgentIdentity.Normalize\"]]\n641:     N -->|Unknown| E2([\"404 not_found, details.resource reviewer\"])\n642:     N -->|reviewer id| SW[[\"SerializableWrite with AuditLedgerGuard\"]]\n643:     SW -->|\"audit unavailable\"| E3([\"503 audit_unavailable\"])\n644:     SW -->|\"attempts exhausted\"| E4([\"409 conflict, retryable true\"])\n645:     SW -->|attempt| VER{\"StateVersion equals expectedStateVersion?\"}\n646:     VER -->|no| E5([\"409 conflict, retryable false, details.field expectedStateVersion\"])\n647:     VER -->|yes| AP[\"Apply the fields\"]\n648:     AP --> CH{\"Strategy, agent path, model, or effort changed?\"}\n649:     CH -->|yes| UV[\"Readiness Unverified, reason configuration_changed\"]\n650:     UV --> NO[[\"NotificationOutbox: reviewer_unverified\"]]\n651:     NO --> INC[\"Increment StateVersion\"]\n652:     CH -->|no| INC\n653:     INC --> R([\"200 HvReviewerDto; the worker is woken after the commit\"])\n654: ```\n655: \n656: #### StartHvReviewerNonceCommand: request a NONCE probe [FR-MCP-HVPIPE-003]\n657: \n658: - Handler: `StartHvReviewerNonceCommand(string WorkspacePath, string ReviewerId) : ICommand<StartHvReviewerNonceResult>` (S-27, R-10). Any caller may request it (no roles, S-29).\n659: - Delegate: AuditLedgerGuard; the reviewer row (404); a disabled reviewer is 409 `hv_reviewer_disabled`; a probe run of this reviewer in `Claimed` or `Running` returns 202 `Running` with its run id and writes nothing; a `ProbeRequestedUtc` already set returns 202 `AlreadyRequested` and writes nothing; otherwise `ProbeRequestedUtc` is set and the result is 202 `Requested`. After the commit the worker is woken; ClaimHvRunCommand creates the probe run.\n660: - Errors: 400 `validation_error` (`workspacePath`); 404 `not_found` (`reviewer`); 409 `hv_reviewer_disabled`, `conflict` (`retryable: true`); 503 `audit_unavailable`.\n661: \n662: ```mermaid\n663: flowchart TD\n664:     S([\"Handler runs: POST reviewers/{reviewerId}/nonce\"]) --> N[[\"AgentIdentity.Normalize\"]]\n665:     N -->|Unknown| E1([\"404 not_found, details.resource reviewer\"])\n666:     N -->|reviewer id| SW[[\"SerializableWrite with AuditLedgerGuard\"]]\n667:     SW -->|\"audit unavailable\"| E2([\"503 audit_unavailable\"])\n668:     SW -->|\"attempts exhausted\"| E3([\"409 conflict, retryable true\"])\n669:     SW -->|attempt| EN{\"Reviewer enabled?\"}\n670:     EN -->|no| E4([\"409 hv_reviewer_disabled\"])\nEXIT_CODE=0\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
