ab24ad00b09053daf07ed3c0d850f70498d (P15 names a plan-created requirement as such, 2026-10-17T08:36 local), and commit 31904493381cfef56c57790950e23e72f3ecc39b (pre-HV holistic review fixes and FR-MCP-HVPIPE-008-AC011, the reviewer's whole process tree ended, 2026-10-17T08:51 local), commit 0a449314528c5bfc07e9b386c97034716e2ddbd4 (FR-MCP-HVPIPE-012-AC007, turns already HV-reviewed migrate Final, 2026-10-17T08:57 local), and commit d3a0beb10b0879f20fb307f205a3bff25ac3a441 (D-07 and D-08 settled by the operator, 2026-10-17T09:16 local). It amends the foundation docs/architecture/SessionTurn-Review-AgentContext-Architecture.md (PLAN-SESSIONTURNREVIEW-001).\"\n13:     - 'Settled requirements: S-01 to S-33, every operator statement of the HV planning conversation, verbatim in amendment section 3, with the standing HV rules P-01 to P-07: five reviewers Cline, Copilot, Claude, Codex, Grok with endpoints and REPL management (S-02); per-turn scores, an overall holistic review, results in the database (S-03, S-10, S-21); review final and no updates to a reviewed turn (S-06, S-07); Unnecessary turns included (S-09); session id means all turns (S-11); standard result payload with the complete request, complete JSONL log, and failures with remediation (S-13); context field and FR/TR/AC/UC references (S-14); failures triaged and reviewer offline until resolved (S-15); refuse with context when no reviewer (S-16); round-robin excluding the submitter (S-17) and, by D-05, the author of the reviewed turns; running, output, ETA, cancel, live SSE endpoints (S-18); completion notification stream (S-19); no force flag (S-20); output captured live and streamed, operator-confirmed gap P8 (S-22); single transaction at end (S-23); auto-start (S-24); verdict only, no TODO automation (S-25); incidents through the triage endpoint (S-26); NONCE means the agent is available and can execute an HV (S-27); self-review not relevant to HV (S-28); database audit, retain until told, no roles, audit failure a hard stop (S-29); GZIP logs (S-30); worktree from develop (S-31).'\n14:     - \"Design: amendment sections 4 to 19: HostileValidation bounded context; resolutions R-01 to R-31; 23 units of work, 8 new policies (HvRetryDecision decides and writes a request outcome for both a failed run and an expired lease; HvReviewerEligibility excludes the submitter and the author), 4 processes plus the reviewer adapter contract (one record-extraction function for the worker and finalization, a verified write barrier per CLI, provenance sources per CLI) and Director commands, 8 shared components (FencedLease, GzipCodec, AuditLedgerGuard, AgentIdentity, TurnSnapshotBuilder, RequirementReferenceExtractor, NotificationOutbox, OrderedEventReplay); 13 new entities, each evidence item stored once in the evidence tables while the append-only audit ledger keeps its own history of every write, never purged by an evidence removal (operator 2026-10-16: \\\"Purging stale data doesn't include removing it from the audit log. That's the opposite of an audit log.\\\"); 12 use cases UC-HV-01 to UC-HV-12; invariants I-01 to I-13; crash windows W-01 to W-12, each proved by a named acceptance criterion.\"\n15:     - 'Foundation amendments A-01 to A-12 (single grader removed, HV request superseded, model grades only from finalization, hostile reviews pipeline-only, frozen and final turns, HvFinalization origin, turn HvState columns): a change to the approved PLAN-SESSIONTURNREVIEW-001 that needs its own new hostile validation before either plan executes them (operator decision D-03).'\n16:     - 'Delivery (amendment section 20): the operator four-phase structure with the handoff dependency order. H0 = Phases 1 to 3 for the whole HV catalog: the requirement records FR, TR, TEST -MCP-HVPIPE-001..021 and their 21 mappings (created 2026-10-16 as pending, read back with 0 mismatches) updated to the approved text, and the use cases UC-HV-01..12 created, through the plugin workflows; interfaces, DTOs, entities, options, and stubs compiling and unregistered; every test of the 114 acceptance criteria written from the criteria and proven against mocks with negative controls before production code (BDPv4 green mock gate); implementation worktree cut from develop at Phase 2 start. Phase 4 contexts in merge order: HvStorageSchema, HvSharedComponents, H1 HvReviewerPool, H2 HvAdmission, H3 HvExecution, H7 HvFinalization, H4 HvRestSurfaces, then H5 HvClientParity and H6 HvStreamsAndOperations, then integration, live checks, independent validation, operator approval. Dependency: PLAN-SESSIONTURNREVIEW-001 delivers the foundation components the HV contexts call (SharedComponents, SessionTurnLogging, TurnReviews, ResponsesAndTrust, PluginCorePowerShell) or their Phase 2 seams.'\n17:     - \"Gates (amendment section 20.2): G1 to G6 through Nuke only, zero failures and zero skips, full current and prior unit suite before leaving a context; three-provider cases in G3; live check on a separate server instance (NONCE every reviewer, each reviewer's turn logging behind its write barrier, session-scope HV, output observed live, worker killed and recovered, cancel, finalize, result and evidence read, writes to reviewed turns refused), never on the live server; no GitHub Actions or Azure Pipelines; releases through Octopus.\"\n18:     - 'Discipline: each slice stops at Validating; the coordinator decides completion; every HV of this plan by the reviewer the operator names, never of the requester family (P-01), unbounded review time (P-02), 98/98 with no FAIL or UNKNOWN (P-05), request and response jsonl and the entire result in the session log; the new pipeline does not validate its own plan until its live check passed and the operator approves the switch.'\n19:     - \"Problems pulled in: REMED-HVPIPELINE-001 (the single problems TODO, operator 2026-10-16). P5 and P7 in H0; P6, P8, and P9 in H1 (P8 proven only by FR-MCP-HVPIPE-008-AC003, a line observable on the stream before the reviewer exits; P9 by the one table of highest efforts in the shared launch builder); P4 in HvSharedComponents (AuditLedgerGuard) and HvStorageSchema (IsDeleted on every HV entity); P1, P2, P3 in H3 (D-02 settled: the HostileReview subsystem stays separate; the worker FR-MCP-HOSTILEREVIEW-003 already specifies is built on HvWorkerHost and the reviewer adapters, and P2 and P3 are fixed in that subsystem). P10 to P15 (the Codex review of pull request 81, added 2026-10-17) sit in code other plans own or have redesigned (P10, P12, P13 the federation plan, P10 and P13 being its undelivered P1.5; P11, P15 the stop path the foundation's slice A7 rewrites; P14 FR-MCP-SESSIONLIFE-004); by D-07 (operator 2026-10-17: \\\"D-07 B: this plan fixes all six (P10 to P15) itself.\\\") this plan fixes them under the owners' approved designs: P10, P12, P13 in HvStorageSchema before any HV entity (P10 and P13 as the federation plan's P1.5: rekey maintenance command, startup guard, token-store rewrite, its D5 and D7; H0 imports FR, TR, TEST-MCP-PATHNORM-001 into this store), P11, P14, P15 in H1 in the PowerShell plugin core synced to every plugin, before FR-MCP-HVPIPE-008-AC010 is bound (P11 and P15 to the foundation's stop gate, FR-MCP-SESSIONTURN-005); a fix an owner already delivered is proven by the named test, not rewritten (DRY).\"\n20:     - 'Verification items (amendment section 20.5; probe receipts in /home/sharpninja/.claude/receipts/McpServer/20261016T153600-hv-amendment-vi-probes/, 78 files copied with SHA-256 checks): settled on 2026-10-16: VI-01 runtime model and effort per CLI (Codex rollout, Claude transcript, Grok session store, Copilot JSON stream record both; Cline records the model only, so it cannot pass a NONCE, D-06); VI-02 Copilot runs unattended with -p and JSON output and needs a configured model; VI-03 write barriers (Codex read-only and Grok plan exercised, Copilot --available-tools structural, Claude and Cline plan modes not accepted); VI-06 turn order is ascend