{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_56","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/pwsh -NoProfile -Command \"pwsh.exe -NoProfile -NonInteractive -File './docs/receipts/hv/hv-r1-inspect.ps1' -Task Read -Path './docs/architecture/SessionTurn-Review-AgentContext-Architecture-Amendment-1-Durable-HV.md' -Start 671 -Count 260\"","aggregated_output":"SOURCE ./docs/architecture/SessionTurn-Review-AgentContext-Architecture-Amendment-1-Durable-HV.md totalLines=2785\n671:     EN -->|yes| RUN{\"A probe run Claimed or Running?\"}\n672:     RUN -->|yes| R1([\"202 Running, with its run id; nothing written\"])\n673:     RUN -->|no| REQ{\"ProbeRequestedUtc already set?\"}\n674:     REQ -->|yes| R2([\"202 AlreadyRequested; nothing written\"])\n675:     REQ -->|no| SET[\"Set ProbeRequestedUtc\"]\n676:     SET --> R3([\"202 Requested; the worker is woken after the commit\"])\n677: ```\n678: \n679: ### 14.2 Admission, queries, and cancellation\n680: \n681: #### SubmitHvRequestCommand: admit an HV request [FR-MCP-HVPIPE-002, -004, -005, -006, -007, -011, -013, -018]\n682: \n683: - Handler: `SubmitHvRequestCommand(string WorkspacePath, SubmitHvRequestRequest Request) : ICommand<HvRequestResult>`.\n684: - Callers: any agent or operator; the plugin verb `workflow.hv.submit` binds the submitting turn automatically (process SubmitHvFromPlugin, section 16.4).\n685: - Order of checks:\n686:   1. Shape (no store read): the scope fields for its kind (400 `hv_scope_invalid` with `details.field`), the submitter fields for its kind (400 `validation_error` with `details.field` under `submitter`), a nonblank `idempotencyKey` of at most 128 characters, `contextFormat` known and `context` at most 65536 characters (400 `validation_error`).\n687:   2. Reads before the transaction (foundation section 3.1, \"Database-only delegates\"): RequirementReferenceExtractor over `context`.\n688:   3. SerializableWrite delegate: AuditLedgerGuard; IdempotentCreate on `IdempotencyKey` (policy `Conflict`, fingerprint of the client inputs): the same inputs return 200 with the stored request, other inputs 409 `conflict` with `retryable: false`; TurnLocator on the submitting turn for `submitter.kind` `Agent` (`InvalidIdentifier`, `SessionNotFound`, or `TurnNotFound` is 400 `validation_error` with `details.field` `submitter`); policy HvScopeResolution; policy HvAdmissionEligibility; policy RoundRobinAssignment; then the inserts.\n689:   4. Inserts in the delegate: the `hvr-` key (ReadableKeyAllocator); `HvRequest` `Queued` with `AssignedReviewerId` and `AuthorReviewerId`; one `HvRequestTurn` per member, each with its TurnSnapshotBuilder snapshot hash, class, and hostile status at admission (S-09); the requirement references; one `HvRequestResponse` `Pending` per agent response of a member turn whose status is `Submitted`, `Grading`, `Trusted`, or `Stale` and that is not `Pending` in another open request (when Phase C has recorded responses); the `Request` evidence through GzipCodec (section 13.3); policy HvTurnFreeze `Freeze` on every member turn (`HvState` `Pending`, `HvRequestId`); the round-robin cursor advance; NotificationOutbox `hv_queued`.\n690:   5. After the commit the worker is woken (S-24, auto-start).\n691: - Response 201 `HvRequestResult` with Location `/qbrainai/hostile-validation/requests/{hvRequestId}`; a repeat with the same key and inputs is 200 with the stored request and its current state.\n692: - Concurrency: two submissions over overlapping turns are serialized by SerializableWrite; the second sees the first's `Pending` items and is refused with `hv_turns_pending` (I-01; the unique filtered index ends a racing insert, and the retried attempt finds the winner). Two submissions over disjoint turns take consecutive cursor values, so round-robin order holds under concurrency.\n693: - Errors, in order: 400 `hv_scope_invalid`, `validation_error` (submitter, key, context, `workspacePath`), `hv_scope_too_large`, `hv_scope_includes_submitting_turn`, `hv_scope_empty`; 409 `conflict` (`retryable: false` key reused, `retryable: true` exhausted), `hv_turns_not_terminal`, `hv_turns_pending`, `hv_turns_already_reviewed`, `hv_no_reviewer_available` (with `details.reviewers`); 500 `evidence_corrupt` (the accepted request failed its GZIP round trip; nothing saved); 503 `audit_unavailable`.\n694: \n695: ```mermaid\n696: flowchart TD\n697:     S([\"Handler runs: POST requests\"]) --> SH{\"Scope, submitter, key, and context well formed?\"}\n698:     SH -->|\"scope\"| E1([\"400 hv_scope_invalid, details.field\"])\n699:     SH -->|\"submitter, key, or context\"| E2([\"400 validation_error, details.field\"])\n700:     SH -->|yes| RX[[\"RequirementReferenceExtractor on the context\"]]\n701:     RX --> SW[[\"SerializableWrite with AuditLedgerGuard\"]]\n702:     SW -->|\"audit unavailable\"| E3([\"503 audit_unavailable\"])\n703:     SW -->|\"attempts exhausted\"| E4([\"409 conflict, retryable true\"])\n704:     SW -->|attempt| IC[[\"IdempotentCreate lookup, policy Conflict\"]]\n705:     IC -->|\"stored, same inputs\"| R2([\"200 the stored request\"])\n706:     IC -->|\"key reused, other inputs\"| E5([\"409 conflict, retryable false\"])\n707:     IC -->|absent| AC[[\"AdmitRequestChecks\"]]\n708:     AC -->|refused| E6([\"Refusal of AdmitRequestChecks, drawn there\"])\n709:     AC -->|\"members and reviewer\"| INS[[\"InsertAdmittedRequest\"]]\n710:     INS -->|\"key collision: attempt ends\"| SW\n711:     INS -->|committed| R([\"201 HvRequestResult; the worker is woken after the commit\"])\n712: ```\n713: \n714: ##### Nested activity: AdmitRequestChecks (the checks of SubmitHvRequestCommand, inside its delegate)\n715: \n716: ```mermaid\n717: flowchart TD\n718:     S([\"AdmitRequestChecks\"]) --> SK{\"Submitter kind Agent?\"}\n719:     SK -->|yes| TL[[\"TurnLocator: the submitting turn\"]]\n720:     TL -->|\"InvalidIdentifier, SessionNotFound, or TurnNotFound\"| E1([\"400 validation_error, details.field submitter\"])\n721:     TL -->|found| SC\n722:     SK -->|\"no: Operator\"| SC[[\"Policy HvScopeResolution\"]]\n723:     SC -->|refused| E2([\"400 hv_scope_invalid, hv_scope_too_large, hv_scope_includes_submitting_turn, or hv_scope_empty\"])\n724:     SC -->|members| EL[[\"Policy HvAdmissionEligibility\"]]\n725:     EL -->|refused| E3([\"409 hv_turns_not_terminal, hv_turns_pending, or hv_turns_already_reviewed, listing every turn\"])\n726:     EL -->|eligible| RR[[\"Policy RoundRobinAssignment\"]]\n727:     RR -->|\"no eligible reviewer\"| E4([\"409 hv_no_reviewer_available, details.reviewers\"])\n728:     RR -->|\"reviewer, cursor advanced\"| OK([\"members and reviewer\"])\n729: ```\n730: \n731: ##### Nested activity: InsertAdmittedRequest (the inserts of SubmitHvRequestCommand, inside its delegate)\n732: \n733: ```mermaid\n734: flowchart TD\n735:     S([\"InsertAdmittedRequest: members, reviewer, references\"]) --> K[[\"ReadableKeyAllocator: hvr- key\"]]\n736:     K -->|collision| C([\"attempt ends: SerializableWrite runs the delegate again\"])\n737:     K -->|key| RQ[\"Insert HvRequest Queued with the assigned reviewer, the submitter, and the author id\"]\n738:     RQ --> TS[[\"TurnSnapshotBuilder for each member turn\"]]\n739:     TS --> IT[\"Insert one HvRequestTurn per member: ordinal, turn key, snapshot hash, class and hostile status at admission, Pending\"]\n740:     IT --> RF[\"Insert the requirement references\"]\n741:     RF --> RS[\"Insert HvRequestResponse Pending for each gradable response of a member turn\"]\n742:     RS --> EV[[\"GzipCodec Compress: the accepted request\"]]\n743:     EV -->|evidence_corrupt| E1([\"attempt fails: 500 evidence_corrupt, nothing saved\"])\n744:     EV -->|compressed| IE[\"Insert HvEvidence Request with its SHA-256 and sizes\"]\n745:     IE --> FZ[[\"Policy HvTurnFreeze Freeze: each member turn Pending with this request\"]]\n746:     FZ --> NO[[\"NotificationOutbox: hv_queued\"]]\n747:     NO --> OK([\"inserted\"])\n748: ```\n749: \n750: #### GetHvRequestQuery: get an HV request with its progress [FR-MCP-HVPIPE-015, -016]\n751: \n752: - Handler: `GetHvRequestQuery(string WorkspacePath, string HvRequestId) : IQuery<HvRequestResult>`.\n753: - Loads the request, its turns, references, responses, and current run with its progress (R-18) and its last 20 output lines (decompressed from the last chunks through GzipCodec). Because the last output is evidence, the unit records the access through AuditLedgerGuard `RecordRead` when it returns any output line (R-19).\n754: - Response 200 `HvRequestResult`. Errors: 400 `validation_error` (`workspacePath`); 404 `not_found` (`hv_request`); 503 `audit_unavailable` (output lines present and the ledger unwritable).\n755: \n756: ```mermaid\n757: flowchart TD\n758:     S([\"Handler runs: GET requests/{hvRequestId}\"]) --> F{\"Request in the workspace?\"}\n759:     F -->|no| E1([\"404 not_found, details.resource hv_request\"])\n760:     F -->|yes| L[\"Load turns, references, responses, and the current run with its progress\"]\n761:     L --> O{\"Current run has output?\"}\n762:     O -->|no| R1([\"200 HvRequestResult, lastOutput empty, etaStatus as recorded\"])\n763:     O -->|yes| G[[\"GzipCodec Decompress the last chunks to 20 lines\"]]\n764:     G --> A[[\"AuditLedgerGuard RecordRead\"]]\n765:     A -->|\"audit unavailable\"| E2([\"503 audit_unavailable\"])\n766:     A -->|recorded| R2([\"200 HvRequestResult with lastOutput\"])\n767: ```\n768: \n769: #### QueryHvRequestsQuery: list HV requests, running ones included [FR-MCP-HVPIPE-015]\n770: \n771: - Handler: `QueryHvRequestsQuery(string WorkspacePath, HvRequestQuery Query) : IQuery<PageResult<HvRequestResult>>`.\n772: - PagedQuery with `PageBounds` `Refuse` (limit 1..1000, default 50); filters combine with AND; order `CreatedUtc` descending, then `HvRequestId`. Summaries carry no output lines, so no read is recorded.\n773: - Errors: 400 `validation_error` (`workspacePath`, `limit`, `offset`, an unknown `status`, an unknown `reviewerId`).\n774: \n775: ```mermaid\n776: flowchart TD\n777:     S([\"Handler runs: GET requests\"]) --> V{\"Status and reviewer filters known?\"}\n778:     V -->|no| E1([\"400 validation_error, details.field status or reviewerId\"])\n779:     V -->|yes| PQ[[\"PagedQuery, PageBounds Refuse: AND filters, CreatedUtc descending then HvRequestId\"]]\n780:     PQ -->|\"limit or offset out of bounds\"| E2([\"400 validation_error, details.field limit or offset\"])\n781:     PQ -->|page| R([\"200 PageResult of HV request summaries\"])\n782: ```\n783: \n784: #### CancelHvRequestCommand: cancel any HV [FR-MCP-HVPIPE-008]\n785: \n786: - Handler: `CancelHvRequestCommand(string WorkspacePath, string HvRequestId) : ICommand<CancelHvRequestResult>` (S-18, R-28). Any caller (no roles).\n787: - Delegate: AuditLedgerGuard; the request (404); by status: `Queued` becomes `Canceled` with `CompletedUtc`, policy HvTurnFreeze `Release` returns its turns to `None`, its `Pending` responses become `Closed` (`request_ended`), and `hv_canceled` is appended; `Running` becomes `CancelRequested` with `CancelRequestedUtc` and `hv_cancel_requested` is appended (the worker stops the process at its next heartbeat, section 16.2); `CancelRequested` and `Canceled` return 200 unchanged; `Finalizing`, `Completed`, and `Failed` are 409 `hv_request_not_cancelable`.\n788: - Response 200 `CancelHvRequestResult`. Errors: 400 `validation_error` (`workspacePath`); 404 `not_found` (`hv_request`); 409 `hv_request_not_cancelable`, `conflict` (`retryable: true`); 503 `audit_unavailable`.\n789: \n790: ```mermaid\n791: flowchart TD\n792:     S([\"Handler runs: POST requests/{hvRequestId}/cancel\"]) --> SW[[\"SerializableWrite with AuditLedgerGuard\"]]\n793:     SW -->|\"audit unavailable\"| E1([\"503 audit_unavailable\"])\n794:     SW -->|\"attempts exhausted\"| E2([\"409 conflict, retryable true\"])\n795:     SW -->|attempt| F{\"Request in the workspace?\"}\n796:     F -->|no| E3([\"404 not_found, details.resource hv_request\"])\n797:     F -->|yes| ST{\"Status?\"}\n798:     ST -->|Queued| CQ[\"Canceled with CompletedUtc; Pending responses Closed request_ended\"]\n799:     CQ --> RL[[\"Policy HvTurnFreeze Release\"]]\n800:     RL --> N1[[\"NotificationOutbox: hv_canceled\"]]\n801:     N1 --> R1([\"200 Canceled\"])\n802:     ST -->|Running| CR[\"CancelRequested with CancelRequestedUtc\"]\n803:     CR --> N2[[\"NotificationOutbox: hv_cancel_requested\"]]\n804:     N2 --> R2([\"200 CancelRequested\"])\n805:     ST -->|\"CancelRequested or Canceled\"| R3([\"200 unchanged\"])\n806:     ST -->|\"Finalizing, Completed, or Failed\"| E4([\"409 hv_request_not_cancelable, details.status\"])\n807: ```\n808: \n809: ### 14.3 Results, evidence, streams, and incidents\n810: \n811: #### GetHvResultQuery: the standard result document [FR-MCP-HVPIPE-010, -015]\n812: \n813: - Handler: `GetHvResultQuery(string WorkspacePath, string HvRequestId) : IQuery<HvResultDocument>` (S-13, section 13.4).\n814: - Order: the request (404); `Completed` required, otherwise 409 `hv_result_not_ready` with the status; evidence removed is 410 `hv_evidence_removed` with the hashes and sizes it keeps; AuditLedgerGuard `RecordRead`; then the document is assembled from the `Result` evidence and the `Request` evidence (GzipCodec) and the finalized run's chunks, streamed in order.\n815: - Errors: 400 `validation_error` (`workspacePath`); 404 `not_found` (`hv_request`); 409 `hv_result_not_ready`; 410 `hv_evidence_removed`; 503 `audit_unavailable`.\n816: \n817: ```mermaid\n818: flowchart TD\n819:     S([\"Handler runs: GET requests/{hvRequestId}/result\"]) --> F{\"Request in the workspace?\"}\n820:     F -->|no| E1([\"404 not_found, details.resource hv_request\"])\n821:     F -->|yes| C{\"Status Completed?\"}\n822:     C -->|no| E2([\"409 hv_result_not_ready, details.status\"])\n823:     C -->|yes| RM{\"Evidence removed?\"}\n824:     RM -->|yes| E3([\"410 hv_evidence_removed, hashes and sizes kept\"])\n825:     RM -->|no| A[[\"AuditLedgerGuard RecordRead\"]]\n826:     A -->|\"audit unavailable\"| E4([\"503 audit_unavailable\"])\n827:     A -->|recorded| D[[\"GzipCodec Decompress: Result and Request evidence\"]]\n828:     D --> LG[\"Stream the finalized run's chunks in order as responseLog\"]\n829:     LG --> R([\"200 HvResultDocument, gzip when the caller accepts it\"])\n830: ```\n831: \n832: #### GetHvEvidenceQuery: download evidence [FR-MCP-HVPIPE-011, -015]\n833: \n834: - Handler: `GetHvEvidenceQuery(string WorkspacePath, string HvRequestId, string Kind, string? RunId, bool Decompressed) : IQuery<HvEvidenceStream>`.\n835: - `Kind` `request` (from admission), `response-log` (the finalized run, or `runId` for any run of the request, including a running one, so a caller can fetch output before finalization), or `result` (only when `Completed`). The default answer is `application/gzip`: the stored GZIP member for `request` and `result`, and for `response-log` the run's chunks served as consecutive GZIP members, which is a valid GZIP stream (RFC 1952, section 2.2); with `Decompressed` the bytes are decompressed on the way (`application/x-ndjson` or `application/json`). Nothing uncompressed is stored (R-14). AuditLedgerGuard `RecordRead` runs before the first byte.\n836: - Errors: 400 `validation_error` (`workspacePath`, an unknown `kind`); 404 `not_found` (`hv_request`; `run` for a `runId` that does not exist or belongs to another request), `hv_evidence_not_available` (a kind not produced yet); 410 `hv_evidence_removed`; 503 `audit_unavailable`.\n837: \n838: ```mermaid\n839: flowchart TD\n840:     S([\"Handler runs: GET requests/{hvRequestId}/evidence/{kind}\"]) --> K{\"Kind request, response-log, or result?\"}\n841:     K -->|no| E1([\"400 validation_error, details.field kind\"])\n842:     K -->|yes| F{\"Request in the workspace, and runId of this request when given?\"}\n843:     F -->|\"request missing\"| E2([\"404 not_found, details.resource hv_request\"])\n844:     F -->|\"runId missing or of another request\"| E3([\"404 not_found, details.resource run\"])\n845:     F -->|yes| P{\"Evidence produced?\"}\n846:     P -->|no| E4([\"404 hv_evidence_not_available\"])\n847:     P -->|\"removed\"| E5([\"410 hv_evidence_removed\"])\n848:     P -->|yes| A[[\"AuditLedgerGuard RecordRead\"]]\n849:     A -->|\"audit unavailable\"| E6([\"503 audit_unavailable\"])\n850:     A -->|recorded| M{\"Decompressed requested?\"}\n851:     M -->|no| G([\"200 application/gzip: the stored member, or the run's chunks as consecutive members\"])\n852:     M -->|yes| D[[\"GzipCodec Decompress, streamed\"]]\n853:     D --> R([\"200 the original bytes\"])\n854: ```\n855: \n856: #### RemoveHvEvidenceCommand: remove evidence on instruction [FR-MCP-HVPIPE-019]\n857: \n858: - Handler: `RemoveHvEvidenceCommand(string WorkspacePath, string HvRequestId, RemoveHvEvidenceRequest Request) : ICommand<RemoveHvEvidenceResult>` (S-29, R-20). Any caller (no roles); `reason` required (1..2048 characters) and recorded with the caller's `removedBy` name (required, 128).\n859: - Delegate: AuditLedgerGuard; the request (404); a request not `Completed`, `Failed`, or `Canceled` is 409 `hv_request_active`; every `HvEvidence` payload and every `HvRunOutputChunk` payload of the request's runs is set to null with `RemovedUtc`, `RemovedBy`, and `RemovalReason`; hashes, sizes, counts, result rows, findings, and turn reviews stay; each change writes its own ledger rows, and no earlier ledger row is changed or deleted (I-13). A repeat finds nothing left and returns 200 with empty `removedKinds`.\n860: - Errors: 400 `validation_error` (`workspacePath`, `reason`, `removedBy`); 404 `not_found` (`hv_request`); 409 `hv_request_active`, `conflict` (`retryable: true`); 503 `audit_unavailable`.\n861: \n862: ```mermaid\n863: flowchart TD\n864:     S([\"Handler runs: POST requests/{hvRequestId}/evidence/remove\"]) --> V{\"reason and removedBy present and within length?\"}\n865:     V -->|no| E1([\"400 validation_error, details.field\"])\n866:     V -->|yes| SW[[\"SerializableWrite with AuditLedgerGuard\"]]\n867:     SW -->|\"audit unavailable\"| E2([\"503 audit_unavailable\"])\n868:     SW -->|\"attempts exhausted\"| E3([\"409 conflict, retryable true\"])\n869:     SW -->|attempt| F{\"Request in the workspace?\"}\n870:     F -->|no| E4([\"404 not_found, details.resource hv_request\"])\n871:     F -->|yes| T{\"Completed, Failed, or Canceled?\"}\n872:     T -->|no| E5([\"409 hv_request_active, details.status\"])\n873:     T -->|yes| RM[\"Null every evidence and chunk payload still present; stamp RemovedUtc, RemovedBy, RemovalReason\"]\n874:     RM --> R([\"200 RemoveHvEvidenceResult: removed kinds and chunk count, empty on a repeat\"])\n875: ```\n876: \n877: #### StreamHvRunOutputQuery: attach to the live output of any HV [FR-MCP-HVPIPE-016]\n878: \n879: - Handler: `StreamHvRunOutputQuery(string WorkspacePath, string HvRequestId, string? LastEventId) : IQuery<IAsyncEnumerable<HvOutputEvent>>`, served by the controller as `text/event-stream` (S-18, S-22).\n880: - Order: the request (404); AuditLedgerGuard `RecordRead` once per connection; then OrderedEventReplay over the request's runs in attempt order and each run's chunks in sequence order (section 13.5), ending when the request is terminal and every chunk has been sent.\n881: - Errors (before the stream starts): 400 `validation_error` (`workspacePath`, `Last-Event-ID`); 404 `not_found` (`hv_request`); 503 `audit_unavailable`.\n882: \n883: ```mermaid\n884: flowchart TD\n885:     S([\"Handler runs: GET requests/{hvRequestId}/output/stream\"]) --> F{\"Request in the workspace?\"}\n886:     F -->|no| E1([\"404 not_found, details.resource hv_request\"])\n887:     F -->|yes| A[[\"AuditLedgerGuard RecordRead\"]]\n888:     A -->|\"audit unavailable\"| E2([\"503 audit_unavailable\"])\n889:     A -->|recorded| OR[[\"OrderedEventReplay: runs in attempt order, chunks in sequence\"]]\n890:     OR -->|\"malformed Last-Event-ID\"| E3([\"400 validation_error, details.field Last-Event-ID\"])\n891:     OR -->|\"request terminal, all sent\"| END([\"stream ended after hv_run_closed\"])\n892:     OR -->|\"caller disconnected\"| END2([\"stream closed\"])\n893: ```\n894: \n895: #### StreamHvNotificationsQuery: the HV notification stream [FR-MCP-HVPIPE-017]\n896: \n897: - Handler: `StreamHvNotificationsQuery(string WorkspacePath, string? LastEventId) : IQuery<IAsyncEnumerable<HvNotificationDto>>`, served as `text/event-stream` (S-19, R-16). Notifications carry ids and verdicts, not evidence, so no read row is recorded.\n898: - Errors (before the stream starts): 400 `validation_error` (`workspacePath`, `Last-Event-ID`).\n899: \n900: ```mermaid\n901: flowchart TD\n902:     S([\"Handler runs: GET notifications/stream\"]) --> OR[[\"OrderedEventReplay: HvNotification rows by sequence\"]]\n903:     OR -->|\"malformed Last-Event-ID\"| E([\"400 validation_error, details.field Last-Event-ID\"])\n904:     OR -->|\"caller disconnected\"| END([\"stream closed\"])\n905: ```\n906: \n907: #### QueryHvNotificationsQuery: poll notifications [FR-MCP-HVPIPE-017]\n908: \n909: - Handler: `QueryHvNotificationsQuery(string WorkspacePath, HvNotificationQuery Query) : IQuery<HvNotificationPage>`: rows with `Sequence` greater than `afterSequence` (at least 0), at most `limit` (1..1000, default 100), in sequence order, with the workspace's `lastSequence`.\n910: - Errors: 400 `validation_error` (`workspacePath`, `afterSequence`, `limit`).\n911: \n912: ```mermaid\n913: flowchart TD\n914:     S([\"Handler runs: GET notifications\"]) --> V{\"afterSequence at least 0, limit 1 to 1000?\"}\n915:     V -->|no| E([\"400 validation_error, details.field\"])\n916:     V -->|yes| Q[\"Read rows after afterSequence in sequence order, up to limit; read lastSequence\"]\n917:     Q --> R([\"200 items and lastSequence\"])\n918: ```\n919: \n920: #### QueryHvIncidentsQuery: list incidents [FR-MCP-HVPIPE-009]\n921: \n922: - Handler: `QueryHvIncidentsQuery(string WorkspacePath, HvIncidentQuery Query) : IQuery<PageResult<HvIncidentDto>>`: PagedQuery with `PageBounds` `Refuse`, filters `reviewerId` and `filingStatus` combined with AND, order `CreatedUtc` descending then `IncidentId`.\n923: - Errors: 400 `validation_error` (`workspacePath`, `limit`, `offset`, an unknown `reviewerId` or `filingStatus`).\n924: \n925: ```mermaid\n926: flowchart TD\n927:     S([\"Handler runs: GET incidents\"]) --> V{\"Filters known?\"}\n928:     V -->|no| E1([\"400 validation_error, details.field\"])\n929:     V -->|yes| PQ[[\"PagedQuery, PageBounds Refuse: AND filters, CreatedUtc descending then IncidentId\"]]\n930:     PQ -->|\"limit or offset out of bounds\"| E2([\"400 validation_error, details.field limit or offset\"])\nEXIT_CODE=0\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
