{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_58","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/pwsh -NoProfile -Command \"pwsh.exe -NoProfile -NonInteractive -File './docs/receipts/hv/hv-r1-inspect.ps1' -Task Read -Path './docs/receipts/hv/hv-r1-store-REMED-HVPIPELINE-001.txt' -Count 150\"","aggregated_output":"SOURCE ./docs/receipts/hv/hv-r1-store-REMED-HVPIPELINE-001.txt totalLines=76\n1: type: result\n2: payload:\n3:   requestId: req-20261017T142447Z-e768\n4:   result:\n5:     id: REMED-HVPIPELINE-001\n6:     title: Problems to fix found while preparing the durable multi-agent HV architecture amendment (pulled into the HV plan)\n7:     section: HostileValidation\n8:     priority: high\n9:     done: false\n10:     description:\n11:     - 'Single tracking item for every problem found while preparing the durable multi-agent hostile validation (HV) architecture amendment (operator, 2026-10-16T14:00 local, verbatim: \"keep track of problems to fix as a single todo item that will be pulled into the plan.\"). The HV plan PLAN-HVPIPELINE-001 pulls these items in (its last task; assignment in amendment section 20.4); nothing here is fixed by the documentation-only amendment, whose section 21 registers these problems (commits 31af8c597e3570a2469a48a238a4aa76107f30bb, 99cb42b24a442377a776aebd58e9df6894c2ce40, 9fd6b653b2522212ad8151091e3a8cdec25e75bd, 6dbc384323c036a57c37fd9eaf2259879c1d956f, bd6e37b33f043b1ede3a1feeaf7073d357ea21cf, f5fd5ab24ad00b09053daf07ed3c0d850f70498d, and d3a0beb10b0879f20fb307f205a3bff25ac3a441, branch docs/hv-architecture-amendment-20261016).'\n12:     - 'Source baseline: develop at 36783b79 (worktree hv-amendment-20261016, branch docs/hv-architecture-amendment-20261016). Each item states the observation with its receipt; an inference is marked as one.'\n13:     - 'P1 (requirement drift): FR-MCP-HOSTILEREVIEW-003 acceptance criterion 4 (server-owned worker, durable queue, bounded at-least-once execution, at most one accepted terminal result) is chec