nnot rely on the ledger as it behaves today.'\n17:     - 'P5 (reviewer pin drift): the foundation architecture docs/architecture/SessionTurn-Review-AgentContext-Architecture.md pins every HV and the model grader to Codex gpt-6-astra at effort max (section 3 Process at line 88, section 3.1 Trust and Model grade at lines 132 and 136, section 6.2 ModelGrader defaults at line 2691, UC-7 at line 5230), and HostileReviewWorkerOptions.Validate refuses any agent other than Astra, gpt-6-astra, xhigh (HostileReviewWorkerOptions.cs:77-82), contrary to the operator ruling of 2026-10-13 (\"HV must not be executed by the same agent family as the requesting agent.  If not specified by operator, ask what agent and model to use for HV in a session.\") and to the settled five-reviewer round-robin pool (Cline, Copilot, Claude, Codex, Grok). The amendment states the replacing rule; the foundation text, its plan, and the options change when the HV plan executes.'\n18:     - 'P6 (capability gap, corrected 2026-10-16T14:10 local): the one-shot strategy has no Copilot branch: OneShotCliAgentExecutionStrategy builds launches for codex, claude, grok, and cline only and throws NotSupportedException for any other agent (src/QBrainAi.Services/Services/OneShotCliAgentExecutionStrategy.cs:238-262). Copilot runs only through the interactive copilot-cli strategy (CopilotCliAgentExecutionStrategy.cs:5-45, registered at IAgentExecutionStrategy.cs:123, wrapping IAgentCliClient.CreateInteractiveSession). Whether that path gives a non-interactive HV run with live output and runtime model and effort provenance is unverified, while the settled reviewer pool includes Copilot. (The first version of this item said no Copilot adapter exists; that was wrong.)'\n19:     - 'P8 (capability gap, operator-confirmed): the operator requires reviewer output \"captured live and streamed\" (Cline session message 148), but the one-shot strategy streaming methods await the whole run and then yield its body once (OneShotCliAgentExecutionStrategy.cs:57-75), so no true live streaming exists on that path today. Operator, 2026-10-16T14:14 local, verbatim: \"Explains a lot.  Gotta be fixed in the plan.\" The HV plan must own the fix with a discriminating acceptance criterion: each output line a reviewer writes is persisted and observable on the run output stream while the reviewer process is still running (test: a scripted fake reviewer writes a line, then blocks on a gate the test controls; the line must arrive on the stream before the gate opens and before the process exits).'\n20:     - 'P7 (traceability drift): EventStreamController cites FR-MCP-045 for the SSE change stream (src/QBrainAi.Support.Mcp/Controllers/EventStreamController.cs:11), but the canonical FR-MCP-045 is \"Cross-Workspace TODO Move\" (requirement store read 2026-10-16T14:02:23 local); the HV reconnectable stream builds on that controller, so its requirement id must be corrected first.'\n21:     - \"P9 (defect and duplicated constants, source search 2026-10-16T15:33:38 local): develop's highest-effort constants disagree and one is refused. OneShotCliAgentExecutionStrategy passes Grok --effort max and --reasoning-effort max (src/QBrainAi.Services/Services/OneShotCliAgentExecutionStrategy.cs:26,332-335), which Grok 1.0.60 refuses with exit 1 (\\\"--effort/--reasoning-effort: unknown effort level 'max'; use one of: xhigh, high, medium, low\\\", probe run 2026-10-16T15:32:48 local, receipt cli-effort-probe/grok-max.stdout.txt in /home/sharpninja/.claude/receipts/McpServer/20261016T153600-hv-amendment-vi-probes/), so a one-shot Grok run fails before it starts (inference from the refused flag; the one-shot path itself was not run); GrokCliAgentExecutionStrategy uses high (src/QBrainAi.Services/Services/GrokCliAgentExecutionStrategy.cs:25,82-83); Codex is pinned to xhigh in two places (OneShotCliAgentExecutionStrategy.cs:23, CodexCliAgentExecutionStrategy.cs:21) although Codex accepted max and recorded effort max in its rol