d\\\" (handoff line 14); the handoff warns not to deploy develop to a server whose database still holds backslash workspace ids (line 16). Codex's suggested provider migration contradicts D5 (no automatic startup migration).\"\n24:     - \"P11 (stop-hook proof unusable; Codex priority 2, discussion_r4300020832): Get-PluginTurnPersistenceProof calls client.SessionLog.GetAsync through Invoke-PluginRepl (plugins/core/lib-ps/plugin-hook.ps1:1041-1065); SessionLogClient.GetAsync returns Task<UnifiedSessionLogDto> (src/QBrainAi.Client/SessionLogClient.cs:95), which is not a case of GenericClientPassthrough.AwaitTaskResultAsync (src/QBrainAi.Repl.Core/GenericClientPassthrough.cs:243-627), so it falls to the throw \\\"Unsupported task result type\\\" (:635-640), and the hook reads no proof and answers Active (plugin-hook.ps1:1063-1087). A supported call would still not carry the fields the hook reads at the top of the result, workspacePath, requestId, outcome, and serverStatus (plugin-hook.ps1:1089-1110): UnifiedSessionLogDto has sourceType, sessionId, status, workspace, and turns, with requestId only inside each turn (src/QBrainAi.Client/Models/SessionLogModels.cs:8-85,108-111). Inference (Codex's, not reproduced): a completed turn behind a stale cache keeps the stop gate blocked. Requirement: FR-MCP-SESSIONLIFE-004 (\\\"exact-turn proof through client.SessionLog.GetAsync\\\", plugin-hook.ps1:1044); the approved foundation plan PLAN-SESSIONTURNREVIEW-001 rewrites this stop path in its slice A7 (its change to TR-MCP-SESSIONLIFE-005: Close-PluginTurnIfNeeded blocks instead of closing, exact-turn proof for every open turn).\"\n25:     - 'P12 (root-relative Windows segment not rooted; Codex priority 2, discussion_r4300020839): WorkspacePathNormalizer.IsWindowsRooted accepts a drive-qualified path and the two UNC spellings only (src/QBrainAi.Client/WorkspacePathNormalizer.cs:161-164), so Combine (:120-144) treats a segment \\repo as relative and appends it: root C:/content with