rride returns before the turn is handled; Codex priority 2, discussion_r4300020859): Get-PluginStopEnforcementDecision returns allow after consuming turn-accept-failure.marker for a failed build or turn-accept-incomplete-audit.marker for an incomplete audit (plugins/core/lib-ps/plugin-hook.ps1:991-994,1009-1012); Close-PluginTurnIfNeeded then returns at :1172-1174, before the workflow.sessionlog.completeTurn branch at :1253, so the stop passes while the turn is still in progress in the cache and on the server. Codex suggests continuing through the completion; the approved foundation plan PLAN-SESSIONTURNREVIEW-001 instead makes the stop gate block a delivered request that is still in progress and never call completeTurn or failTurn (its FR-MCP-SESSIONTURN-005 acceptance criteria 1 and 4, which that plan creates and the store does not hold yet, requirement read 2026-10-17T08:36:10 local; its change to TR-MCP-SESSIONLIFE-005; slice A7). Requirements today: FR-MCP-SESSIONLIFE-004 and FR-MCP-SESSIONLIFE-005 (\"Stop hook stale pin and session-log uniqueness\").'\n29:     - \"D-07 settled by the operator on 2026-10-17 (verbatim: \\\"D-07 B: this plan fixes all six (P10 to P15) itself.\\\"): the HV plan fixes P10 to P15, each under the owning plan's approved design and through its existing requirement, whose acceptance criteria H0 strengthens with a named test (amendment section 20.4). P10, P12, and P13 in HvStorageSchema before any HV entity is created: P10 and P13 as the federation plan's P1.5 decided them (the rekey maintenance command, its startup guard, and the token-store key rewrite; its D5 and D7; never an automatic startup migration or a dual-key lookup), P12 in the normalizer; H0 first imports FR, TR, and TEST-MCP-PATHNORM-001 into this workspace's store. P11, P14, and P15 in H1, in the PowerShell plugin core synced to every plugin that carries it, before FR-MCP-HVPIPE-008-AC010 is bound to the real hosts; P11 and P15 to the foundation's stop gate (FR-MCP-SESSION