{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_59","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/pwsh -NoProfile -Command \"pwsh.exe -NoProfile -NonInteractive -File './docs/receipts/hv/hv-r1-inspect.ps1' -Task Read -Path './docs/architecture/SessionTurn-Review-AgentContext-Architecture-Amendment-1-Durable-HV.md' -Start 931 -Count 260\"","aggregated_output":"SOURCE ./docs/architecture/SessionTurn-Review-AgentContext-Architecture-Amendment-1-Durable-HV.md totalLines=2785\n931:     PQ -->|page| R([\"200 PageResult of HvIncidentDto\"])\n932: ```\n933: \n934: ### 14.4 Execution (internal units, dispatched only by the worker host)\n935: \n936: Every unit here is internal (R-29): its caller is process HvWorkerHost (section 16.1) or another unit of this section, never a route, tool, or client. Each returns a typed result to its caller; the codes in its list are those results, and none reaches a public surface.\n937: \n938: #### ClaimHvRunCommand: claim the next probe or review [FR-MCP-HVPIPE-003, -007]\n939: \n940: - Handler: `ClaimHvRunCommand(string WorkspacePath, string WorkerId) : ICommand<HvRunClaim?>`; `HvRunClaim { runId, kind, reviewerId, attempt, fenceToken, leaseExpiresUtc, hvRequestId, expectedModel, expectedEffort, probeNonce }`.\n941: - Delegate: AuditLedgerGuard; then, in this order: (1) a probe: the first enabled reviewer, in pool order, with `ProbeRequestedUtc` set and fewer active runs than its `MaxConcurrentRuns`: insert its `Probe` run (`hvprobe-` key, a fresh 32-byte random `ProbeNonce` in lower-case hex), FencedLease `Claim`, clear `ProbeRequestedUtc`; (2) otherwise a review: the oldest `Queued` request (by `CreatedUtc`, then `HvRequestId`) whose assignee is eligible with capacity, or whose assignee is no longer eligible and for which policy RoundRobinAssignment finds an eligible reviewer with capacity (the reassignment is recorded on the request); insert its `Review` run (`hvrun-<hvRequestId>-<nn>`, `Attempt` = `AttemptCount` + 1), FencedLease `Claim`, set the request `Running` (with `StartedUtc` on the first attempt) and `AttemptCount` + 1, and append `hv_started`. With nothing claimable it returns null and writes nothing; a request whose turns are all frozen stays `Queued` while no reviewer is eligible (ETA `Unknown`, R-18).\n942: - Concurrency: the request's state, version, and the one-live-run index are checked and written in the delegate, so two workers never claim one request (W-11).\n943: - Results: a claim; null; 409 `conflict` (`retryable: true`, the worker tries again at its next poll); 503 `audit_unavailable`.\n944: \n945: ```mermaid\n946: flowchart TD\n947:     S([\"ClaimHvRunCommand: workerId\"]) --> SW[[\"SerializableWrite with AuditLedgerGuard\"]]\n948:     SW -->|\"audit unavailable\"| E1([\"503 audit_unavailable\"])\n949:     SW -->|\"attempts exhausted\"| E2([\"409 conflict, retryable true\"])\n950:     SW -->|attempt| P{\"An enabled reviewer with a requested probe and free capacity?\"}\n951:     P -->|yes| PR[\"Insert the Probe run with a fresh nonce; clear ProbeRequestedUtc\"]\n952:     PR --> L1[[\"FencedLease Claim\"]]\n953:     L1 --> R1([\"probe claim\"])\n954:     P -->|no| Q{\"Oldest Queued request whose assignee is eligible with capacity?\"}\n955:     Q -->|yes| RV\n956:     Q -->|\"no, assignee no longer eligible\"| RR[[\"Policy RoundRobinAssignment\"]]\n957:     RR -->|\"no eligible reviewer with capacity\"| NX{\"Another Queued request?\"}\n958:     NX -->|yes| Q\n959:     NX -->|no| R0([\"null: nothing claimable\"])\n960:     RR -->|\"reviewer, reassignment recorded\"| RV[\"Insert the Review run, attempt AttemptCount plus 1\"]\n961:     Q -->|\"no Queued request\"| R0\n962:     RV --> L2[[\"FencedLease Claim\"]]\n963:     L2 --> RS[\"Request Running, AttemptCount plus 1, StartedUtc on the first attempt\"]\n964:     RS --> N[[\"NotificationOutbox: hv_started\"]]\n965:     N --> R2([\"review claim\"])\n966: ```\n967: \n968: #### RecordHvRunHeartbeatCommand: renew the lease and read cancellation [FR-MCP-HVPIPE-007, -008]\n969: \n970: - Handler: `RecordHvRunHeartbeatCommand(string WorkspacePath, string RunId, string WorkerId, long FenceToken) : ICommand<HvHeartbeatResult>`; `HvHeartbeatResult { leaseExpiresUtc, cancelRequested }`.\n971: - Delegate: AuditLedgerGuard; FencedLease `Renew`; `LastHeartbeatUtc`; `cancelRequested` is true when the request is `CancelRequested` (a probe run is never canceled this way).\n972: - Results: renewed; `stale_fence` (the worker stops its process, section 16.2); 409 `conflict` (`retryable: true`); 503 `audit_unavailable`.\n973: \n974: ```mermaid\n975: flowchart TD\n976:     S([\"RecordHvRunHeartbeatCommand: run, worker, fence\"]) --> SW[[\"SerializableWrite with AuditLedgerGuard\"]]\n977:     SW -->|\"audit unavailable\"| E1([\"503 audit_unavailable\"])\n978:     SW -->|\"attempts exhausted\"| E2([\"409 conflict, retryable true\"])\n979:     SW -->|attempt| L[[\"FencedLease Renew\"]]\n980:     L -->|stale_fence| E3([\"stale_fence: nothing changed\"])\n981:     L -->|renewed| H[\"Set LastHeartbeatUtc; read whether the request is CancelRequested\"]\n982:     H --> R([\"renewed: leaseExpiresUtc, cancelRequested\"])\n983: ```\n984: \n985: #### AppendHvRunOutputCommand: persist live output [FR-MCP-HVPIPE-008, -011, -016]\n986: \n987: - Handler: `AppendHvRunOutputCommand(string WorkspacePath, string RunId, string WorkerId, long FenceToken, int Sequence, IReadOnlyList<string> Lines, IReadOnlyList<string> CompletedRecords) : ICommand<HvAppendResult>` (S-22, R-12); `CompletedRecords` are the reviewer records whose messages the adapter's extraction completed with this batch (section 16.3), often none.\n988: - Validation: `Sequence` at least 1; at least one line; every line one UTF-8 JSON object (the adapter has already wrapped raw lines, section 13.3); every completed record one JSON object of a reviewer record type.\n989: - Delegate: AuditLedgerGuard; FencedLease `Guard`; a chunk with this `Sequence` already stored whose SHA-256 equals the batch's returns it unchanged (a retried append), and one with another SHA-256 is 409 `conflict` with `retryable: false`; a `Sequence` other than `OutputChunkCount` + 1 is 409 `conflict` with `details.field` `sequence`; GzipCodec `Compress`; insert the chunk with its SHA-256 and chain hash; update the run's manifest (`OutputChunkCount`, `OutputLineCount`, `OutputBytes`, `OutputChainSha256`) and `LastOutputUtc`; the last `hv_progress` among the batch's completed records sets the run's progress (R-18) and an `hv_reviewer_turn` among them its reviewer turn ids. After the commit the output streams are woken.\n990: - Results: appended (`sequence`, `chainSha256`); unchanged; `stale_fence`; 409 `conflict`; 500 `evidence_corrupt` (the round trip failed; nothing saved); 503 `audit_unavailable`.\n991: \n992: ```mermaid\n993: flowchart TD\n994:     S([\"AppendHvRunOutputCommand: run, fence, sequence, lines\"]) --> V{\"Sequence at least 1 and every line one JSON object?\"}\n995:     V -->|no| E1([\"400 validation_error\"])\n996:     V -->|yes| SW[[\"SerializableWrite with AuditLedgerGuard\"]]\n997:     SW -->|\"audit unavailable\"| E2([\"503 audit_unavailable\"])\n998:     SW -->|\"attempts exhausted\"| E3([\"409 conflict, retryable true\"])\n999:     SW -->|attempt| G[[\"FencedLease Guard\"]]\n1000:     G -->|stale_fence| E4([\"stale_fence: nothing changed\"])\n1001:     G -->|guarded| D{\"A chunk with this sequence stored?\"}\n1002:     D -->|\"yes, same SHA-256\"| R1([\"unchanged: the stored chunk\"])\n1003:     D -->|\"yes, other SHA-256\"| E5([\"409 conflict, retryable false\"])\n1004:     D -->|no| Q{\"Sequence is OutputChunkCount plus 1?\"}\n1005:     Q -->|no| E6([\"409 conflict, details.field sequence\"])\n1006:     Q -->|yes| C[[\"GzipCodec Compress\"]]\n1007:     C -->|evidence_corrupt| E7([\"500 evidence_corrupt: nothing saved\"])\n1008:     C -->|compressed| I[\"Insert the chunk: SHA-256, chain hash, fence; update the run manifest and LastOutputUtc\"]\n1009:     I --> PG[\"Set progress from the last completed hv_progress record and reviewer turn ids from hv_reviewer_turn\"]\n1010:     PG --> R2([\"appended: sequence, chainSha256; streams woken after the commit\"])\n1011: ```\n1012: \n1013: #### CloseHvRunOutputCommand: close a run's output [FR-MCP-HVPIPE-003, -008, -011]\n1014: \n1015: - Handler: `CloseHvRunOutputCommand(string WorkspacePath, string RunId, string WorkerId, long FenceToken, int ChunkCount, HvProvenance Provenance) : ICommand<HvCloseResult>`; the worker calls it only after the reviewer process exited with code 0 and every batch was appended; any other exit goes to FailHvRunCommand. Exit code 0 only routes the run here; whether it produced a review or a probe answer is decided by V-8 or policy ReadinessProbeVerdict (R-11).\n1016: - Delegate: AuditLedgerGuard; FencedLease `Guard`; `ChunkCount` equal to `OutputChunkCount`, otherwise 409 `conflict` with `details.field` `chunkCount` (the worker appends what is missing and closes again); the run becomes `OutputClosed` with `EndedUtc`, `ExitCode` 0, `RuntimeModel`, and `RuntimeEffort`; FencedLease `Release`. A `Review` run: the request becomes `Finalizing` and `hv_finalizing` is appended; after the commit the worker dispatches FinalizeHvRequestCommand. A `Probe` run: policy ReadinessProbeVerdict decides in the same transaction: a pass makes the run `Succeeded` and the reviewer `Online` with `ResolvedModel` and `ResolvedEffort` and appends `reviewer_online`; a failure makes the run `Failed` with the policy's code and the reviewer `Offline`, inserts an `HvIncident` (`Pending`, `DedupeKey` `hv-reviewer-<reviewerId>-<code>`), and appends `reviewer_offline`.\n1017: - Results: closed (`Finalizing`, probe passed, or probe failed); `stale_fence`; 409 `conflict`; 503 `audit_unavailable`.\n1018: \n1019: ```mermaid\n1020: flowchart TD\n1021:     S([\"CloseHvRunOutputCommand: run, fence, chunk count, provenance\"]) --> SW[[\"SerializableWrite with AuditLedgerGuard\"]]\n1022:     SW -->|\"audit unavailable\"| E1([\"503 audit_unavailable\"])\n1023:     SW -->|\"attempts exhausted\"| E2([\"409 conflict, retryable true\"])\n1024:     SW -->|attempt| G[[\"FencedLease Guard\"]]\n1025:     G -->|stale_fence| E3([\"stale_fence: nothing changed\"])\n1026:     G -->|guarded| C{\"ChunkCount equals OutputChunkCount?\"}\n1027:     C -->|no| E4([\"409 conflict, details.field chunkCount\"])\n1028:     C -->|yes| OC[\"Run OutputClosed: EndedUtc, exit 0, runtime model and effort\"]\n1029:     OC --> RL[[\"FencedLease Release\"]]\n1030:     RL --> K{\"Run kind?\"}\n1031:     K -->|Review| FZ[\"Request Finalizing\"]\n1032:     FZ --> N1[[\"NotificationOutbox: hv_finalizing\"]]\n1033:     N1 --> R1([\"closed: Finalizing; the worker dispatches FinalizeHvRequestCommand\"])\n1034:     K -->|Probe| PV[[\"Policy ReadinessProbeVerdict\"]]\n1035:     PV -->|passed| ON[\"Run Succeeded; reviewer Online with resolved model and effort\"]\n1036:     ON --> N2[[\"NotificationOutbox: reviewer_online\"]]\n1037:     N2 --> R2([\"closed: probe passed\"])\n1038:     PV -->|\"failed: code\"| OFF[\"Run Failed with the code; reviewer Offline; insert HvIncident Pending\"]\n1039:     OFF --> N3[[\"NotificationOutbox: reviewer_offline\"]]\n1040:     N3 --> R3([\"closed: probe failed\"])\n1041: ```\n1042: \n1043: #### FailHvRunCommand: record an execution failure [FR-MCP-HVPIPE-009]\n1044: \n1045: - Handler: `FailHvRunCommand(string WorkspacePath, string RunId, string? WorkerId, long FenceToken, string FailureCode, string Detail) : ICommand<HvFailResult>`. Callers: the worker (`WorkerId` set, a `Claimed` or `Running` run) and FinalizeHvRequestCommand (`WorkerId` null, an `OutputClosed` run with its released lease, whose stored fence the finalizer passes).\n1046: - Delegate: AuditLedgerGuard; FencedLease `Guard`; the run becomes `Failed` (or `Canceled` for the code `canceled`) with the code and the detail (through SecretRedactor) and `EndedUtc`, and its lease is released; `canceled` and `worker_shutdown` insert no incident and change no reviewer; every other failure inserts an `HvIncident` (`Pending`) with `DedupeKey` `hv-reviewer-<reviewerId>-<failureCode>` when the failure is attributable to the reviewer (`reviewer_launch_failed`, `reviewer_exited_nonzero`, `reviewer_output_invalid`, `reviewer_turn_unverified`, `runtime_identity_mismatch`, `verdict_binding_failed`), and `hv-server-<failureCode>` otherwise (`evidence_corrupt`, `snapshot_changed`, `reviewer_not_independent`); a reviewer-attributable failure also makes the reviewer `Offline` with `ReadinessReason` the code and `OpenIncidentId`, and appends `reviewer_offline` (S-15); then policy HvRetryDecision decides and writes the request's next state: `Queued` again (its assignee re-evaluated at the next claim), `Failed` with `attempts_exhausted`, or, for a `CancelRequested` request, `Canceled`, each ended request with its turns released, its `Pending` responses closed, and its notification (section 15). After the commit the worker is woken to file the incident (FileHvIncidentCommand) and claim again.\n1047: - Results: failed with the request's next state; `stale_fence`; 409 `conflict`; 503 `audit_unavailable`.\n1048: \n1049: ```mermaid\n1050: flowchart TD\n1051:     S([\"FailHvRunCommand: run, fence, failure code, detail\"]) --> SW[[\"SerializableWrite with AuditLedgerGuard\"]]\n1052:     SW -->|\"audit unavailable\"| E1([\"503 audit_unavailable\"])\n1053:     SW -->|\"attempts exhausted\"| E2([\"409 conflict, retryable true\"])\n1054:     SW -->|attempt| G[[\"FencedLease Guard\"]]\n1055:     G -->|stale_fence| E3([\"stale_fence: nothing changed\"])\n1056:     G -->|guarded| F[\"Run Failed, or Canceled for canceled: code, redacted detail, EndedUtc; lease released\"]\n1057:     F --> NI{\"Code canceled or worker_shutdown?\"}\n1058:     NI -->|yes| RD\n1059:     NI -->|no| AT{\"Failure attributable to the reviewer?\"}\n1060:     AT -->|yes| OFF[\"Insert HvIncident Pending, key hv-reviewer-id-code; reviewer Offline with the code and incident\"]\n1061:     OFF --> N1[[\"NotificationOutbox: reviewer_offline\"]]\n1062:     N1 --> RD\n1063:     AT -->|no| SI[\"Insert HvIncident Pending, key hv-server-code\"]\n1064:     SI --> RD[[\"Policy HvRetryDecision: decides and writes the request's next state\"]]\n1065:     RD -->|\"requeue\"| R1([\"failed: request Queued\"])\n1066:     RD -->|\"attempts exhausted\"| R2([\"failed: request Failed, turns released, hv_failed\"])\n1067:     RD -->|\"cancel requested\"| R3([\"failed: request Canceled, turns released, hv_canceled\"])\n1068: ```\n1069: \n1070: #### ExpireHvRunLeasesCommand: recover from dead workers [FR-MCP-HVPIPE-007]\n1071: \n1072: - Handler: `ExpireHvRunLeasesCommand(string WorkspacePath) : ICommand<HvSweepResult>`; `HvSweepResult { abandonedRunIds, finalizationPending }`.\n1073: - For each run in `Claimed` or `Running` whose `LeaseExpiresUtc` has passed, one SerializableWrite (so one stuck run never blocks the others): AuditLedgerGuard; the lease still expired as read (otherwise skipped: its worker renewed it); the run becomes `Abandoned` with `lease_expired`, and its `FenceToken` is incremented, so the old worker's next write is `stale_fence` (W-03); a server incident (`hv-server-lease_expired`) is inserted; for a `Review` run, policy HvRetryDecision decides and writes its request's next state (`Queued`; `Failed` on its last counted attempt; `Canceled` when a cancel was requested, which completes the cancel of a dead worker's run, R-28), the ended request with its turns released, its `Pending` responses closed, and `hv_failed` or `hv_canceled`, as after FailHvRunCommand (a `Probe` run's reviewer stays as it was and its probe is requested again). Then it lists the `Finalizing` requests (W-05) for the worker to finalize.\n1074: - Results: the sweep result; 503 `audit_unavailable` ends the sweep (W-12).\n1075: \n1076: ```mermaid\n1077: flowchart TD\n1078:     S([\"ExpireHvRunLeasesCommand\"]) --> L[\"List runs Claimed or Running with an expired lease\"]\n1079:     L --> MORE{\"Next expired run?\"}\n1080:     MORE -->|no| FP[\"List Finalizing requests\"]\n1081:     FP --> R([\"sweep result: abandoned runs, finalization pending\"])\n1082:     MORE -->|yes| SW[[\"SerializableWrite with AuditLedgerGuard, one per run\"]]\n1083:     SW -->|\"audit unavailable\"| E([\"503 audit_unavailable: sweep ends\"])\n1084:     SW -->|\"attempts exhausted\"| MORE\n1085:     SW -->|attempt| X{\"Lease still expired?\"}\n1086:     X -->|\"no: renewed\"| MORE\n1087:     X -->|yes| AB[\"Run Abandoned lease_expired; FenceToken incremented; insert server incident\"]\n1088:     AB --> K{\"Run kind?\"}\n1089:     K -->|Review| RD[[\"Policy HvRetryDecision: requeue, fail, or cancel the request, with release and notification\"]]\n1090:     RD --> MORE\n1091:     K -->|Probe| PQ[\"Request the probe again: ProbeRequestedUtc set\"]\n1092:     PQ --> MORE\n1093: ```\n1094: \n1095: #### FinalizeHvRequestCommand: verify and commit the result atomically [FR-MCP-HVPIPE-010, -011, -012, -013, -014, -021]\n1096: \n1097: - Handler: `FinalizeHvRequestCommand(string WorkspacePath, string HvRequestId) : ICommand<HvFinalizeResult>` (S-03, S-06, S-07, S-10, S-13, S-21, S-23, R-15). Callers: the worker after CloseHvRunOutputCommand, and the worker's sweep for every `Finalizing` request (W-05, W-06).\n1098: - Reads, with no transaction open (foundation section 3.1, \"Database-only delegates\"): the request (`Completed` returns the stored outcome and writes nothing, I-03; any status other than `Finalizing` returns `not_finalizable` and writes nothing); its `OutputClosed` run; every chunk decompressed and checked by policy HvFinalVerification V-1, then the reviewer's records, extracted from the stored log by the reviewer's adapter (`ExtractReviewerRecords`, the same function the worker ran, section 16.3), checked by V-2 to V-8 (section 15); when the request links responses and `Mcp:AgentContext:Mode` is not `Off`, EvaluateStalenessCommand is dispatched for them, as the foundation's grade units do before their write (foundation section 3.1).\n1099: - Verification failure: FailHvRunCommand is dispatched with the run's stored fence and the failing check's code, and the result is `verification_failed` with the request's next state (`Queued` or `Failed`); nothing of the result is written.\n1100: - Delegate (SerializableWrite, S-23): AuditLedgerGuard; re-check that the request is `Finalizing` at the version read, the run is `OutputClosed` with the fence and chunk manifest read, every member turn is `Pending` for this request, and each linked response's status is the one the reads saw (a difference ends the attempt and the unit reads again); then, all in this transaction: the `HvTurnAssessment` and `HvFinding` rows; the holistic scores and verdict and the overall verdict on the request (ScoreVerdict at `max(threshold, 0.98)`, R-31); for each member turn RecordSessionTurnReviewCommand (kind hostile, origin `HvFinalization`, dispatched in the delegate so it joins the transaction) with `hvVerdict` the turn's verdict, its scores, `reasons` its FAIL and UNKNOWN findings prefixed `FAIL:` or `UNKNOWN:`, `reviewer` `<reviewerId>/<runtimeModel>/<runtimeEffort>`, `reviewedAt` the run's `EndedUtc`, and `requestJsonlPath` and `responseJsonlPath` the evidence references `hv-evidence:<hvRequestId>/request` and `hv-evidence:<hvRequestId>/response-log/<runId>` (policy HvVerdictMapping stores the status, A-06); policy HvTurnFreeze `Finalize` (`HvState` `Final`); each `HvRequestTurn` `Reviewed`; for each `Pending` linked response, when Mode is not `Off`, RecordModelGradeCommand (origin `HvFinalization`, the run's reviewer as grader, the response's `hv_response_grade` record) with its trust decision, which marks the response item `Graded`, and when Mode is `Off`, the item `NotGraded` (`agent_context_disabled`); the `Result` evidence (GzipCodec) and `ResultSha256`; the request `Completed` with `CompletedUtc` and `FinalizedRunId`; the run `Succeeded`; NotificationOutbox `hv_completed` with the overall verdict. After the commit, the post-commit dispatches the foundation's grade units make (EvaluateStalenessCommand for dependents, the projection pass) run as they do for a grade (foundation section 3.1, \"Projection pass\").\n1101: - Results: `completed` (with the overall verdict); `already_completed`; `not_finalizable`; `verification_failed` (code); 409 `conflict` (`retryable: true`, the sweep finalizes again); 503 `audit_unavailable` (the request stays `Finalizing`, W-06).\n1102: \n1103: ```mermaid\n1104: flowchart TD\n1105:     S([\"FinalizeHvRequestCommand: hvRequestId\"]) --> ST{\"Request status?\"}\n1106:     ST -->|Completed| R0([\"already_completed: the stored outcome\"])\n1107:     ST -->|\"other than Finalizing\"| R1([\"not_finalizable: nothing written\"])\n1108:     ST -->|Finalizing| RD[[\"ReadFinalizationInputs\"]]\n1109:     RD -->|\"check failed: code\"| FR[[\"FailHvRunCommand with the stored fence and the code\"]]\n1110:     FR --> R2([\"verification_failed: request Queued or Failed\"])\n1111:     RD -->|\"verified records\"| SW[[\"SerializableWrite with AuditLedgerGuard\"]]\n1112:     SW -->|\"audit unavailable\"| E1([\"503 audit_unavailable: request stays Finalizing\"])\n1113:     SW -->|\"attempts exhausted\"| E2([\"409 conflict, retryable true: the sweep finalizes again\"])\n1114:     SW -->|attempt| RC{\"Request, run, chunk manifest, turn states, and response states as read?\"}\n1115:     RC -->|\"no: attempt ends, reads again\"| RD\n1116:     RC -->|yes| CM[[\"CommitFinalResult\"]]\n1117:     CM --> R3([\"completed: overall verdict; post-commit grade dispatches run\"])\n1118: ```\n1119: \n1120: ##### Nested activity: ReadFinalizationInputs (reads of FinalizeHvRequestCommand, no transaction open)\n1121: \n1122: ```mermaid\n1123: flowchart TD\n1124:     S([\"ReadFinalizationInputs\"]) --> RN[\"Load the OutputClosed run and its chunks in sequence\"]\n1125:     RN --> V[[\"Policy HvFinalVerification V-1 to V-8\"]]\n1126:     V -->|\"failed: code\"| F([\"check failed: code\"])\n1127:     V -->|passed| M{\"Linked responses and Mode not Off?\"}\n1128:     M -->|yes| ES[[\"EvaluateStalenessCommand for the linked responses\"]]\n1129:     ES --> OK([\"verified records, response states read\"])\n1130:     M -->|no| OK\n1131: ```\n1132: \n1133: ##### Nested activity: CommitFinalResult (the writes of FinalizeHvRequestCommand, inside its delegate)\n1134: \n1135: ```mermaid\n1136: flowchart TD\n1137:     S([\"CommitFinalResult\"]) --> A[\"Insert HvTurnAssessment and HvFinding rows\"]\n1138:     A --> H[[\"ScoreVerdict at max threshold and 0.98: holistic and overall verdicts on the request\"]]\n1139:     H --> TR[[\"RecordSessionTurnReviewCommand per member turn, origin HvFinalization: policy HvVerdictMapping stores hostileReview\"]]\n1140:     TR --> FN[[\"Policy HvTurnFreeze Finalize: each member turn Final\"]]\n1141:     FN --> RV[\"Each HvRequestTurn Reviewed\"]\n1142:     RV --> MD{\"Pending linked responses?\"}\n1143:     MD -->|\"yes, Mode not Off\"| MG[[\"RecordModelGradeCommand per response, origin HvFinalization, with its trust decision\"]]\n1144:     MD -->|\"yes, Mode Off\"| NG[\"Items NotGraded agent_context_disabled\"]\n1145:     MD -->|no| EV\n1146:     MG --> EV[[\"GzipCodec Compress: the Result evidence\"]]\n1147:     NG --> EV\n1148:     EV --> CP[\"Request Completed with CompletedUtc and FinalizedRunId; run Succeeded\"]\n1149:     CP --> N[[\"NotificationOutbox: hv_completed\"]]\n1150:     N --> OK([\"committed\"])\n1151: ```\n1152: \n1153: #### FileHvIncidentCommand: file an incident through the triage endpoint [FR-MCP-HVPIPE-009]\n1154: \n1155: - Handler: `FileHvIncidentCommand(string WorkspacePath, string IncidentId) : ICommand<HvIncidentDto>` (S-15, S-26, R-17).\n1156: - Order: the incident (`Filed` returns it unchanged); outside any transaction, `ITriageService` submits the report (title `Hostile validation <failureCode> on <reviewerId>`, summary, component `hostile-validation`, `dedupeKey`, `errorSignature` the failure code, the sanitized evidence, the run and request ids, reporter `QBrainAi`), the service behind `POST /qbrainai/triage/reports`; then one SerializableWrite with AuditLedgerGuard records the outcome: accepted sets `TriageReportId`, `TriageGroupId`, `FilingStatus` `Filed`, `FiledUtc`, and appends `incident_filed`; refused or unreachable increments `FilingAttempts` and sets `LastFilingError`, and the sweep tries again (W-08, W-09).\n1157: - Results: filed; filing pending with the error; 409 `conflict` (`retryable: true`); 503 `audit_unavailable`.\n1158: \n1159: ```mermaid\n1160: flowchart TD\n1161:     S([\"FileHvIncidentCommand: incidentId\"]) --> F{\"Incident Filed already?\"}\n1162:     F -->|yes| R0([\"unchanged\"])\n1163:     F -->|no| T[\"ITriageService submit: dedupeKey, errorSignature, sanitized evidence, run and request ids\"]\n1164:     T -->|accepted| SW1[[\"SerializableWrite with AuditLedgerGuard\"]]\n1165:     SW1 -->|committed| FI[\"Filed: report and group ids, FiledUtc\"]\n1166:     FI --> N[[\"NotificationOutbox: incident_filed\"]]\n1167:     N --> R1([\"filed\"])\n1168:     T -->|\"refused or unreachable\"| SW2[[\"SerializableWrite with AuditLedgerGuard\"]]\n1169:     SW2 -->|committed| P[\"FilingAttempts plus 1, LastFilingError set\"]\n1170:     P --> R2([\"filing pending: the sweep tries again\"])\n1171:     SW1 -->|\"audit unavailable\"| E1([\"503 audit_unavailable\"])\n1172:     SW2 -->|\"audit unavailable\"| E1\n1173: ```\n1174: \n1175: ### 14.5 Amended foundation units\n1176: \n1177: - RecordSessionTurnReviewCommand (foundation section 5.2): before policy ReviewValidation it applies the hostile-review rule of A-06 (403 `review_hostile_pipeline_only` for `Pass`, `Fail`, `Running`, or `hvVerdict` on a hostile review from any origin other than `HvFinalization`) and, through TurnWritePipeline, policy HvTurnFreeze (A-07); its error list gains both codes. ResetSessionTurnReviewCommand, the section replace and clear routes and MCP tools, the dialog, title, and turn write units of foundation section 4.2, and the session-level replace and delete gain the 409 `turn_immutable` refusal of HvTurnFreeze.\n1178: - RecordModelGradeCommand (foundation section 6.5): A-05.\n1179: - CreateAgentContextHvRequestCommand, GetAgentContextHvRequestQuery, and QueryAgentContextHvRequestsQuery (foundation section 6.5): superseded, A-04.\n1180: \n1181: ## 15. Policies\n1182: \n1183: ### Policy HvScopeResolution: resolve the member turns [FR-MCP-HVPIPE-004]\n1184: \n1185: Applied by SubmitHvRequestCommand inside its delegate, reading only the database. TurnLocator finds the reviewed session by `agent` and `sessionId` (`SessionNotFound` is `hv_scope_invalid`); `Turn`: the one turn by `requestId`; `Range`: both endpoint turns, then every turn between them inclusive in the session's turn order (the order develop reads a session's turns in: ascending turn row `Id`, VI-06), refused when an endpoint is missing or the start is after the end; `Session`: every turn of the session at this moment (S-11). The submitting turn is removed from a `Session` scope (`ExcludedSubmittingTurn` true) and refuses a `Turn` or `Range` scope that contains it. More than `MaxTurnsPerRequest` members is `hv_scope_too_large` with the count; no member left is `hv_scope_empty`.\n1186: \n1187: ```mermaid\n1188: flowchart TD\n1189:     S([\"HvScopeResolution: scope, submitting turn\"]) --> TL[[\"TurnLocator: the reviewed session\"]]\n1190:     TL -->|\"InvalidIdentifier or SessionNotFound\"| E1([\"400 hv_scope_invalid\"])\nEXIT_CODE=0\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
