{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_60","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/pwsh -NoProfile -Command \"pwsh.exe -NoProfile -NonInteractive -File './docs/receipts/hv/hv-r1-inspect.ps1' -Task Read -Path './docs/architecture/SessionTurn-Review-AgentContext-Architecture-Amendment-1-Durable-HV.md' -Start 1191 -Count 260\"","aggregated_output":"SOURCE ./docs/architecture/SessionTurn-Review-AgentContext-Architecture-Amendment-1-Durable-HV.md totalLines=2785\n1191:     TL -->|session| K{\"Scope kind?\"}\n1192:     K -->|Turn| T1[[\"TurnLocator: the turn\"]]\n1193:     T1 -->|TurnNotFound| E1\n1194:     T1 -->|found| M1[\"Members: that turn\"]\n1195:     K -->|Range| T2[[\"TurnLocator: both endpoint turns\"]]\n1196:     T2 -->|TurnNotFound| E1\n1197:     T2 -->|found| O{\"Start not after end?\"}\n1198:     O -->|no| E1\n1199:     O -->|yes| M2[\"Members: every turn from start to end, inclusive, in session order\"]\n1200:     K -->|Session| M3[\"Members: every turn of the session now\"]\n1201:     M1 --> SB{\"Submitting turn among the members?\"}\n1202:     M2 --> SB\n1203:     SB -->|yes| E2([\"400 hv_scope_includes_submitting_turn\"])\n1204:     SB -->|no| MX\n1205:     M3 --> X[\"Remove the submitting turn when present; set ExcludedSubmittingTurn\"]\n1206:     X --> EM{\"Members left?\"}\n1207:     EM -->|no| E3([\"400 hv_scope_empty\"])\n1208:     EM -->|yes| MX{\"At most MaxTurnsPerRequest?\"}\n1209:     MX -->|no| E4([\"400 hv_scope_too_large, details.count and details.max\"])\n1210:     MX -->|yes| R([\"members in session order\"])\n1211: ```\n1212: \n1213: ### Policy HvAdmissionEligibility: admit only reviewable turns [FR-MCP-HVPIPE-005, -013]\n1214: \n1215: Applied by SubmitHvRequestCommand after HvScopeResolution. It reads each member's status and HV state and never its `agentReview` (R-21). It collects every violation before it refuses, so the refusal names all affected turns: a non-terminal turn (`TurnStatus.IsTerminal` false) is `hv_turns_not_terminal`; a `Pending` turn is `hv_turns_pending` with its open request; a `Final` turn is `hv_turns_already_reviewed` with its request (null for a turn the A-11 migration made `Final`). When more than one kind applies, the first in that order is the code and `details` lists every kind (R-05, R-27).\n1216: \n1217: ```mermaid\n1218: flowchart TD\n1219:     S([\"HvAdmissionEligibility: members\"]) --> C[\"For each member read status and HV state, never agentReview\"]\n1220:     C --> NT{\"Any member not terminal?\"}\n1221:     NT -->|yes| E1([\"409 hv_turns_not_terminal, details lists every turn of every kind\"])\n1222:     NT -->|no| PD{\"Any member Pending?\"}\n1223:     PD -->|yes| E2([\"409 hv_turns_pending, with their open requests\"])\n1224:     PD -->|no| FN{\"Any member Final?\"}\n1225:     FN -->|yes| E3([\"409 hv_turns_already_reviewed, with their requests\"])\n1226:     FN -->|no| R([\"eligible\"])\n1227: ```\n1228: \n1229: ### Policy HvReviewerEligibility: who may review [FR-MCP-HVPIPE-002, -003]\n1230: \n1231: A reviewer is eligible for a request when it is enabled, `Online`, and its id differs from both the request's `SubmitterReviewerId` and its `AuthorReviewerId` (AgentIdentity, R-08). Capacity (`MaxConcurrentRuns`) is a claim-time condition (ClaimHvRunCommand), not eligibility, so admission never refuses a request only because reviewers are busy.\n1232: \n1233: ```mermaid\n1234: flowchart TD\n1235:     S([\"HvReviewerEligibility: reviewer, submitter id, author id\"]) --> E{\"Enabled?\"}\n1236:     E -->|no| N([\"not eligible: disabled\"])\n1237:     E -->|yes| O{\"Online?\"}\n1238:     O -->|no| N2([\"not eligible: readiness and reason\"])\n1239:     O -->|yes| X[[\"AgentIdentity.IsSameReviewer with the submitter id and with the author id\"]]\n1240:     X -->|\"same as either\"| N3([\"not eligible: submitter or author\"])\n1241:     X -->|\"different from both\"| Y([\"eligible\"])\n1242: ```\n1243: \n1244: ### Policy RoundRobinAssignment: pick the next reviewer [FR-MCP-HVPIPE-002, -007]\n1245: \n1246: Applied inside a SerializableWrite (admission, and reassignment at claim). The pool order is Cline, Copilot, Claude, Codex, Grok. Starting after `HvWorkspaceState.LastAssignedReviewerId` (or at the start when null), it takes the first reviewer in cyclic order that HvReviewerEligibility accepts and sets the cursor to it in the same transaction (S-17, R-07). With none eligible it refuses with `hv_no_reviewer_available` and `details.reviewers`, each reviewer's enabled flag, readiness, reason, and open incident, the context S-16 asks the plugin to show.\n1247: \n1248: ```mermaid\n1249: flowchart TD\n1250:     S([\"RoundRobinAssignment: submitter id, author id\"]) --> C[\"Start after the cursor in pool order\"]\n1251:     C --> N{\"Next reviewer in cyclic order, five at most?\"}\n1252:     N -->|\"none left\"| E([\"409 hv_no_reviewer_available, details.reviewers\"])\n1253:     N -->|reviewer| EL[[\"Policy HvReviewerEligibility\"]]\n1254:     EL -->|\"not eligible\"| N\n1255:     EL -->|eligible| U[\"Set LastAssignedReviewerId to the reviewer\"]\n1256:     U --> R([\"assigned reviewer\"])\n1257: ```\n1258: \n1259: ### Policy HvTurnFreeze: freeze, release, finalize, and guard [FR-MCP-HVPIPE-012]\n1260: \n1261: - `Freeze(turns, hvRequestId)`: `HvState` `Pending` and `HvRequestId` on each member turn (SubmitHvRequestCommand). `Release(hvRequestId)`: back to `None` for the turns of a request that ended `Canceled` or `Failed`. `Finalize(hvRequestId)`: `Final` (FinalizeHvRequestCommand). Each writes the turn's HV columns only, never its content, inside the caller's transaction.\n1262: - `Guard(turn, origin)`: applied by TurnWritePipeline after TurnLocator and before every other policy, and by every unit of A-07: a turn whose `HvState` is `Pending` or `Final` refuses every write and delete of the turn or its children, from every origin except `HvFinalization` writing a `Pending` turn of its own request, with 409 `turn_immutable`, `details.reason` `hv_pending` or `hv_final`, and `details.hvRequestId` (S-06, S-07, R-04). A session-level replace or delete that would change such a turn is refused the same way.\n1263: \n1264: ```mermaid\n1265: flowchart TD\n1266:     S([\"HvTurnFreeze Guard: turn, write origin, request\"]) --> ST{\"Turn HvState?\"}\n1267:     ST -->|None| OK([\"allowed\"])\n1268:     ST -->|Final| E1([\"409 turn_immutable, reason hv_final\"])\n1269:     ST -->|Pending| O{\"Origin HvFinalization for this turn's request?\"}\n1270:     O -->|yes| OK\n1271:     O -->|no| E2([\"409 turn_immutable, reason hv_pending\"])\n1272: ```\n1273: \n1274: ### Policy HvFinalVerification: the eight verification steps [FR-MCP-HVPIPE-010, -011, -021]\n1275: \n1276: Applied by FinalizeHvRequestCommand to the run's stored chunks before any transaction; each failed step returns its code, and the steps run in the diagram's order (V-1, V-8, V-2, V-3, V-4, V-5, V-6, V-7), so the log's integrity and completeness are known before any record is bound. They replace the foundation's eight receipt checks (A-05): `receipt_path` becomes V-1 (the evidence is held by the server, not found on disk), `request_meta` becomes V-3 and V-7 (the expected reviewer is recorded on the run), `verdict_block` becomes V-8, `verdict_binding` becomes V-2 and V-3, `verdict_match` becomes V-4, `reviewer_turn` becomes V-6, `reviewer_independent` becomes V-5 (amended, A-09), and `runtime_identity` becomes V-7.\n1277: \n1278: - V-1 Evidence integrity (`evidence_corrupt`): the chunks run 1 to `OutputChunkCount` without a gap; each decompresses (GzipCodec), its SHA-256 equals the stored one, the chain hash equals `OutputChainSha256`, and every line parses as one JSON object (I-06).\n1279: - V-2 Snapshot binding: each `hv_turn_assessment` names a member's ordinal, turn key, and admission snapshot hash (`verdict_binding_failed` otherwise), and TurnSnapshotBuilder over each turn now yields that hash (`snapshot_changed` otherwise; HvTurnFreeze makes it unreachable, and the step proves it, I-02).\n1280: - V-3 Verdict binding (`verdict_binding_failed`): the `hv_verdict` record names this `hvRequestId` and run, its counts equal the members and the `Pending` responses, its reviewer equals the run's reviewer, and each `hv_response_grade` names a `Pending` response with that response's `ContentSha256`.\n1281: - V-4 Verdict consistency (`reviewer_output_invalid`): every score is a valid lexeme (ScoreLexeme); each turn's verdict is `AGREE` exactly when ScoreVerdict derives `Pass` at the hostile thresholds and its findings hold no FAIL or UNKNOWN; the holistic verdict likewise at `max(threshold, 0.98)` (R-31); each response grade follows the foundation's `verdict_match` rule; and the overall verdict is `AGREE` exactly when the holistic verdict and every turn's verdict are `AGREE`.\n1282: - V-5 Reviewer independence (`reviewer_not_independent`): the run's reviewer id differs from the request's submitter id and from its author id (S-17, S-28, P-01, P-07).\n1283: - V-6 Reviewer turn (`reviewer_turn_unverified`): the `hv_reviewer_turn` record names a turn TurnLocator finds, whose agent AgentIdentity maps to the run's reviewer, whose session is neither the reviewed session nor the submitter's, created at or after the run's `StartedUtc`, whose stored result (its response, then its dialog parts in order with each part's header line removed, as foundation check 6 reads it) contains the `hv_verdict` record byte for byte in its stored normal form (P-06, R-24).\n1284: - V-7 Runtime identity (`runtime_identity_mismatch`): the log holds at least one top-level `hv_provenance` line written by the worker from the CLI's runtime receipt of this run, and every one names the run's expected model (or, when the reviewer has no configured model, the model the last NONCE resolved) and expected effort (P-04).\n1285: - V-8 Completeness (`reviewer_output_invalid`): exactly one `hv_verdict`, the last reviewer record; exactly one `hv_holistic`; exactly one `hv_turn_assessment` per member and one `hv_response_grade` per `Pending` response; every finding has an outcome, a category, a location, evidence, and a remediation (S-13); the failures list equals every FAIL and UNKNOWN finding.\n1286: \n1287: ```mermaid\n1288: flowchart TD\n1289:     S([\"HvFinalVerification: run chunks, request, members, responses\"]) --> L[[\"VerifyLogAndBinding: V-1, V-8, V-2, V-3\"]]\n1290:     L -->|\"failed: code\"| E1([\"the step's code, drawn there\"])\n1291:     L -->|\"bound records\"| R[[\"VerifyVerdictAndReviewer: V-4, V-5, V-6, V-7\"]]\n1292:     R -->|\"failed: code\"| E2([\"the step's code, drawn there\"])\n1293:     R -->|passed| OK([\"verified records\"])\n1294: ```\n1295: \n1296: ##### Nested activity: VerifyLogAndBinding (V-1, V-8, V-2, V-3 of HvFinalVerification)\n1297: \n1298: ```mermaid\n1299: flowchart TD\n1300:     S([\"VerifyLogAndBinding\"]) --> V1{\"V-1 chunks contiguous, hashes and chain equal, lines JSON?\"}\n1301:     V1 -->|no| E1([\"evidence_corrupt\"])\n1302:     V1 -->|yes| V8{\"V-8 one verdict last, one holistic, one assessment per member, one grade per pending response, complete findings?\"}\n1303:     V8 -->|no| E8([\"reviewer_output_invalid\"])\n1304:     V8 -->|yes| V2{\"V-2 assessments bound to members and admission hashes?\"}\n1305:     V2 -->|\"assessment names another hash\"| E2a([\"verdict_binding_failed\"])\n1306:     V2 -->|\"turn re-hash differs\"| E2b([\"snapshot_changed\"])\n1307:     V2 -->|yes| V3{\"V-3 verdict names this request, run, counts, reviewer, response hashes?\"}\n1308:     V3 -->|no| E3([\"verdict_binding_failed\"])\n1309:     V3 -->|yes| OK([\"bound records\"])\n1310: ```\n1311: \n1312: ##### Nested activity: VerifyVerdictAndReviewer (V-4 to V-7 of HvFinalVerification)\n1313: \n1314: ```mermaid\n1315: flowchart TD\n1316:     S([\"VerifyVerdictAndReviewer: bound records\"]) --> V4{\"V-4 verdicts consistent with scores and findings?\"}\n1317:     V4 -->|no| E4([\"reviewer_output_invalid\"])\n1318:     V4 -->|yes| V5{\"V-5 reviewer id differs from the submitter and author ids?\"}\n1319:     V5 -->|no| E5([\"reviewer_not_independent\"])\n1320:     V5 -->|yes| V6{\"V-6 reviewer turn found, independent, after the run start, holding the verdict record?\"}\n1321:     V6 -->|no| E6([\"reviewer_turn_unverified\"])\n1322:     V6 -->|yes| V7{\"V-7 worker provenance present, every line the expected model and effort?\"}\n1323:     V7 -->|no| E7([\"runtime_identity_mismatch\"])\n1324:     V7 -->|yes| OK([\"passed\"])\n1325: ```\n1326: \n1327: ### Policy ReadinessProbeVerdict: the NONCE decision [FR-MCP-HVPIPE-003]\n1328: \n1329: Applied by CloseHvRunOutputCommand to a `Probe` run in its transaction. The probe passes when V-1 holds for its chunks, its log holds exactly one `hv_probe` record whose `nonce` equals the run's `ProbeNonce` (`probe_nonce_mismatch` otherwise), an `hv_provenance` line names the expected model and effort (`runtime_identity_mismatch` otherwise; with no configured model the runtime model is accepted and becomes `ResolvedModel`), and its `hv_reviewer_turn` names a turn TurnLocator finds for that reviewer created after the run started (`reviewer_turn_logging_unsupported` otherwise, R-24) (S-27: \"the agent is available and can execute an HV\").\n1330: \n1331: ```mermaid\n1332: flowchart TD\n1333:     S([\"ReadinessProbeVerdict: probe run\"]) --> I{\"Chunks pass V-1?\"}\n1334:     I -->|no| E1([\"failed: evidence_corrupt\"])\n1335:     I -->|yes| N{\"Exactly one hv_probe with the run's nonce?\"}\n1336:     N -->|no| E2([\"failed: probe_nonce_mismatch\"])\n1337:     N -->|yes| P{\"Provenance names the expected model and effort?\"}\n1338:     P -->|no| E3([\"failed: runtime_identity_mismatch\"])\n1339:     P -->|yes| T{\"Reviewer turn found for this reviewer, created after the run started?\"}\n1340:     T -->|no| E4([\"failed: reviewer_turn_logging_unsupported\"])\n1341:     T -->|yes| OK([\"passed: resolved model and effort\"])\n1342: ```\n1343: \n1344: ### Policy HvRetryDecision: requeue, fail, or cancel [FR-MCP-HVPIPE-007, -009]\n1345: \n1346: Applied inside the caller's transaction by FailHvRunCommand and ExpireHvRunLeasesCommand for a review run's request; it decides the request's next state and writes it, so a request ends the same way whether its attempt failed or its worker died. A `CancelRequested` request becomes `Canceled`; otherwise, with the counted attempts (the request's runs except those that ended `worker_shutdown`, which a graceful restart causes and no reviewer does) below `MaxAttemptsPerRequest` the request returns to `Queued` (its assignee re-evaluated at the next claim, R-07); otherwise it becomes `Failed` with `attempts_exhausted`. A canceled or failed request gets `CompletedUtc`, releases its turns (HvTurnFreeze `Release`), closes its `Pending` responses with `request_ended`, and appends `hv_canceled` or `hv_failed` (NotificationOutbox).\n1347: \n1348: ```mermaid\n1349: flowchart TD\n1350:     S([\"HvRetryDecision: request, in the caller's transaction\"]) --> C{\"CancelRequested?\"}\n1351:     C -->|yes| CN[\"Request Canceled with CompletedUtc; Pending responses Closed request_ended\"]\n1352:     CN --> RL1[[\"Policy HvTurnFreeze Release\"]]\n1353:     RL1 --> N1[[\"NotificationOutbox: hv_canceled\"]]\n1354:     N1 --> R1([\"cancel: request Canceled\"])\n1355:     C -->|no| A{\"Counted attempts, worker_shutdown excluded, below MaxAttemptsPerRequest?\"}\n1356:     A -->|yes| QD[\"Request Queued; assignee re-evaluated at the next claim\"]\n1357:     QD --> R2([\"requeue: request Queued\"])\n1358:     A -->|no| FL[\"Request Failed attempts_exhausted with CompletedUtc; Pending responses Closed request_ended\"]\n1359:     FL --> RL2[[\"Policy HvTurnFreeze Release\"]]\n1360:     RL2 --> N2[[\"NotificationOutbox: hv_failed\"]]\n1361:     N2 --> R3([\"fail: request Failed\"])\n1362: ```\n1363: \n1364: ### Reused policy HvVerdictMapping\n1365: \n1366: Foundation section 5.3, unchanged in its rule; its only caller is now RecordSessionTurnReviewCommand dispatched by FinalizeHvRequestCommand with origin `HvFinalization` (A-06).\n1367: \n1368: ## 16. Processes\n1369: \n1370: ### 16.1 Process HvWorkerHost: the durable worker [FR-MCP-HVPIPE-007, -008, -009]\n1371: \n1372: A hosted `BackgroundService` per workspace application (`src/QBrainAi.Services/HostileValidation/Execution/HvWorkerHost.cs`), with a worker id of the host name, process id, and a random suffix. It is the only dispatcher of the internal units (R-29). At start, while `WorkerEnabled`, it requests a NONCE for every enabled `Unverified` reviewer (StartHvReviewerNonceCommand, R-10). Then it loops, woken by an `IChangeEventBus` wake-up or at `PollInterval`: a sweep (ExpireHvRunLeasesCommand, FinalizeHvRequestCommand for every `Finalizing` request it lists, FileHvIncidentCommand for every `Pending` incident), then claims until ClaimHvRunCommand returns null, starting one process RunReviewerProcess per claim. On a graceful shutdown it stops claiming and ends each of its running runs with FailHvRunCommand code `worker_shutdown`, which files no incident, marks no reviewer offline, and does not count as an attempt (policy HvRetryDecision); after a crash the leases expire instead (W-03). A 503 `audit_unavailable` from any unit stops the loop iteration and the next iteration starts from the sweep (W-12).\n1373: \n1374: ```mermaid\n1375: flowchart TD\n1376:     S([\"HvWorkerHost starts\"]) --> EN{\"WorkerEnabled?\"}\n1377:     EN -->|no| IDLE([\"idle: no claims\"])\n1378:     EN -->|yes| NV[[\"StartHvReviewerNonceCommand for each enabled Unverified reviewer\"]]\n1379:     NV --> W[\"Wait for a wake-up or PollInterval\"]\n1380:     W --> SD{\"Shutting down?\"}\n1381:     SD -->|yes| FS[[\"FailHvRunCommand worker_shutdown for each own running run\"]]\n1382:     FS --> END([\"stopped\"])\n1383:     SD -->|no| SW[[\"ExpireHvRunLeasesCommand\"]]\n1384:     SW -->|audit_unavailable| W\n1385:     SW -->|\"sweep result\"| FZ[[\"FinalizeHvRequestCommand for each Finalizing request\"]]\n1386:     FZ --> FI[[\"FileHvIncidentCommand for each Pending incident\"]]\n1387:     FI --> CL[[\"ClaimHvRunCommand\"]]\n1388:     CL -->|\"null, audit_unavailable, or conflict\"| W\n1389:     CL -->|claim| RP[[\"Process RunReviewerProcess, started for this claim\"]]\n1390:     RP --> CL\n1391: ```\n1392: \n1393: ### 16.2 Process RunReviewerProcess: one attempt, live [FR-MCP-HVPIPE-008, -016]\n1394: \n1395: Runs one claimed run. It builds the brief (section 13.3: the accepted request read from the `Request` evidence inside the run envelope, or the probe brief with its nonce), asks the reviewer's adapter for the launch (section 16.3), starts the process with the workspace as its working directory and its plugin as a host session of its own (R-24), and appends the `hv_brief` record as sequence 1. While the process runs it has three concurrent duties and no time limit (R-11, P-02): every line the adapter delivers goes into a buffer that is appended (AppendHvRunOutputCommand) whenever `OutputFlushInterval` passes or `OutputFlushBytes` accumulate (R-12); a heartbeat every `HeartbeatInterval` (RecordHvRunHeartbeatCommand) renews the lease and reads cancellation; and the process exit is awaited. `stale_fence` from any unit kills the process and ends the attempt without another write (W-03); `audit_unavailable` kills the process and ends the attempt (W-12); a retryable `conflict` repeats the same unit call with the same sequence. Every append carries the records the adapter's extraction completed with that batch. On exit the remaining buffer is appended, the adapter's provenance lines are appended (section 16.3), and the run is closed (exit code 0, CloseHvRunOutputCommand, then FinalizeHvRequestCommand for a review; exit code 0 is not evidence of a review, R-11) or failed (FailHvRunCommand with `reviewer_exited_nonzero`, or `reviewer_launch_failed` when the process never started). A cancellation read at a heartbeat kills the process and fails the run with `canceled`, which policy HvRetryDecision turns into the request's `Canceled` (R-28). Killing the process, here and in the diagrams, ends the reviewer's whole process tree, descendants included, also when the root process has already exited; and when the root exits while a descendant still holds its output pipes, the worker ends that descendant before it reads the output to its end. Without that, a descendant that outlives the reviewer would hold the run open forever, because no time limit ends a run (P-02); P14 is the same defect class in the plugin core (FR-MCP-HVPIPE-008-AC011).\n1396: \n1397: ```mermaid\n1398: flowchart TD\n1399:     S([\"RunReviewerProcess: claim\"]) --> B[\"Build the brief: accepted request in the run envelope, or the probe brief\"]\n1400:     B --> L[[\"Reviewer adapter BuildLaunch\"]]\n1401:     L --> ST{\"Process started?\"}\n1402:     ST -->|no| FL[[\"FailHvRunCommand reviewer_launch_failed\"]]\n1403:     FL --> END1([\"attempt ended\"])\n1404:     ST -->|yes| A1[[\"AppendHvRunOutputCommand: sequence 1, the hv_brief record\"]]\n1405:     A1 --> RUN[[\"StreamReviewerOutput: lines, flushes, heartbeats, until exit, stale fence, audit failure, or cancel\"]]\n1406:     RUN -->|\"stale_fence or audit_unavailable\"| K1[\"Kill the process\"]\n1407:     K1 --> END2([\"attempt ended, no further write\"])\n1408:     RUN -->|\"cancel requested\"| K2[\"Kill the process\"]\n1409:     K2 --> FC[[\"FailHvRunCommand canceled\"]]\n1410:     FC --> END3([\"attempt ended: request Canceled\"])\n1411:     RUN -->|\"exited\"| FLS[[\"AppendHvRunOutputCommand: remaining lines, then the adapter's hv_provenance lines\"]]\n1412:     FLS --> EX{\"Exit code 0?\"}\n1413:     EX -->|no| FN[[\"FailHvRunCommand reviewer_exited_nonzero\"]]\n1414:     FN --> END4([\"attempt ended\"])\n1415:     EX -->|yes| CO[[\"CloseHvRunOutputCommand\"]]\n1416:     CO -->|\"Review: Finalizing\"| FZ[[\"FinalizeHvRequestCommand\"]]\n1417:     FZ --> END5([\"attempt ended: request Completed, Queued, or Failed\"])\n1418:     CO -->|\"Probe: passed or failed\"| END6([\"attempt ended: reviewer Online or Offline\"])\n1419: ```\n1420: \n1421: ##### Nested activity: StreamReviewerOutput (the loop of RunReviewerProcess, collapsed above)\n1422: \n1423: ```mermaid\n1424: flowchart TD\n1425:     S([\"StreamReviewerOutput\"]) --> E{\"Next event?\"}\n1426:     E -->|\"line from the adapter\"| BUF[\"Add the JSONL line to the buffer\"]\n1427:     BUF --> FT{\"Flush interval passed or flush bytes reached?\"}\n1428:     FT -->|no| E\n1429:     FT -->|yes| AP[[\"AppendHvRunOutputCommand: the buffer as the next sequence\"]]\n1430:     AP -->|appended| E\n1431:     AP -->|\"retryable conflict\"| AP\n1432:     AP -->|\"stale_fence or audit_unavailable\"| X1([\"stop: stale fence or audit failure\"])\n1433:     E -->|\"heartbeat timer\"| HB[[\"RecordHvRunHeartbeatCommand\"]]\n1434:     HB -->|\"renewed, no cancel\"| E\n1435:     HB -->|\"cancelRequested\"| X2([\"stop: cancel requested\"])\n1436:     HB -->|\"stale_fence or audit_unavailable\"| X1\n1437:     E -->|\"process exited\"| X3([\"stop: exited, with the exit code\"])\n1438: ```\n1439: \n1440: ### 16.3 Reviewer adapter contract [FR-MCP-HVPIPE-001, -003, -008]\n1441: \n1442: `IHvReviewerAdapter` (namespace `QBrainAi.Support.Mcp.HostileValidation.Reviewers`), one implementation per reviewer id:\n1443: \n1444: - `BuildLaunch(brief, reviewer)`: a `ProcessStartInfo` built as an argument list, never a shell string, with the brief on standard input or in a temporary file the adapter deletes after the run; the launch arguments come from one shared launch builder that develop's one-shot strategy also uses, so the per-CLI arguments of `OneShotCliAgentExecutionStrategy` (`AddCodexArguments`, `AddClaudeArguments`, `AddGrokArguments`, `AddClineArguments`, `OneShotCliAgentExecutionStrategy.cs:238-262`) are written once (DRY); processes start through the existing `IProcessSpawner` and `IProcessEnvironmentService` (`OneShotCliAgentExecutionStrategy.cs:18-21`). The shared launch builder holds the one table of highest efforts of section 10 (P9). The reviewer runs behind a write barrier verified for its CLI (VI-03, probes of 2026-10-16): Codex `exec -s read-only` (a write attempt was refused by its sandbox), Grok `--permission-mode plan` (a write call was refused; a headless Grok run then ends `cancelled` at the first call that needs approval, so its launch allows the read tools a review uses), and Copilot `--available-tools` naming only read tools (write and shell tools are not offered at all). Claude's and Cline's plan modes are not accepted as barriers on that evidence (Claude's model declined before its barrier was exercised; Cline ran a shell command in plan mode), so Claude's launch restricts its tools structurally (`--tools`) and Cline stays unqualified until H1 proves a barrier. Whether each reviewer's plugin can still log its turn behind its barrier (the plugin writes host-session state and calls the server) is verified in H1 (VI-03, VI-04); a reviewer that cannot fails its NONCE (R-24).\n1445: - Live lines (R-12, P8): standard output and standard error are read line by line as the process writes them (asynchronous line reads on the redirected streams), and each line is handed to the run's callback at once; nothing waits for the process to end.\n1446: - `NormalizeLine(line, stream)`: a native JSON event line of a CLI run in a JSON streaming mode is kept as written; any other line becomes `{ \"type\": \"hv_raw\", \"stream\", \"line\" }`.\n1447: - `ExtractReviewerRecords(lines)`: one pure function over a run's ordered native lines. It assembles each agent message's complete text by the CLI's event model (Grok's per-token `text` events, Copilot's `assistant.message_delta` events followed by the whole `assistant.message`, Claude's whole assistant messages, Codex's `agent_message` items, Cline's accumulated content) and returns, in message order, every line of that text that is exactly one JSON object of a reviewer record type of section 13.3; the fence lines of a fenced block are ignored, and a line holding other text beside a record is free text. The worker runs it as lines arrive and passes each batch's completed records to AppendHvRunOutputCommand; finalization runs it over the stored log; both get the same records (R-12). Record types the worker writes itself (`hv_brief`, `hv_provenance`, `hv_raw`) are never accepted from message text, so a reviewer cannot forge them.\n1448: - `ReadProvenance(run)`: `hv_provenance` lines read from the CLI's own runtime receipt after the run (P-04), sources verified on 2026-10-16 (VI-01): for Codex, the thread's rollout `turn_context` (fields `model` and `effort`; observed `model` `gpt-6-astra`, `effort` `max`), the source the foundation's `runtime_identity` check reads (foundation section 6.3, check 8); for Claude, the session transcript under `~/.claude/projects` (the assistant message `model` and the request `effort`), written only when session persistence is on, so the launch never passes `--no-session-persistence`; for Grok, the session store `~/.grok/sessions/<cwd>/<sessionId>/` (`summary.json` `reasoning_effort`, and a model id that `chat_history.jsonl` names `grok-4.7-build` while the events name `grok-4.7`, so H1 pins the field V-7 compares); for Copilot, the run's own JSON stream (each call's `assistant.message.model` and `user.message.responsesReasoning.effort`; `--usage-output-file` holds the model only); for Cline, none, because its run records hold the model and only whether thinking was on, so V-7 and the NONCE fail closed (L-04, D-06).\n1449: - Highest effort when none is configured: the verified values of section 10 (VI-08), never develop's one-shot constants (P9).\n1450: \nEXIT_CODE=0\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
