{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_66","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/pwsh -NoProfile -Command \"pwsh.exe -NoProfile -NonInteractive -File './docs/receipts/hv/hv-r1-inspect.ps1' -Task Read -Path './docs/architecture/SessionTurn-Review-AgentContext-Architecture-Amendment-1-Durable-HV.md' -Start 1451 -Count 400\"","aggregated_output":"SOURCE ./docs/architecture/SessionTurn-Review-AgentContext-Architecture-Amendment-1-Durable-HV.md totalLines=2785\n1451: ### 16.4 Process SubmitHvFromPlugin: the plugin verb [FR-MCP-HVPIPE-005, -020]\n1452: \n1453: `workflow.hv.submit` in the PowerShell core (`plugins/core/lib-ps/repl-invoke.ps1`): process BindVerbToTurn (foundation section 4.4) binds the invocation to its turn; the verb sends SubmitHvRequestCommand through the REPL with `submitter` that turn's key and `idempotencyKey` `hv-<requestId>-<first 16 hex of the SHA-256 of the scope and context>`, so a repeat of the same call is the same request. A created or stored request is recorded in `sessions/<hostSessionKey>/hv-notifications.yaml` (`submitted`) for the watcher (section 16.5) and reported with its id, status, and reviewer. `hv_no_reviewer_available` is reported with the context S-16 asks for: each reviewer's enabled flag, readiness, and reason from `details.reviewers`, the open incident of each `Offline` reviewer (through `workflow.hv.incidents`), and the remedy text \"after the cause is fixed, NONCE the reviewer: workflow.hv.nonce <reviewerId>\". Every other refusal is reported with its code, final. A retryable answer (transport outage, 503, 409 with `retryable: true`) is reported with `retryable: true` and exit 1 and is not queued in the failsafe, because the same call with the same key can simply be repeated (the reviews' no-failsafe rule, foundation section 5.2).\n1454: \n1455: ```mermaid\n1456: flowchart TD\n1457:     S([\"workflow.hv.submit: scope, context\"]) --> B[[\"Process BindVerbToTurn\"]]\n1458:     B -->|refused| E1([\"refusal of BindVerbToTurn, drawn there\"])\n1459:     B -->|bound turn| K[\"Submitter the bound turn key; idempotencyKey from requestId, scope, and context\"]\n1460:     K --> SUB[\"REPL: SubmitHvRequestCommand\"]\n1461:     SUB -->|\"201 or 200\"| REC[\"Record the hvRequestId in hv-notifications.yaml submitted\"]\n1462:     REC --> R1([\"reported: id, status, reviewer\"])\n1463:     SUB -->|\"409 hv_no_reviewer_available\"| CTX[\"Add reviewer statuses, open incidents, and the NONCE remedy\"]\n1464:     CTX --> R2([\"reported: refusal with context, exit 1\"])\n1465:     SUB -->|\"retryable answer\"| R3([\"reported: code, retryable true, exit 1, not queued\"])\n1466:     SUB -->|\"other refusal\"| R4([\"reported: code, final, exit 1\"])\n1467: ```\n1468: \n1469: ### 16.5 Process WatchHvNotifications: completions into the plugin [FR-MCP-HVPIPE-017, -020]\n1470: \n1471: Started by process StartHostSession (foundation section 4.4) for each host session and stopped by EndHostSession; one instance per host session (`sessions/<hostSessionKey>/hv-watcher.pid`, the arrival bridge's pattern). It runs the REPL streaming verb `workflow.hv.watchNotifications` with `Last-Event-ID` the `lastSequence` of `sessions/<hostSessionKey>/hv-notifications.yaml`. For each event it records `lastSequence` and, when the event is `hv_completed`, `hv_failed`, or `hv_canceled` for a request in `submitted`, appends it to `sessions/<hostSessionKey>/hv-inbox.yaml`; each write is one atomic replace (temp file, flush, rename) under `hv-notifications.lock`. A disconnect reconnects with backoff from the recorded sequence, so nothing is missed (R-16). The prompt hook adds each undelivered inbox entry once to the next prompt's context (\"HV <hvRequestId> <status>, overall verdict <verdict>; result: workflow.hv.result <hvRequestId>\") and marks it delivered. Plugins never call REST; the REPL holds the stream (R-30).\n1472: \n1473: ```mermaid\n1474: flowchart TD\n1475:     S([\"WatchHvNotifications: host session\"]) --> P{\"Watcher already running for this host session?\"}\n1476:     P -->|yes| X([\"exit: one instance\"])\n1477:     P -->|no| C[\"REPL workflow.hv.watchNotifications from lastSequence\"]\n1478:     C --> E{\"Next event?\"}\n1479:     E -->|\"notification\"| M{\"Terminal kind for a submitted request?\"}\n1480:     M -->|yes| IN[\"Append to hv-inbox.yaml and record lastSequence, one atomic replace\"]\n1481:     M -->|no| LS[\"Record lastSequence, one atomic replace\"]\n1482:     IN --> E\n1483:     LS --> E\n1484:     E -->|disconnected| BK[\"Wait with backoff\"]\n1485:     BK --> C\n1486:     E -->|\"host session ended\"| END([\"stopped\"])\n1487: ```\n1488: \n1489: ### 16.6 Director HV commands [FR-MCP-HVPIPE-020]\n1490: \n1491: The Director commands of section 13.1 run through `IHostileValidationDirectorExecutor` in `src/QBrainAi.Cqrs.Mvvm/HostileValidationDirectorCommands.cs`, the pattern of the existing hostile-review Director commands (`src/QBrainAi.Cqrs.Mvvm/HostileReviewDirectorCommands.cs:22`); `hv-output` and `hv-notifications` consume the client streams and reconnect from their last event id; `hv-submit` submits as `Operator` with the operator's name (R-09). Each command is a thin call of one client method and carries no logic of its own.\n1492: \n1493: ## 17. Sequence diagrams\n1494: \n1495: Participants: `Caller` is any surface's caller (a plugin through the REPL, the REPL, Director, an MCP client, or a REST client); `API` is the controller or MCP tool, which dispatches through `IDispatcher`; `Pipe` is WorkspaceResolutionBehavior; `H` is the unit's handler; `DB` is the relational store; `W` is process HvWorkerHost with RunReviewerProcess; `AD` is the reviewer adapter and its process; `TG` is `ITriageService`. Every sequence that dispatches draws the workspace refusal after the dispatch (foundation section 3, \"Errors\"); a body that does not bind keeps the existing validation problem. Shared components appear as one message.\n1496: \n1497: ### 17.1 ListHvReviewersQuery and GetHvReviewerQuery\n1498: \n1499: ```mermaid\n1500: sequenceDiagram\n1501:     participant Caller\n1502:     participant API\n1503:     participant Pipe\n1504:     participant H\n1505:     participant DB\n1506:     Caller->>API: GET reviewers, or GET reviewers/{reviewerId}\n1507:     API->>Pipe: QueryAsync\n1508:     alt workspace unresolved\n1509:         Pipe-->>Caller: 400 validation_error, details.field workspacePath\n1510:     else resolved\n1511:         Pipe->>H: handler runs\n1512:         H->>H: AgentIdentity.Normalize, for one reviewer\n1513:         alt unknown reviewer id\n1514:             H-->>Caller: 404 not_found, reviewer\n1515:         else known\n1516:             H->>DB: load reviewers and count active runs\n1517:             DB-->>H: rows\n1518:             H-->>Caller: 200 HvReviewerDto list, or one HvReviewerDto\n1519:         end\n1520:     end\n1521: ```\n1522: \n1523: ### 17.2 UpdateHvReviewerCommand\n1524: \n1525: ```mermaid\n1526: sequenceDiagram\n1527:     participant Caller\n1528:     participant API\n1529:     participant Pipe\n1530:     participant H\n1531:     participant DB\n1532:     participant W\n1533:     Caller->>API: PATCH reviewers/{reviewerId} with expectedStateVersion\n1534:     API->>Pipe: SendAsync\n1535:     alt workspace unresolved\n1536:         Pipe-->>Caller: 400 validation_error, workspacePath\n1537:     else resolved\n1538:         Pipe->>H: handler runs\n1539:         alt invalid field or no expectedStateVersion\n1540:             H-->>Caller: 400 validation_error, details.field\n1541:         else unknown reviewer id\n1542:             H-->>Caller: 404 not_found, reviewer\n1543:         else valid\n1544:             H->>DB: SerializableWrite with AuditLedgerGuard\n1545:             alt audit ledger unavailable\n1546:                 DB-->>H: refused\n1547:                 H-->>Caller: 503 audit_unavailable\n1548:             else stale expectedStateVersion\n1549:                 H-->>Caller: 409 conflict, retryable false, details.field expectedStateVersion\n1550:             else attempts exhausted\n1551:                 H-->>Caller: 409 conflict, retryable true\n1552:             else committed\n1553:                 DB-->>H: updated row, readiness Unverified when the launch changed\n1554:                 H-->>Caller: 200 HvReviewerDto\n1555:                 H-)W: wake, NONCE the Unverified reviewer\n1556:             end\n1557:         end\n1558:     end\n1559: ```\n1560: \n1561: ### 17.3 StartHvReviewerNonceCommand and the probe it starts\n1562: \n1563: ```mermaid\n1564: sequenceDiagram\n1565:     participant Caller\n1566:     participant API\n1567:     participant H\n1568:     participant DB\n1569:     participant W\n1570:     participant AD\n1571:     Caller->>API: POST reviewers/{reviewerId}/nonce\n1572:     API->>H: SendAsync, after the workspace behavior\n1573:     alt unknown reviewer\n1574:         H-->>Caller: 404 not_found, reviewer\n1575:     else disabled\n1576:         H-->>Caller: 409 hv_reviewer_disabled\n1577:     else probe already running\n1578:         H-->>Caller: 202 Running with its runId\n1579:     else probe already requested\n1580:         H-->>Caller: 202 AlreadyRequested\n1581:     else audit ledger unavailable\n1582:         H-->>Caller: 503 audit_unavailable\n1583:     else requested\n1584:         H->>DB: set ProbeRequestedUtc\n1585:         H-->>Caller: 202 Requested\n1586:         H-)W: wake\n1587:         W->>DB: ClaimHvRunCommand creates the Probe run with a fresh nonce\n1588:         W->>AD: launch with the probe brief\n1589:         AD-->>W: live lines, the hv_probe record, then exit\n1590:         W->>DB: AppendHvRunOutputCommand for each batch, then the hv_provenance lines\n1591:         W->>DB: CloseHvRunOutputCommand, policy ReadinessProbeVerdict\n1592:         alt probe passed\n1593:             DB-->>W: reviewer Online, notification reviewer_online\n1594:         else nonce, provenance, or reviewer turn failed\n1595:             DB-->>W: reviewer Offline, incident Pending, notification reviewer_offline\n1596:             W->>TG: FileHvIncidentCommand at the next sweep\n1597:         end\n1598:     end\n1599: ```\n1600: \n1601: ### 17.4 SubmitHvRequestCommand from the plugin verb\n1602: \n1603: ```mermaid\n1604: sequenceDiagram\n1605:     participant Model\n1606:     participant Plugin\n1607:     participant API\n1608:     participant Pipe\n1609:     participant H\n1610:     participant DB\n1611:     participant W\n1612:     Model->>Plugin: workflow.hv.submit with a scope and context\n1613:     Plugin->>Plugin: process BindVerbToTurn, then the idempotency key\n1614:     alt binding refused\n1615:         Plugin-->>Model: the refusal of BindVerbToTurn\n1616:     else bound\n1617:         Plugin->>API: REPL SubmitHvRequestCommand with the submitter turn key\n1618:         API->>Pipe: SendAsync\n1619:         alt workspace unresolved\n1620:             Pipe-->>Plugin: 400 validation_error, workspacePath\n1621:         else resolved\n1622:             Pipe->>H: handler runs\n1623:             H->>H: shape checks, RequirementReferenceExtractor\n1624:             H->>DB: SerializableWrite with AuditLedgerGuard\n1625:             Note over H,DB: ref AdmitRequestChecks and InsertAdmittedRequest, section 14.2\n1626:             alt malformed scope or submitter\n1627:                 H-->>Plugin: 400 hv_scope_invalid or validation_error\n1628:             else scope too large, includes the submitting turn, or empty\n1629:                 H-->>Plugin: 400 hv_scope_too_large, hv_scope_includes_submitting_turn, or hv_scope_empty\n1630:             else turns not terminal, pending, or already reviewed\n1631:                 H-->>Plugin: 409 with every affected turn listed\n1632:             else no eligible reviewer\n1633:                 H-->>Plugin: 409 hv_no_reviewer_available with details.reviewers\n1634:                 Plugin-->>Model: refusal with reviewer statuses, open incidents, and the NONCE remedy\n1635:             else same key and same inputs\n1636:                 H-->>Plugin: 200 the stored request\n1637:             else key reused with other inputs\n1638:                 H-->>Plugin: 409 conflict, retryable false\n1639:             else audit unavailable or attempts exhausted\n1640:                 H-->>Plugin: 503 audit_unavailable or 409 conflict, retryable true\n1641:                 Plugin-->>Model: retryable true, exit 1, not queued\n1642:             else admitted\n1643:                 DB-->>H: request Queued, turns Pending, notification hv_queued\n1644:                 H-->>Plugin: 201 HvRequestResult\n1645:                 H-)W: wake, auto-start\n1646:                 Plugin->>Plugin: record the hvRequestId for the watcher\n1647:                 Plugin-->>Model: id, status, assigned reviewer\n1648:             end\n1649:         end\n1650:     end\n1651: ```\n1652: \n1653: ### 17.5 GetHvRequestQuery and QueryHvRequestsQuery\n1654: \n1655: ```mermaid\n1656: sequenceDiagram\n1657:     participant Caller\n1658:     participant API\n1659:     participant H\n1660:     participant DB\n1661:     Caller->>API: GET requests/{hvRequestId}, or GET requests with filters\n1662:     API->>H: QueryAsync, after the workspace behavior\n1663:     alt one request, not found\n1664:         H-->>Caller: 404 not_found, hv_request\n1665:     else one request, found\n1666:         H->>DB: load turns, references, responses, current run, last chunks\n1667:         alt output present and audit ledger unavailable\n1668:             H-->>Caller: 503 audit_unavailable\n1669:         else read recorded or no output\n1670:             H-->>Caller: 200 HvRequestResult with progress, etaStatus, and the last 20 lines\n1671:         end\n1672:     else query with an unknown filter or out-of-bounds page\n1673:         H-->>Caller: 400 validation_error, details.field\n1674:     else query\n1675:         H->>DB: PagedQuery, CreatedUtc descending\n1676:         H-->>Caller: 200 PageResult of summaries\n1677:     end\n1678: ```\n1679: \n1680: ### 17.6 CancelHvRequestCommand\n1681: \n1682: ```mermaid\n1683: sequenceDiagram\n1684:     participant Caller\n1685:     participant API\n1686:     participant H\n1687:     participant DB\n1688:     participant W\n1689:     participant AD\n1690:     Caller->>API: POST requests/{hvRequestId}/cancel\n1691:     API->>H: SendAsync, after the workspace behavior\n1692:     H->>DB: SerializableWrite with AuditLedgerGuard\n1693:     alt not found\n1694:         H-->>Caller: 404 not_found, hv_request\n1695:     else Finalizing, Completed, or Failed\n1696:         H-->>Caller: 409 hv_request_not_cancelable\n1697:     else already CancelRequested or Canceled\n1698:         H-->>Caller: 200 unchanged\n1699:     else audit unavailable or attempts exhausted\n1700:         H-->>Caller: 503 audit_unavailable or 409 conflict, retryable true\n1701:     else Queued\n1702:         DB-->>H: Canceled, turns released, hv_canceled\n1703:         H-->>Caller: 200 Canceled\n1704:     else Running\n1705:         DB-->>H: CancelRequested, hv_cancel_requested\n1706:         H-->>Caller: 200 CancelRequested\n1707:         W->>DB: RecordHvRunHeartbeatCommand\n1708:         DB-->>W: cancelRequested true\n1709:         W->>AD: kill the process\n1710:         W->>DB: FailHvRunCommand canceled\n1711:         DB-->>W: run Canceled, request Canceled, turns released, hv_canceled\n1712:     end\n1713: ```\n1714: \n1715: ### 17.7 A review attempt, from claim to finalization\n1716: \n1717: ```mermaid\n1718: sequenceDiagram\n1719:     participant W\n1720:     participant H\n1721:     participant DB\n1722:     participant AD\n1723:     W->>H: ClaimHvRunCommand\n1724:     H->>DB: SerializableWrite: oldest Queued request, eligible reviewer with capacity, FencedLease Claim\n1725:     alt nothing claimable\n1726:         H-->>W: null\n1727:     else claimed\n1728:         DB-->>H: run Claimed, request Running, hv_started\n1729:         H-->>W: claim with fence token\n1730:         W->>AD: BuildLaunch and start the process\n1731:         alt launch failed\n1732:             W->>H: FailHvRunCommand reviewer_launch_failed\n1733:             Note over W,H: ref the execution failure sequence, 17.8\n1734:         else started\n1735:             W->>H: AppendHvRunOutputCommand sequence 1, the hv_brief record\n1736:             Note over W,AD: ref StreamOneAttempt (below)\n1737:             alt stale fence or audit unavailable during the run\n1738:                 W->>AD: kill the process\n1739:                 Note over W: attempt ends without another write, the lease expires later, 17.9\n1740:             else cancel requested\n1741:                 W->>AD: kill the process\n1742:                 W->>H: FailHvRunCommand canceled\n1743:             else exited with a nonzero code\n1744:                 W->>H: FailHvRunCommand reviewer_exited_nonzero\n1745:             else exited with code 0\n1746:                 W->>H: AppendHvRunOutputCommand, the remaining lines and the hv_provenance lines\n1747:                 W->>H: CloseHvRunOutputCommand with the chunk count\n1748:                 H-->>W: request Finalizing\n1749:                 Note over W,H: ref FinalizeOneRequest (below)\n1750:             end\n1751:         end\n1752:     end\n1753: ```\n1754: \n1755: #### Nested sequence: StreamOneAttempt (the live part of the review attempt)\n1756: \n1757: ```mermaid\n1758: sequenceDiagram\n1759:     participant W\n1760:     participant H\n1761:     participant DB\n1762:     participant AD\n1763:     loop until the process exits, a stale fence, an audit failure, or a cancel\n1764:         alt a line arrives\n1765:             AD-->>W: output line, at once\n1766:             W->>W: add to the buffer\n1767:             opt flush interval passed or flush bytes reached\n1768:                 W->>H: AppendHvRunOutputCommand with the next sequence\n1769:                 alt appended\n1770:                     H->>DB: chunk stored, manifest and progress updated\n1771:                     H-->>W: appended, streams woken\n1772:                 else retryable conflict\n1773:                     H-->>W: 409 conflict, retryable true\n1774:                     W->>H: the same append again\n1775:                 else stale fence or audit unavailable\n1776:                     H-->>W: stale_fence or 503 audit_unavailable\n1777:                 end\n1778:             end\n1779:         else the heartbeat timer fires\n1780:             W->>H: RecordHvRunHeartbeatCommand\n1781:             alt renewed\n1782:                 H-->>W: lease extended, cancelRequested false\n1783:             else cancel requested\n1784:                 H-->>W: cancelRequested true\n1785:             else stale fence or audit unavailable\n1786:                 H-->>W: stale_fence or 503 audit_unavailable\n1787:             end\n1788:         end\n1789:     end\n1790: ```\n1791: \n1792: #### Nested sequence: FinalizeOneRequest (FinalizeHvRequestCommand after a closed attempt)\n1793: \n1794: ```mermaid\n1795: sequenceDiagram\n1796:     participant W\n1797:     participant H\n1798:     participant DB\n1799:     W->>H: FinalizeHvRequestCommand\n1800:     alt already Completed\n1801:         H-->>W: already_completed, nothing written\n1802:     else not Finalizing\n1803:         H-->>W: not_finalizable, nothing written\n1804:     else Finalizing\n1805:         H->>DB: read the run and its chunks, no transaction\n1806:         H->>H: policy HvFinalVerification V-1 to V-8\n1807:         alt a step failed\n1808:             H->>H: FailHvRunCommand with the stored fence and the code\n1809:             H-->>W: verification_failed, request Queued or Failed\n1810:         else verified\n1811:             opt linked responses and Mode not Off\n1812:                 H->>H: EvaluateStalenessCommand for the linked responses\n1813:             end\n1814:             H->>DB: SerializableWrite with AuditLedgerGuard: re-check, then CommitFinalResult\n1815:             alt state differs from the reads\n1816:                 DB-->>H: attempt ends, reads again\n1817:             else audit unavailable or attempts exhausted\n1818:                 H-->>W: 503 audit_unavailable or 409 conflict, the request stays Finalizing\n1819:             else committed\n1820:                 DB-->>H: assessments, findings, hostile reviews, turns Final, grades, Completed, hv_completed\n1821:                 H-->>W: completed with the overall verdict\n1822:             end\n1823:         end\n1824:     end\n1825: ```\n1826: \n1827: ### 17.8 An execution failure, its incident, and the reviewer going offline\n1828: \n1829: ```mermaid\n1830: sequenceDiagram\n1831:     participant W\n1832:     participant H\n1833:     participant DB\n1834:     participant TG\n1835:     participant Caller\n1836:     W->>H: FailHvRunCommand with a reviewer-attributable code\n1837:     H->>DB: SerializableWrite with AuditLedgerGuard and FencedLease Guard\n1838:     alt stale fence\n1839:         H-->>W: stale_fence, nothing changed\n1840:     else guarded\n1841:         DB-->>H: run Failed, incident Pending, reviewer Offline, reviewer_offline\n1842:         alt attempts left\n1843:             DB-->>H: request Queued, through policy HvRetryDecision\n1844:         else attempts exhausted\n1845:             DB-->>H: request Failed, turns released, responses closed, hv_failed\n1846:         end\n1847:         H-->>W: failed with the request's next state\n1848:         W->>H: FileHvIncidentCommand at the sweep\n1849:         H->>TG: submit the report with dedupeKey hv-reviewer-id-code\n1850:         alt triage accepted\nEXIT_CODE=0\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
