v_failed\n1883:         end\n1884:     end\n1885:     H-->>W2: abandoned runs and Finalizing requests\n1886:     W2->>H: FinalizeHvRequestCommand for each Finalizing request\n1887:     W2->>H: ClaimHvRunCommand\n1888:     opt worker A was alive but paused past its lease\n1889:         W1->>H: any fenced write with the old fence\n1890:         H-->>W1: stale_fence\n1891:         W1->>W1: kill its process, end the attempt\n1892:     end\n1893: ```\n1894: \n1895: ### 17.10 GetHvResultQuery and GetHvEvidenceQuery\n1896: \n1897: ```mermaid\n1898: sequenceDiagram\n1899:     participant Caller\n1900:     participant API\n1901:     participant H\n1902:     participant DB\n1903:     Caller->>API: GET requests/{hvRequestId}/result, or GET requests/{hvRequestId}/evidence/{kind}\n1904:     API->>H: QueryAsync, after the workspace behavior\n1905:     alt unknown kind\n1906:         H-->>Caller: 400 validation_error, details.field kind\n1907:     else request or run not found\n1908:         H-->>Caller: 404 not_found, hv_request or run\n1909:     else result before Completed\n1910:         H-->>Caller: 409 hv_result_not_ready\n1911:     else evidence not produced yet\n1912:         H-->>Caller: 404 hv_evidence_not_available\n1913:     else evidence removed\n1914:         H-->>Caller: 410 hv_evidence_removed with hashes and sizes\n1915:     else audit ledger unavailable\n1916:         H-->>Caller: 503 audit_unavailable\n1917:     else available\n1918:         H->>DB: AuditLedgerGuard RecordRead, then read the evidence\n1919:         DB-->>H: GZIP members and chunks\n1920:         H-->>Caller: 200 gzip, or decompressed when asked, streamed\n1921:     end\n1922: ```\n1923: \n1924: ### 17.11 RemoveHvEvidenceCommand\n1925: \n1926: ```mermaid\n1927: sequenceDiagram\n1928:     participant Caller\n1929:     participant API\n1930:     participant H\n1931:     participant DB\n1932:     Caller->>API: POST requests/{hvRequestId}/evidence/remove with reason and removedBy\n1933:     API->>H: SendAsync, after the workspace behavior\n1934:     alt reason or removedBy missing or too long\n1935:         H-->>Caller: 400 validation_error, details.field\n1936:     else not found\n1937:         H-->>Caller: 404 not_found, hv_request\n1938:     else request not terminal\n1939:         H-->>Caller: 409 hv_request_active\n1940:     else audit unavailable or attempts exhausted\n1941:         H-->>Caller: 503 audit_unavailable or 409 conflict, retryable true\n1942:     else removed or nothing left\n1943:         H->>DB: null the payloads, stamp the removal, ledger rows\n1944:         H-->>Caller: 200 removed kinds and chunk count, empty on a repeat\n1945:     end\n1946: ```\n1947: \n1948: ### 17.12 StreamHvRunOutputQuery with a reconnect\n1949: \n1950: ```mermaid\n1951: sequenceDiagram\n1952:     participant Caller\n1953:     participant API\n1954:     participant H\n1955:     participant DB\n1956:     participant W\n1957:     Caller->>API: GET requests/{hvRequestId}/output/stream\n1958:     API->>H: QueryAsync, after the workspace behavior\n1959:     alt not found\n1960:         H-->>Caller: 404 not_found, hv_request\n1961:     else malformed Last-Event-ID\n1962:         H-->>Caller: 400 validation_error, Last-Event-ID\n1963:     else audit ledger unavailable\n1964:         H-->>Caller: 503 audit_unavailable\n1965:     else attached\n1966:         H->>DB: RecordRead, then stored chunks after the position\n1967:         H-->>Caller: hv_output events with id runId and sequence\n1968:         W-)H: wake after each append\n1969:         H->>DB: new chunks\n1970:         H-->>Caller: hv_output events, live while the reviewer runs\n1971:         Note over Caller,API: the connection drops\n1972:         Caller->>API: GET the same stream with Last-Event-ID runId and sequence\n1973:         API->>H: QueryAsync\n1974:         H->>DB: chunks after that sequence, then later runs\n1975:         H-->>Caller: the missed events, then live events\n1976:         H-->>Caller: hv_run_closed, then the stream ends when the request is terminal\n1977:     end\n1978: ```\n1979: \n1980: ### 17.13 StreamHvNotificationsQuery through the plugin watcher\n1981: \n1982: ```mermaid\n1983: sequenceDiagram\n1984:     participant Watcher as Plugin watcher\n1985:     participant API\n1986:     participant H\n1987:     participant DB\n1988:     participant Hook as Prompt hook\n1989:     Watcher->>API: REPL workflow.hv.watchNotifications from lastSequence\n1990:     API->>H: QueryAsync, after the workspace behavior\n1991:     alt malformed Last-Event-ID\n1992:         H-->>Watcher: 400 validation_error, Last-Event-ID\n1993:     else attached\n1994:         H->>DB: notifications after lastSequence\n1995:         H-->>Watcher: events in sequence order\n1996:         Watcher->>Watcher: record lastSequence, inbox the completions of its own requests\n1997:         Note over Watcher,API: the connection drops\n1998:         Watcher->>API: reconnect with Last-Event-ID lastSequence, with backoff\n1999:         H-->>Watcher: the missed events, then live events\n2000:         Hook->>Watcher: read the inbox at the next prompt\n2001:         Hook->>Hook: add each undelivered completion to the prompt context once\n2002:     end\n2003: ```\n2004: \n2005: ### 17.14 QueryHvNotificationsQuery and QueryHvIncidentsQuery\n2006: \n2007: ```mermaid\n2008: sequenceDiagram\n2009:     participant Caller\n2010:     participant API\n2011:     participant H\n2012:     participant DB\n2013:     Caller->>API: GET notifications with afterSequence and limit, or GET incidents with filters\n2014:     API->>H: QueryAsync, after the workspace behavior\n2015:     alt a parameter out of range or an unknown filter\n2016:         H-->>Caller: 400 validation_error, details.field\n2017:     else valid\n2018:         H->>DB: rows after the sequence, or PagedQuery of incidents\n2019:         H-->>Caller: 200 items and lastSequence, or a PageResult of incidents\n2020:     end\n2021: ```\n2022: \n2023: ### 17.15 A write to a frozen turn, and a hostile review from an agent surface\n2024: \n2025: ```mermaid\n2026: sequenceDiagram\n2027:     participant Model\n2028:     participant Plugin\n2029:     participant API\n2030:     participant H\n2031:     participant DB\n2032:     Model->>Plugin: any session-log verb for a turn under HV\n2033:     Plugin->>API: the verb's route, through the REPL\n2034:     API->>H: the foundation unit, through TurnWritePipeline\n2035:     H->>DB: TurnLocator, then policy HvTurnFreeze Guard\n2036:     alt turn Pending\n2037:         H-->>Plugin: 409 turn_immutable, reason hv_pending, hvRequestId\n2038:     else turn Final\n2039:         H-->>Plugin: 409 turn_immutable, reason hv_final, hvRequestId\n2040:     end\n2041:     Plugin-->>Model: final refusal: record later changes in a later turn\n2042:     Model->>Plugin: recordReview hostile with status Pass, Fail, Running, or an hvVerdict\n2043:     Plugin->>API: RecordSessionTurnReviewCommand\n2044:     API->>H: handler runs\n2045:     H-->>Plugin: 403 review_hostile_pipeline_only\n2046:     Plugin-->>Model: final refusal: request an HV instead\n2047: ```\n2048: \n2049: ## 18. Use cases\n2050: \n2051: The foundation's notation (foundation section 7): actors are stadium shapes on the left, the use case is the central oval, included and extending behaviors are ovals linked `include` or `extend`. Labels `UC-HV-01` to `UC-HV-12` are document labels; the use-case store keys a use case by a numeric surrogate and its title (`src/QBrainAi.Storage/Entities/UseCaseEntity.cs:12-13`), so H0 creates each under its section title and records the store id beside the label (section 20). Actor names describe participants, not access roles (S-29). One alternate applies to every use case and is not repeated: an unresolved workspace is refused with 400 `validation_error`, `details.field` `workspacePath`. A flow names in parentheses the unit, policy, process, or component that performs a step.\n2052: \n2053: ### 18.1 Overview\n2054: \n2055: ```mermaid\n2056: flowchart LR\n2057:     OP([\"Operator\"])\n2058:     MD([\"Model, through its plugin\"])\n2059:     WK([\"HV worker\"])\n2060:     RV([\"Reviewer agent\"])\n2061:     CL([\"Any client: REPL, Director, MCP, REST\"])\n2062:     TG([\"Triage\"])\n2063:     U1((\"UC-HV-01 Manage the reviewer pool\"))\n2064:     U2((\"UC-HV-02 NONCE a reviewer\"))\n2065:     U3((\"UC-HV-03 Submit an HV request\"))\n2066:     U4((\"UC-HV-04 Run a review live\"))\n2067:     U5((\"UC-HV-05 Finalize the HV result\"))\n2068:     U6((\"UC-HV-06 Watch an HV live\"))\n2069:     U7((\"UC-HV-07 Receive completion notifications\"))\n2070:     U8((\"UC-HV-08 Cancel an HV\"))\n2071:     U9((\"UC-HV-09 Recover from failures\"))\n2072:     U10((\"UC-HV-10 Retrieve the result and evidence\"))\n2073:     U11((\"UC-HV-11 Remove evidence on instruction\"))\n2074:     U12((\"UC-HV-12 Remediate after a reviewed turn\"))\n2075:     OP --- U1\n2076:     OP --- U2\n2077:     OP --- U8\n2078:     OP --- U11\n2079:     MD --- U3\n2080:     MD --- U7\n2081:     MD --- U12\n2082:     CL --- U3\n2083:     CL --- U6\n2084:     CL --- U8\n2085:     CL --- U10\n2086:     WK --- U2\n2087:     WK --- U4\n2088:     WK --- U5\n2089:     WK --- U9\n2090:     RV --- U2\n2091:     RV --- U4\n2092:     TG --- U9\n2093: ```\n2094: \n2095: ### 18.2 UC-HV-01 Manage the reviewer pool [FR-MCP-HVPIPE-001]\n2096: \n2097: Actors: Operator (through Director or the REPL), server. Trigger: the operator lists, inspects, enables, disables, or retunes a reviewer. Preconditions: the server started with the five reviewers configured and seeded (section 10). Main flow: the operator lists the pool (ListHvReviewersQuery), reads one reviewer (GetHvReviewerQuery), and changes its enabled flag, strategy, agent path, model, effort, or concurrency with the state version it read (UpdateHvReviewerCommand); a change to the strategy, agent path, model, or effort makes the reviewer `Unverified`, and the worker NONCEs it (UC-HV-02). Alternates: a stale state version is refused with 409 `conflict` and the operator reads again; an unknown reviewer is 404; an invalid field is 400; the audit ledger is unavailable and nothing changes (503). Postconditions: the change is stored, audited, and announced (`reviewer_unverified` when the launch changed); a disabled reviewer gets no new assignment, and the requests it held are reassigned at their next claim. Invariants: I-10; no change applies without its ledger rows.\n2098: \n2099: ```mermaid\n2100: flowchart LR\n2101:     OP([\"Operator\"]) --- U((\"Manage the reviewer pool\"))\n2102:     U -. include .-> I1((\"List and read reviewers\"))\n2103:     U -. include .-> I2((\"Update with the state version (UpdateHvReviewerCommand)\"))\n2104:     E1((\"Launch changed: Unverified, then NONCE\")) -. extend .-> U\n2105:     E2((\"Stale state version: 409 conflict\")) -. extend .-> U\n2106:     E3((\"Audit ledger unavailable: 503\")) -. extend .-> U\n2107: ```\n2108: \n2109: ### 18.3 UC-HV-02 NONCE a reviewer [FR-MCP-HVPIPE-003]\n2110: \n2111: Actors: operator or any agent, HV worker, reviewer agent. Trigger: a reviewer is `Unverified` (startup or a launch change, requested by the worker) or `Offline` after its cause was fixed (requested by a caller, S-15). Preconditions: the reviewer is enabled. Main flow: the caller requests a NONCE (StartHvReviewerNonceCommand); the worker claims the probe (ClaimHvRunCommand), launches the reviewer with a probe brief carrying a fresh nonce (RunReviewerProcess), streams its output (AppendHvRunOutputCommand), appends the adapter's provenance, and closes the run (CloseHvRunOutputCommand); policy ReadinessProbeVerdict passes: the nonce is echoed, the provenance shows the expected model and effort, and the reviewer logged its own turn; the reviewer becomes `Online` with its resolved model and effort. Alternates: a probe already requested or running is reported without a second probe; a disabled reviewer is refused with 409 `hv_reviewer_disabled`; the probe fails (wrong nonce, wrong or missing provenance, no reviewer turn, launch failure, nonzero exit) and the reviewer stays or becomes `Offline` with an incident filed through triage (UC-HV-09); the worker dies during the probe and the sweep requests it again. Postconditions: the reviewer's readiness reflects a probe of this moment (S-27); `reviewer_online` or `reviewer_offline` is announced. Invariants: only a passing NONCE moves a reviewer to `Online` (R-10).\n2112: \n2113: ```mermaid\n2114: flowchart LR\n2115:     OP([\"Operator or agent\"]) --- U((\"NONCE a reviewer\"))\n2116:     WK([\"HV worker\"]) --- U\n2117:     RV([\"Reviewer agent\"]) --- U\n2118:     U -. include .-> I1((\"Probe run with a fresh nonce (RunReviewerProcess)\"))\n2119:     U -. include .-> I2((\"Decide (ReadinessProbeVerdict)\"))\n2120:     E1((\"Already requested or running: no second probe\")) -. extend .-> U\n2121:     E2((\"Disabled reviewer: 409\")) -. extend .-> U\n2122:     E3((\"Probe failed: Offline, incident filed\")) -. extend .-> U\n2123:     E4((\"Worker died: probe requested again\")) -. extend .-> U\n2124: ```\n2125: \n2126: ### 18.4 UC-HV-03 Submit an HV request [FR-MCP-HVPIPE-002, -004, -005, -006, -013, -018]\n2127: \n2128: Actors: model (through its plugin) or operator (through Director), any client, server. Trigger: a caller wants a turn, an inclusive range of turns, or a whole session reviewed (S-03, S-11). Preconditions: the turns to review are terminal; for an agent caller, its own turn is bound by the plugin (BindVerbToTurn). Main flow: the caller submits the scope, optional context in Markdown or YAML, and an idempotency key (SubmitHvRequestCommand); the server resolves the requirement references of the context (RequirementReferenceExtractor), resolves the members (HvScopeResolution: the session's turns at admission time for a session scope, without the submitting turn), checks that every member is terminal, not under review, and never reviewed (HvAdmissionEligibility), picks the next eligible reviewer round-robin, never the submitter, the author of the reviewed session, or an alias of either (RoundRobinAssignment, HvReviewerEligibility), snapshots every member without its review records (TurnSnapshotBuilder), stores the complete accepted request compressed (GzipCodec), freezes the members (HvTurnFreeze), announces `hv_queued`, and wakes the worker (auto-start, S-24). Alternates: the same key and inputs return the stored request; the key with other inputs is a conflict; a malformed scope, a scope over the limit, a scope naming the submitting turn, or an empty session scope is refused (400); turns that are not terminal, under review, or already reviewed are refused with every affected turn listed (409); no reviewer is eligible and the request is refused with every reviewer's status, and the plugin adds the reviewers' open incidents and the NONCE remedy (409, S-16); a turn whose class is `Chore` and whose hostile review is `Unnecessary` is admitted and graded like any other (S-09); a turn has no self-review, or any self-review grade or status, and admission is the same (S-28); the audit ledger is unavailable and nothing is written (503, S-29). Postconditions: one `Queued` request with its members frozen `Pending`, its accepted request stored, and its reviewer assigned. Invariants: I-01, I-07, I-08, I-10.\n2129: \n2130: ```mermaid\n2131: flowchart LR\n2132:     MD([\"Model, through its plugin\"]) --- U((\"Submit an HV request\"))\n2133:     OP([\"Operator, through Director\"]) --- U\n2134:     U -. include .-> I1((\"Resolve members (HvScopeResolution)\"))\n2135:     U -. include .-> I2((\"Check eligibility (HvAdmissionEligibility)\"))\n2136:     U -. include .-> I3((\"Assign round-robin, submitter and author excluded (RoundRobinAssignment)\"))\n2137:     U -. include .-> I4((\"Store the accepted request and freeze the turns\"))\n2138:     E1((\"Same key and inputs: stored request\")) -. extend .-> U\n2139:     E2((\"Bad, oversized, self-including, or empty scope: 400\")) -. extend .-> U\n2140:     E3((\"Not terminal, pending, or reviewed: 409 listing every turn\")) -. extend .-> U\n2141:     E4((\"No eligible reviewer: 409 with reviewer context\")) -. extend .-> U\n2142:     E5((\"Unnecessary turn: included and graded\")) -. extend .-> U\n2143:     E6((\"Self-review absent or any grade: same admission\")) -. extend .-> U\n2144:     E7((\"Audit ledger unavailable: 503, nothing written\")) -. extend .-> U\n2145: ```\n2146: \n2147: ### 18.5 UC-HV-04 Run a review live [FR-MCP-HVPIPE-007, -008]\n2148: \n2149: Actors: HV worker, reviewer agent, server. Trigger: a `Queued` request whose reviewer is eligible and has capacity. Preconditions: UC-HV-03 completed. Main flow: the worker claims the request with a lease and a fence (ClaimHvRunCommand); it launches the reviewer with the brief (RunReviewerProcess) and records the brief as the log's first record; every line the reviewer writes is appended within the flush interval (AppendHvRunOutputCommand) and is visible on the output stream while the reviewer runs (S-22); progress records set the request's progress and ETA (R-18); heartbeats renew the lease (RecordHvRunHeartbeatCommand); the reviewer reviews each turn and the whole set, logs its own `Chore` turn holding its result, and emits its verdict record last; on exit with code 0 the worker appends the provenance and closes the output (CloseHvRunOutputCommand), and the request becomes `Finalizing`. Alternates: the assignee is no longer eligible and the claim reassigns round-robin; a cancel arrives and the worker stops the reviewer (UC-HV-08); the reviewer fails to start or exits nonzero (UC-HV-09); the worker loses its lease and its writes are refused as stale, so it stops (UC-HV-09); no reviewer is eligible and the request waits `Queued` with an unknown ETA; the reviewer runs for any length of time without a timeout (P-02). Postconditions: the attempt's complete log is stored, compressed, contiguous, and hashed. Invariants: I-05, I-06.\n2150: \nEXIT_CODE=0\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
