{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_68","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/pwsh -NoProfile -Command \"pwsh.exe -NoProfile -NonInteractive -File './docs/receipts/hv/hv-r1-inspect.ps1' -Task Read -Path './docs/architecture/SessionTurn-Review-AgentContext-Architecture-Amendment-1-Durable-HV.md' -Start 2151 -Count 170\"","aggregated_output":"SOURCE ./docs/architecture/SessionTurn-Review-AgentContext-Architecture-Amendment-1-Durable-HV.md totalLines=2785\n2151: ```mermaid\n2152: flowchart LR\n2153:     WK([\"HV worker\"]) --- U((\"Run a review live\"))\n2154:     RV([\"Reviewer agent\"]) --- U\n2155:     U -. include .-> I1((\"Claim with lease and fence (ClaimHvRunCommand)\"))\n2156:     U -. include .-> I2((\"Stream every line as it is written (AppendHvRunOutputCommand)\"))\n2157:     U -. include .-> I3((\"Heartbeat (RecordHvRunHeartbeatCommand)\"))\n2158:     U -. include .-> I4((\"Close the output (CloseHvRunOutputCommand)\"))\n2159:     E1((\"Assignee ineligible: reassigned at claim\")) -. extend .-> U\n2160:     E2((\"Cancel: reviewer stopped\")) -. extend .-> U\n2161:     E3((\"Launch failure or nonzero exit: UC-HV-09\")) -. extend .-> U\n2162:     E4((\"Lease lost: stale fence, worker stops\")) -. extend .-> U\n2163:     E5((\"No eligible reviewer: waits Queued, ETA unknown\")) -. extend .-> U\n2164: ```\n2165: \n2166: ### 18.6 UC-HV-05 Finalize the HV result [FR-MCP-HVPIPE-010, -011, -012, -014, -021]\n2167: \n2168: Actors: HV worker, server. Trigger: a request is `Finalizing` (after UC-HV-04, or found by the sweep after a crash). Main flow: the server reads the attempt's log and verifies it (HvFinalVerification: integrity, completeness, binding to the request and to each turn's admission snapshot, verdict consistency at 98/98, reviewer independence, the reviewer's own turn, and runtime identity); then, in one transaction (S-23), it stores the per-turn assessments, the holistic evaluation, and the delineated failures with their remediation, writes each turn's hostile review through HvVerdictMapping, makes every member turn final, grades the linked agent responses and decides their trust when agent context is on, stores the result document compressed, completes the request, and announces `hv_completed`. Alternates: a verification step fails, the attempt fails with that code (UC-HV-09), and the request is queued again or fails when its attempts are spent; the store changed since the reads and the transaction runs again from the reads; the audit ledger is unavailable or the transaction keeps conflicting and the request stays `Finalizing` for the sweep; the request was already finalized and the stored outcome returns; agent context is `Off` and the linked responses are recorded `NotGraded`. Postconditions: either every part of the result is committed or none is (I-04); the TODOs the turns name are unchanged (S-25); the self-review records were never read (S-28). Invariants: I-02, I-03, I-04, I-09.\n2169: \n2170: ```mermaid\n2171: flowchart LR\n2172:     WK([\"HV worker\"]) --- U((\"Finalize the HV result\"))\n2173:     U -. include .-> I1((\"Verify V-1 to V-8 (HvFinalVerification)\"))\n2174:     U -. include .-> I2((\"Commit everything at once (CommitFinalResult)\"))\n2175:     U -. include .-> I3((\"Hostile review per turn (HvVerdictMapping)\"))\n2176:     E1((\"Verification failed: attempt fails, request requeued or failed\")) -. extend .-> U\n2177:     E2((\"State changed: transaction runs again\")) -. extend .-> U\n2178:     E3((\"Audit unavailable: stays Finalizing for the sweep\")) -. extend .-> U\n2179:     E4((\"Already finalized: stored outcome\")) -. extend .-> U\n2180:     E5((\"Agent context Off: responses NotGraded\")) -. extend .-> U\n2181: ```\n2182: \n2183: ### 18.7 UC-HV-06 Watch an HV live [FR-MCP-HVPIPE-015, -016]\n2184: \n2185: Actors: any client (Director `hv-output`, the REPL, a REST client). Trigger: a caller wants to see a running HV (S-18). Main flow: the caller lists running HVs (QueryHvRequestsQuery with `status` `Running`), reads one with its progress, ETA, and last 20 lines (GetHvRequestQuery), and attaches to its output stream (StreamHvRunOutputQuery), which replays the stored chunks and then sends each new chunk as it is appended; the stream ends after the request reaches a terminal state. Alternates: the connection drops and the caller reconnects with its last event id, receiving exactly the events it missed (OrderedEventReplay); the reviewer reports no progress and the ETA is `Unknown` (R-18); a new attempt starts and the stream continues with the new run's events; the audit ledger is unavailable and the attach is refused (503, evidence access is audited). Postconditions: the caller saw every output line in order. Invariants: I-06.\n2186: \n2187: ```mermaid\n2188: flowchart LR\n2189:     CL([\"Any client\"]) --- U((\"Watch an HV live\"))\n2190:     U -. include .-> I1((\"List running HVs (QueryHvRequestsQuery)\"))\n2191:     U -. include .-> I2((\"Progress, ETA, last output (GetHvRequestQuery)\"))\n2192:     U -. include .-> I3((\"Attach to the output stream (StreamHvRunOutputQuery)\"))\n2193:     E1((\"Dropped: reconnect with Last-Event-ID\")) -. extend .-> U\n2194:     E2((\"No progress reported: ETA Unknown\")) -. extend .-> U\n2195:     E3((\"New attempt: stream continues\")) -. extend .-> U\n2196: ```\n2197: \n2198: ### 18.8 UC-HV-07 Receive completion notifications [FR-MCP-HVPIPE-017, -020]\n2199: \n2200: Actors: the plugin's watcher and the model, Director, any client. Trigger: an HV completes, fails, or is canceled (S-19). Main flow: the plugin's watcher follows the notification stream from its last sequence (WatchHvNotifications, StreamHvNotificationsQuery); a terminal notification for a request its host session submitted goes to the host session's inbox; at the next prompt the plugin adds it to the model's context once, with the overall verdict and how to read the result. Alternates: the stream drops and the watcher reconnects from its recorded sequence, missing nothing; the server restarts and the outbox rows are still there; a client without streams polls (QueryHvNotificationsQuery); a notification arrives twice (at least once) and the sequence deduplicates it. Postconditions: every terminal outcome of a request the host session submitted reaches that session's model exactly once. Invariants: I-12.\n2201: \n2202: ```mermaid\n2203: flowchart LR\n2204:     PL([\"Plugin watcher and model\"]) --- U((\"Receive completion notifications\"))\n2205:     CL([\"Director or any client\"]) --- U\n2206:     U -. include .-> I1((\"Follow the stream from the last sequence (StreamHvNotificationsQuery)\"))\n2207:     U -. include .-> I2((\"Inbox and deliver at the next prompt (WatchHvNotifications)\"))\n2208:     E1((\"Dropped: reconnect from the recorded sequence\")) -. extend .-> U\n2209:     E2((\"No streams: poll (QueryHvNotificationsQuery)\")) -. extend .-> U\n2210:     E3((\"Delivered twice: deduplicated by sequence\")) -. extend .-> U\n2211: ```\n2212: \n2213: ### 18.9 UC-HV-08 Cancel an HV [FR-MCP-HVPIPE-008]\n2214: \n2215: Actors: any caller (S-18, no roles). Main flow: the caller cancels (CancelHvRequestCommand); a `Queued` request is canceled at once and its turns released; a `Running` request becomes `CancelRequested`, the worker reads it at its next heartbeat, stops the reviewer, and the request becomes `Canceled` with its turns released. Alternates: the request is already `CancelRequested` or `Canceled` and nothing changes; it is `Finalizing`, `Completed`, or `Failed` and the cancel is refused (409); the worker died and the lease expiry completes the cancel (ExpireHvRunLeasesCommand). Postconditions: a canceled request's turns are writable again; nothing of an unfinished review is recorded on them. Invariants: I-04.\n2216: \n2217: ```mermaid\n2218: flowchart LR\n2219:     CL([\"Any caller\"]) --- U((\"Cancel an HV\"))\n2220:     U -. include .-> I1((\"Cancel (CancelHvRequestCommand)\"))\n2221:     E1((\"Running: worker stops the reviewer at its heartbeat\")) -. extend .-> U\n2222:     E2((\"Already canceled: unchanged\")) -. extend .-> U\n2223:     E3((\"Finalizing or terminal: 409\")) -. extend .-> U\n2224:     E4((\"Worker dead: lease expiry completes the cancel\")) -. extend .-> U\n2225: ```\n2226: \n2227: ### 18.10 UC-HV-09 Recover from failures [FR-MCP-HVPIPE-007, -009]\n2228: \n2229: Actors: HV worker, triage, server. Trigger: an execution failure (launch failure, nonzero exit, invalid output, failed verification, missing reviewer turn, runtime identity mismatch) or a dead worker. Main flow: the failure is recorded on the attempt (FailHvRunCommand); a failure attributable to the reviewer marks it `Offline` until a NONCE passes (S-15); an incident is recorded and filed through the triage endpoint with a deduplication key (FileHvIncidentCommand, S-26); the request returns to `Queued` and the next claim assigns the next eligible reviewer. Alternates: attempts are spent and the request fails, releasing its turns; triage is unreachable and the filing is retried at each sweep; a worker died and its expired leases are swept (ExpireHvRunLeasesCommand), its runs abandoned and fenced out; a graceful shutdown ends runs with `worker_shutdown`, which is not counted as an attempt; the audit ledger is unavailable and the failed run cannot be recorded until it returns, after which the lease expiry recovers it. Postconditions: no failure is silent, no incident group is duplicated, and no reviewer is used again before it proves itself. Invariants: I-05.\n2230: \n2231: ```mermaid\n2232: flowchart LR\n2233:     WK([\"HV worker\"]) --- U((\"Recover from failures\"))\n2234:     TG([\"Triage\"]) --- U\n2235:     U -. include .-> I1((\"Record the failure (FailHvRunCommand)\"))\n2236:     U -. include .-> I2((\"File the incident (FileHvIncidentCommand)\"))\n2237:     U -. include .-> I3((\"Requeue and reassign (HvRetryDecision, RoundRobinAssignment)\"))\n2238:     E1((\"Attempts spent: request Failed, turns released\")) -. extend .-> U\n2239:     E2((\"Triage unreachable: filing retried\")) -. extend .-> U\n2240:     E3((\"Dead worker: leases swept, runs fenced out\")) -. extend .-> U\n2241:     E4((\"Graceful shutdown: not counted\")) -. extend .-> U\n2242: ```\n2243: \n2244: ### 18.11 UC-HV-10 Retrieve the result and evidence [FR-MCP-HVPIPE-011, -015]\n2245: \n2246: Actors: any client. Main flow: the caller reads the standard result document (GetHvResultQuery: the complete accepted request, the complete response log, every turn with its score, the holistic evaluation, the delineated failures with remediation, the overall verdict, and the evidence hashes, S-13, S-21) or downloads one evidence item compressed or decompressed (GetHvEvidenceQuery); every read is audited. Alternates: the result is not ready (409); the evidence was removed (410, with the hashes and sizes kept); the audit ledger is unavailable (503). Postconditions: the bytes returned decompress to exactly the bytes stored at admission and during the run. Invariants: I-06, I-11.\n2247: \n2248: ```mermaid\n2249: flowchart LR\n2250:     CL([\"Any client\"]) --- U((\"Retrieve the result and evidence\"))\n2251:     U -. include .-> I1((\"Result document (GetHvResultQuery)\"))\n2252:     U -. include .-> I2((\"Evidence download (GetHvEvidenceQuery)\"))\n2253:     U -. include .-> I3((\"Audit every read (AuditLedgerGuard)\"))\n2254:     E1((\"Not ready: 409\")) -. extend .-> U\n2255:     E2((\"Removed: 410 with hashes\")) -. extend .-> U\n2256:     E3((\"Audit unavailable: 503\")) -. extend .-> U\n2257: ```\n2258: \n2259: ### 18.12 UC-HV-11 Remove evidence on instruction [FR-MCP-HVPIPE-019]\n2260: \n2261: Actors: operator (S-29: \"Retain until told to remove.\"). Main flow: the operator removes a terminal request's evidence with a reason and a name (RemoveHvEvidenceCommand); the evidence and chunk bytes are removed, while the result rows, findings, turn reviews, hashes, and sizes stay; the removal is audited. Alternates: the request is still active (409); the evidence was already removed and nothing changes. Postconditions: nothing else ever removes evidence (I-11). Invariants: I-10, I-11.\n2262: \n2263: ```mermaid\n2264: flowchart LR\n2265:     OP([\"Operator\"]) --- U((\"Remove evidence on instruction\"))\n2266:     U -. include .-> I1((\"Remove with reason and name (RemoveHvEvidenceCommand)\"))\n2267:     E1((\"Request active: 409\")) -. extend .-> U\n2268:     E2((\"Already removed: unchanged\")) -. extend .-> U\n2269: ```\n2270: \n2271: ### 18.13 UC-HV-12 Remediate after a reviewed turn [FR-MCP-HVPIPE-012, -014]\n2272: \n2273: Actors: model. Trigger: an HV found failures in reviewed turns. Main flow: the model reads the result's failures and their remediation (UC-HV-10), does the corrective work in a later turn, and requests a new HV for the new turns (UC-HV-03) (S-06). Alternates: the model tries to change a reviewed turn and every write is refused with 409 `turn_immutable` (HvTurnFreeze); it tries to write a hostile review itself and is refused with 403 `review_hostile_pipeline_only`; it tries to submit the reviewed turns again and is refused with 409 `hv_turns_already_reviewed` (S-20); an AGREE verdict never moves a TODO, so the coordinator decides completion (S-25). Postconditions: the reviewed history is unchanged; the remediation is new work with its own HV. Invariants: I-01, I-09.\n2274: \n2275: ```mermaid\n2276: flowchart LR\n2277:     MD([\"Model\"]) --- U((\"Remediate after a reviewed turn\"))\n2278:     U -. include .-> I1((\"Read the failures and remediation\"))\n2279:     U -. include .-> I2((\"New turns, new HV request\"))\n2280:     E1((\"Write to a reviewed turn: 409 turn_immutable\")) -. extend .-> U\n2281:     E2((\"Own hostile review: 403\")) -. extend .-> U\n2282:     E3((\"Same turns again: 409 already reviewed\")) -. extend .-> U\n2283:     E4((\"AGREE: TODO unchanged, coordinator decides\")) -. extend .-> U\n2284: ```\n2285: \n2286: ## 19. Requirements, acceptance criteria, and traceability (proposed)\n2287: \n2288: Every identifier here is proposed, and the requirement records exist: the requirement store answered `not_found` for all 63 of `FR-MCP-HVPIPE-001` to `-021`, `TR-MCP-HVPIPE-001` to `-021`, and `TEST-MCP-HVPIPE-001` to `-021` at 2026-10-16T14:50:04 local and again in the pre-check of 2026-10-16T16:32:30 local, and the records and the 21 mapping edges below were then created through the plugin's requirements workflow (`createFrBatch`, `createTrBatch`, `createTestBatch`, `createMapping`), each with status `pending` and every acceptance criterion not satisfied, and read back with 0 mismatches. The plugin's requirements skill directs exactly that: \"Capture requirements as they emerge; do not defer to end of session.\" H0 updates them to the text the hostile validation and the operator's approval settle. Each FR has one TR (`TR-MCP-HVPIPE-<same number>`, the implementation contract: the units, components, and entities named in its line) and one TEST (`TEST-MCP-HVPIPE-<same number>`, the named test cases of its acceptance criteria); the one-to-one numbering is a naming convenience, not a rule, and the mapping edges are explicit below. Acceptance criteria use Given, When, Then; each names the test that proves it, in PascalCase without underscores (CA1707), in the test class named after the unit or component (foundation section 3.5). Cases that need three storage providers run in G3 (`MigrationIntegrationTests` cases), the rest in G2, and the plugin cases in Pester (G4).\n2289: \n2290: ### 19.1 Catalog\n2291: \n2292: Problem domains (the foundation's rule of 2026-10-13, \"Dividing the new reqs into problem domains would be best split.\"; each domain owns its requirements, their acceptance criteria, and their mappings): reviewer pool and readiness (FR-001 to FR-003), admission (FR-004 to FR-006, FR-013), scheduling and execution (FR-007 to FR-009), evidence and finalization (FR-010 to FR-012, FR-021), outcomes (FR-014, FR-015), observability (FR-016, FR-017), audit and retention (FR-018, FR-019), and surfaces (FR-020). The domains follow the bounded contexts of section 20.1.\n2293: \n2294: - FR-MCP-HVPIPE-001 Reviewer pool configuration and real-time management. Sources S-02, R-08. UC-HV-01. TR-MCP-HVPIPE-001: HostileValidationOptions, HvReviewer, ListHvReviewersQuery, GetHvReviewerQuery, UpdateHvReviewerCommand, IHvReviewerAdapter.\n2295:   - AC001 Given options missing one of the five reviewers, naming an unknown or duplicate reviewer, an unknown strategy, or an enabled Copilot reviewer without a configured model (section 10), when the server starts, then startup fails naming the entry (`HostileValidationOptionsMissingUnknownOrDuplicateReviewerFailsStartup`).\n2296:   - AC002 Given a fresh workspace, when the server starts, then five `HvReviewer` rows exist `Unverified`, and a second start does not overwrite a row changed through the API (`ReviewerSeedingInsertsFiveOnceNeverOverwrites`).\n2297:   - AC003 Given a reviewer with no configured effort, and a reviewer other than Copilot with no configured model, when its launch is built, then the effort is the highest its CLI accepts (Codex `max`, Claude `max`, Cline `xhigh`, Grok `xhigh`, Copilot `max`; VI-08), never a lower or a refused value, and the model is the CLI default recorded from provenance (`ReviewerAdapterDefaultsToHighestEffortAndCliDefaultModel`).\n2298:   - AC004 Given an update with a stale `expectedStateVersion`, when it is applied, then 409 `conflict` with `retryable: false` and `details.field` `expectedStateVersion` and nothing changes (`UpdateReviewerStaleStateVersion409NothingChanged`).\n2299:   - AC005 Given an update that changes the strategy, agent path, model, or effort, when it commits, then the reviewer is `Unverified` with reason `configuration_changed` and `reviewer_unverified` is appended (`UpdateReviewerLaunchChangeMakesUnverifiedAndNotifies`).\n2300:   - AC006 Given the REST, MCP, client, REPL, and Director surfaces, when each lists, gets, and updates a reviewer, then each returns the same record and the same error codes (`ReviewerSurfacesParityGoldenContract`).\n2301: - FR-MCP-HVPIPE-002 Identity normalization, submitter and author exclusion, and round-robin assignment. Sources S-17, S-28, P-01, P-07, R-07, R-08. UC-HV-03, UC-HV-04. TR: AgentIdentity, HvReviewerEligibility, RoundRobinAssignment, HvWorkspaceState.\n2302:   - AC001 Given each alias of the alias table in any case and with any separators, when normalized, then it maps to its reviewer id, in C# and in PowerShell from one golden contract (`AgentIdentityGoldenContractTests`, C# and Pester).\n2303:   - AC002 Given a submitting turn whose agent is `ClaudeCode` (or `ClaudeCowork`, `claude-code`, `cowork`), when a request is admitted, then Claude is never assigned, and V-5 refuses a run whose reviewer is Claude (`SubmitterAliasesNeverAssignedClaudeFamily`, `FinalVerificationSubmitterReviewerRefusedNotIndependent`).\n2304:   - AC003 Given a free-text submitter name that differs from the submitting turn's agent, when a request is admitted, then exclusion uses the turn's agent (`SubmitterExclusionUsesTurnAgentNeverFreeText`).\n2305:   - AC004 Given the cursor at Copilot, every reviewer enabled and `Online`, and three requests that Cline submits over Cline sessions (so only Cline is excluded), when they are admitted one after another, then Claude, Codex, and Grok are assigned and the cursor ends at Grok (`RoundRobinAssignsInPoolOrderAfterCursor`).\n2306:   - AC005 Given the server restarts between two submissions, when the second is admitted, then it takes the reviewer after the cursor stored before the restart (`RoundRobinCursorSurvivesRestart`).\n2307:   - AC006 Given two concurrent submissions, when both commit, then they take the next two eligible reviewers in cyclic order, never the same cursor value, on SQLite, PostgreSQL, and SQL Server (`RoundRobinConcurrentSubmissionsConsecutiveReviewersThreeProviders`).\n2308:   - AC007 Given the assignee becomes `Offline` before the claim, when the request is claimed, then it is reassigned to the next eligible reviewer and the reassignment is recorded (`ClaimReassignsWhenAssigneeNoLongerEligible`).\n2309:   - AC008 Given a request over a Grok session submitted by Claude, and another submitted by an `Operator`, when each is admitted and claimed, then Grok is never assigned to either, `AuthorReviewerId` is `Grok`, and V-5 refuses a run whose reviewer is Grok with `reviewer_not_independent` (`AuthorAgentNeverAssignedAndRefusedByVerification`).\n2310: - FR-MCP-HVPIPE-003 Reviewer readiness: NONCE, offline, and online. Sources S-15, S-27, P-04, R-10, R-24. UC-HV-02. TR: StartHvReviewerNonceCommand, ClaimHvRunCommand (probe), CloseHvRunOutputCommand, ReadinessProbeVerdict.\n2311:   - AC001 Given an `Offline` reviewer, when nothing but an execution or a configuration change happens, then it never becomes `Online`; only a passing probe makes it `Online` (`ReviewerBecomesOnlineOnlyByPassingProbe`).\n2312:   - AC002 Given a probe whose log echoes the run's nonce, whose provenance names the expected model and effort, and whose reviewer turn exists, when it closes, then the reviewer is `Online` with the resolved model and effort and `reviewer_online` is appended (`ProbePassedReviewerOnlineResolvedModelAndEffort`).\n2313:   - AC003 Given a probe with a wrong nonce, missing or different provenance, or no reviewer turn, when it closes, then the reviewer is `Offline` with `probe_nonce_mismatch`, `runtime_identity_mismatch`, or `reviewer_turn_logging_unsupported` and an incident is `Pending` (`ProbeFailuresOfflineWithCodeAndIncident`).\n2314:   - AC004 Given a probe already requested or running, when another NONCE is requested, then 202 `AlreadyRequested` or `Running` and no second probe exists (`NonceRepeatNoSecondProbe`).\n2315:   - AC005 Given a disabled reviewer, when a NONCE is requested, then 409 `hv_reviewer_disabled` (`NonceDisabledReviewer409`).\n2316:   - AC006 Given enabled `Unverified` reviewers at startup, when the worker starts, then a probe is requested for each and none for a disabled or `Offline` reviewer (`WorkerStartupProbesUnverifiedEnabledReviewersOnly`).\n2317: - FR-MCP-HVPIPE-004 Submission scopes and snapshot membership. Sources S-03, S-09, S-11, R-05, R-26. UC-HV-03. TR: SubmitHvRequestCommand, HvScopeResolution, TurnSnapshotBuilder, HvRequestTurn.\n2318:   - AC001 Given a turn scope, a range scope, and a session scope, when each is admitted, then the members are that turn, every turn from start to end inclusive in session order, and every turn of the session at admission (`ScopeResolutionTurnRangeAndSessionMembers`).\n2319:   - AC002 Given a session scope submitted from a turn of that session, when admitted, then the submitting turn is not a member and `excludedSubmittingTurn` is true; given a turn or range scope that contains the submitting turn, then 400 `hv_scope_includes_submitting_turn` (`ScopeResolutionSubmittingTurnExcludedOrRefused`).\n2320:   - AC003 Given a session with `MaxTurnsPerRequest` plus one turns, when a session scope is submitted, then 400 `hv_scope_too_large` with the count and no request exists (`ScopeResolutionOverMaxRefusedNeverTruncated`).\nEXIT_CODE=0\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
