{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_70","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/pwsh -NoProfile -Command \"pwsh.exe -NoProfile -NonInteractive -File './docs/receipts/hv/hv-r1-inspect.ps1' -Task Read -Path './docs/architecture/SessionTurn-Review-AgentContext-Architecture-Amendment-1-Durable-HV.md' -Start 2321 -Count 143\"","aggregated_output":"SOURCE ./docs/architecture/SessionTurn-Review-AgentContext-Architecture-Amendment-1-Durable-HV.md totalLines=2785\n2321:   - AC004 Given a turn added to the session after admission, when the request finalizes, then the turn is not a member (`SessionScopeSnapshotAtAdmissionLaterTurnNotMember`).\n2322:   - AC005 Given a member turn with class `Chore` and hostile review `Unnecessary`, when the request finalizes, then the turn has an assessment and its hostile review holds the HV result (`UnnecessaryTurnIncludedAssessedAndReviewed`).\n2323:   - AC006 Given a range whose start is after its end, an endpoint outside the session, or an unknown session, when submitted, then 400 `hv_scope_invalid` naming the field (`ScopeResolutionInvalidRangeOrSession400`).\n2324: - FR-MCP-HVPIPE-005 Admission eligibility and refusal with context. Sources S-16, S-20, R-05, R-27. UC-HV-03, UC-HV-12. TR: HvAdmissionEligibility, RoundRobinAssignment, SubmitHvFromPlugin.\n2325:   - AC001 Given members that are not terminal, under review, and already reviewed, when submitted, then 409 with the first code of that order and `details` listing every affected turn of every kind (`AdmissionRefusalListsEveryAffectedTurn`).\n2326:   - AC002 Given two concurrent submissions over overlapping turns, when both run, then exactly one is admitted and the other is refused `hv_turns_pending`, on three providers (`AdmissionConcurrentOverlapOneWinsThreeProviders`).\n2327:   - AC003 Given no eligible reviewer, when submitted, then 409 `hv_no_reviewer_available` with every reviewer's enabled flag, readiness, reason, and open incident, and no request exists (`AdmissionNoEligibleReviewer409WithReviewerContext`).\n2328:   - AC004 Given that refusal through the plugin verb, when the model receives it, then the report carries the reviewer statuses, the open incidents, and the NONCE remedy text (`HvSubmitVerbNoReviewerAddsContext`, Pester).\n2329:   - AC005 Given the same idempotency key and inputs, when submitted twice, then the second returns 200 with the stored request; with other inputs, 409 `conflict` with `retryable: false` (`SubmitIdempotencyKeyReplayAndReuse`).\n2330:   - AC006 Given any submission surface, when a caller asks to re-review, then no force or re-review parameter exists in any request shape (`SubmitRequestShapeHasNoForceFlag`).\n2331: - FR-MCP-HVPIPE-006 Request context and requirement references. Sources S-14, R-23. UC-HV-03. TR: RequirementReferenceExtractor, HvRequestRequirementRef.\n2332:   - AC001 Given a Markdown or YAML context naming FR, TR, and TEST ids, acceptance-criterion forms, and a use case, when admitted, then each reference is stored in order of first appearance without duplicates, resolved against the effective requirements and use cases, and listed in the brief (`RequirementReferenceExtractorFindsResolvesAndOrders`).\n2333:   - AC002 Given a reference that resolves to nothing, when admitted, then it is listed unresolved and the request is admitted (`RequirementReferenceUnresolvedListedNeverRefused`).\n2334:   - AC003 Given a context over 65536 characters or an unknown format, when submitted, then 400 `validation_error` naming the field (`SubmitContextTooLongOrUnknownFormat400`).\n2335:   - AC004 Given a context holding a secret, when the brief is built, then the secret is redacted in the brief and the stored context is returned redacted on every read surface (`ContextSecretRedactedInBriefAndReads`).\n2336: - FR-MCP-HVPIPE-007 Durable scheduling: queue, leases, fences, and restart safety. Sources S-17, S-24, handoff requirement 10, R-07, R-13. UC-HV-04, UC-HV-09. TR: ClaimHvRunCommand, RecordHvRunHeartbeatCommand, ExpireHvRunLeasesCommand, FencedLease, HvRetryDecision, HvWorkerHost.\n2337:   - AC001 Given a submission, when it commits, then the worker is woken and claims it without a manual trigger, and when the wake-up is lost (a crash after the commit, W-01) the next poll claims it (`SubmitWakesWorkerAutoStart`).\n2338:   - AC002 Given two workers claiming at once, when both run, then exactly one run is claimed per request, on three providers (W-11, `ClaimConcurrentWorkersOneRunPerRequestThreeProviders`).\n2339:   - AC003 Given a run whose lease expired before its process started, while it ran, or after its process exited but before its close committed (W-02, W-03, W-04), when the sweep runs, then the run is `Abandoned`, its fence token is incremented, its output stays stored as evidence (L-02), and the request is `Queued` with attempts left; on its last counted attempt it is `Failed`, and with a cancel requested it is `Canceled`, each ended request with its turns `None`, its `Pending` responses `Closed` with `request_ended`, and `hv_failed` or `hv_canceled` appended, exactly as after FailHvRunCommand (`LeaseExpiryAbandonsFencesAndRequeues`, `LeaseExpiryEndsRequestLikeFailedRun`).\n2340:   - AC004 Given a worker whose lease was taken over, when it appends, heartbeats, closes, or fails, then each answers `stale_fence` and nothing changes (`StaleFenceEveryWorkerWriteRefusedNothingChanged`).\n2341:   - AC005 Given a request `Finalizing` when the server restarted (W-05), when the sweep runs, then FinalizeHvRequestCommand finalizes it once (`SweepFinalizesFinalizingRequestOnce`).\n2342:   - AC006 Given a graceful shutdown during a run, when the worker stops, then the run ends `worker_shutdown`, no incident exists, the reviewer is unchanged, and the attempt is not counted (`GracefulShutdownNotCountedNoIncident`).\n2343:   - AC007 Given two registered workspaces, each with queued requests, when each workspace's worker claims, then no run or request crosses workspaces (`WorkerClaimsOnlyItsWorkspace`).\n2344: - FR-MCP-HVPIPE-008 Execution lifecycle: true live output, heartbeats, no time limit, cancellation. Sources S-18, S-22, P-02, R-11, R-12, R-28. UC-HV-04, UC-HV-08. TR: RunReviewerProcess, StreamReviewerOutput, IHvReviewerAdapter live lines and launch barrier, AppendHvRunOutputCommand, CancelHvRequestCommand.\n2345:   - AC001 Given a reviewer that writes lines over time, when it runs, then every line is appended within `OutputFlushInterval` of being written, in order (`OutputLinesAppendedWithinFlushIntervalInOrder`).\n2346:   - AC002 Given a buffer reaching `OutputFlushBytes`, when the next line arrives, then the buffer is appended at once (`OutputFlushedAtByteThreshold`).\n2347:   - AC003 Given a scripted fake reviewer that writes one line and then blocks on a gate the test controls, when the test reads the run's output stream, then the line arrives while the gate is closed and the process is still running (operator-confirmed P8, `LiveOutputLineObservableBeforeReviewerExits`).\n2348:   - AC004 Given a reviewer running longer than any interval the configuration names, when nothing else happens, then no unit or process ends it (`ReviewerRunHasNoTimeLimit`).\n2349:   - AC005 Given a `Queued` request, when canceled, then it is `Canceled`, its turns are `None`, and `hv_canceled` is appended; given a `Running` request, then it becomes `CancelRequested`, and at the next heartbeat the process is stopped and the request is `Canceled` (`CancelQueuedImmediateRunningAtNextHeartbeat`).\n2350:   - AC006 Given a cancel racing a finalization, a claim, or a close of one request (W-10), when both run, then exactly one commits and the other sees its state, on three providers (`CancelVersusFinalizeOneCommitsThreeProviders`).\n2351:   - AC007 Given a `Finalizing`, `Completed`, or `Failed` request, when canceled, then 409 `hv_request_not_cancelable` (`CancelTerminalOrFinalizing409`).\n2352:   - AC008 Given an interactive session of a reviewer's agent live in the workspace, when a review run and a probe run of that reviewer start and end, then the interactive session's plugin state files and its session-log session are byte-for-byte unchanged, and the reviewer's turn is in a session of its own (H1 Pester per plugin host, and the live check: `ReviewerRunLeavesSameAgentLiveSessionUnchanged`).\n2353:   - AC009 Given each adapter's launch and a reviewer told to create or change a workspace file, when the run ends, then the attempt was refused or the tool was never offered, and the workspace tree outside the plugin's own host-session state is unchanged (H1, per adapter, with the probe streams of 2026-10-16 as fixtures: `ReviewerRunCannotChangeWorkspaceFilesPerAdapter`).\n2354:   - AC010 Given a server-launched reviewer whose host enforces the foundation's Stop gate, when it has emitted its verdict record, then its own `Chore` turn is closed through the completion gate and the process exits on its own, never held open by the gate (H1 Pester per host and the live check: `ReviewerClosesOwnTurnAndExitsUnderStopGate`).\n2355:   - AC011 Given a scripted fake reviewer that starts a child process which keeps the reviewer's output pipes open, when its run is canceled, its fence goes stale, or the ledger fails, and also when the reviewer's root process exits on its own first, then the reviewer and every descendant are ended, the output is read to its end, and the attempt ends with no process left running (H3: `ReviewerStopEndsWholeProcessTree`).\n2356: - FR-MCP-HVPIPE-009 Execution failures: incidents through triage, offline, retry bound. Sources S-15, S-26, R-17. UC-HV-09. TR: FailHvRunCommand, FileHvIncidentCommand, HvIncident, HvRetryDecision.\n2357:   - AC001 Given a reviewer-attributable failure, when recorded, then the reviewer is `Offline` with the code and incident, and an incident is `Pending` with `dedupeKey` `hv-reviewer-<reviewerId>-<code>` (`ReviewerFailureOfflineWithIncident`).\n2358:   - AC002 Given a pending incident, when filed, then the triage service receives its `dedupeKey` and the incident records the report and group ids (`IncidentFiledThroughTriageWithDedupeKey`).\n2359:   - AC003 Given the same failure twice, or one filing retried after triage accepted it but before its report id was recorded (W-09, L-03), when both are filed, then triage groups them in one group (`RepeatedFailureSameTriageGroup`).\n2360:   - AC004 Given triage unreachable, or a crash after the incident committed and before its filing (W-08), when filing, then the incident stays `Pending` with the error and the next sweep files it (`IncidentFilingRetriedUntilFiled`).\n2361:   - AC005 Given attempts spent, when the last attempt fails, then the request is `Failed` with `attempts_exhausted`, its turns are `None`, and `hv_failed` is appended (`AttemptsExhaustedRequestFailedTurnsReleased`).\n2362:   - AC006 Given a server-attributable failure (`evidence_corrupt`, `snapshot_changed`, `reviewer_not_independent`), when recorded, then an incident with `hv-server-<code>` exists and the reviewer is unchanged (`ServerFailureIncidentReviewerUnchanged`).\n2363: - FR-MCP-HVPIPE-010 Reviewer output contract, per-turn and holistic evaluation. Sources S-03, S-10, S-13, S-21, R-31. UC-HV-05. TR: reviewer contract v1, IHvReviewerAdapter ExtractReviewerRecords, HvFinalVerification V-4 and V-8, HvTurnAssessment, HvFinding.\n2364:   - AC001 Given a log with one assessment per member, one holistic record, and one verdict record last, when finalized, then each requested turn has its score and the holistic evaluation is stored separately (`FinalizeStoresPerTurnScoresAndSeparateHolistic`).\n2365:   - AC002 Given a log missing an assessment, with two verdict records, without a holistic record, or with a finding without remediation, when finalized, then `reviewer_output_invalid` and nothing is committed (`FinalizeIncompleteOutputRefusedNothingCommitted`).\n2366:   - AC003 Given a holistic correctness of 0.97 with every turn AGREE, when finalized, then the overall verdict is DISAGREE (`OverallVerdictHolisticBelow098Disagree`); given an AGREE verdict with a FAIL finding, then `reviewer_output_invalid` (`VerdictAgreeWithFailFindingRefused`).\n2367:   - AC004 Given turn scores whose mean differs from the holistic scores, when finalized, then the stored holistic scores are the reviewer's own, never recomputed (`HolisticScoresNeverComputedFromTurnScores`).\n2368:   - AC005 Given a record the reviewer forged as `hv_provenance` or `hv_brief` inside its message text, when the log is read, then it is not accepted as a worker record (`ForgedWorkerRecordInMessageTextIgnored`).\n2369:   - AC006 Given native streams of each CLI, recorded from the probe runs of 2026-10-16, in which a record is split across events (Grok's per-token text), repeated in a delta and in the whole message (Copilot), inside a fenced block, or beside other text on its line, when the records are extracted as the lines arrive and again over the stored log, then each record is extracted exactly once, the line with other text is free text, and both extractions return the same records (`ReviewerRecordsExtractedOnceFromAssembledMessagesPerCli`).\n2370:   - AC007 Given a run that exits with code 0 and holds no reviewer records (an empty output, or a stream its CLI ended `cancelled`), when it closes, then a review fails with `reviewer_output_invalid`, the reviewer is `Offline` with an incident, and a probe fails with `probe_nonce_mismatch`; an exit code never stands in for a verdict (`ExitZeroWithoutReviewerRecordsIsNotAReview`).\n2371: - FR-MCP-HVPIPE-011 Evidence completeness, GZIP at rest, round-trip verification. Sources S-13, S-30, R-12, R-14. UC-HV-04, UC-HV-05, UC-HV-10. TR: GzipCodec, HvEvidence, HvRunOutputChunk, V-1.\n2372:   - AC001 Given an accepted request and a run's lines, when stored, then every payload is a GZIP member that decompresses to the exact bytes, and no uncompressed copy is stored (`EvidenceStoredGzipOnlyRoundTripExact`).\n2373:   - AC002 Given a chunk whose bytes, SHA-256, or chain hash was altered, or a missing sequence, when finalized, then `evidence_corrupt` and nothing is committed (`FinalizeCorruptOrTruncatedLogRefused`).\n2374:   - AC003 Given a compression whose round trip fails, when admitted or appended, then 500 `evidence_corrupt` and nothing is saved (`CompressionRoundTripFailureNothingSaved`).\n2375:   - AC004 Given a finalized run, when the response log is downloaded compressed and read back as one GZIP stream (VI-07), then decompression yields every stored line in order and its SHA-256 chain equals the run's (`ResponseLogDownloadMultiMemberGzipMatchesChain`).\n2376:   - AC005 Given a reviewer output of any size, when appended, then no limit truncates it (`OutputHasNoSizeLimitNeverTruncated`).\n2377: - FR-MCP-HVPIPE-012 Atomic finalization and turn finality. Sources S-06, S-07, S-23, R-04, R-15. UC-HV-05, UC-HV-12. TR: FinalizeHvRequestCommand, CommitFinalResult, HvTurnFreeze, A-07, A-08, A-11.\n2378:   - AC001 Given a fault injected after each write of CommitFinalResult (W-06), when finalization runs, then nothing of the result is visible after the rollback, the request stays `Finalizing`, and the next sweep finalizes it, on three providers (`FinalizeFaultAfterEachWriteNothingVisibleThreeProviders`).\n2379:   - AC002 Given an admitted turn, when any turn write, review write, review reset, section write, dialog append, title change, or session replace or delete targets it from any origin but `HvFinalization`, then 409 `turn_immutable` with `hv_pending`, and after finalization with `hv_final` (`FrozenTurnEveryWritePathRefused`).\n2380:   - AC003 Given a canceled or failed request, when it ends, then its turns are writable again (`EndedRequestReleasesTurns`).\n2381:   - AC004 Given a request finalized, when FinalizeHvRequestCommand runs again, then it returns the stored outcome and writes nothing (`FinalizeTwiceSecondReturnsStoredNothingWritten`).\n2382:   - AC005 Given a member turn changed by a path that bypasses the guard (a fixture writing the store directly), when finalized, then V-2 refuses with `snapshot_changed` (`FinalizeSnapshotChangedRefused`).\n2383:   - AC006 Given a `Code` turn completed with hostile review `Other` \"HV requested\", when its HV finalizes, then its hostile review holds the HV result and its status stays `completed` (`FinalizeReplacesOtherPendingHvReviewKeepsStatus`).\n2384:   - AC007 Given turns whose hostile review is `Pass` or `Fail`, `Other`, or absent when the A-11 migration adds the HV columns, when the migration runs, then exactly the `Pass` and `Fail` turns are `Final` with no request id, every write to them is refused with 409 `turn_immutable` `hv_final`, and an HV over them is refused with 409 `hv_turns_already_reviewed`, on three providers (HvStorageSchema: `MigrationMarksHvReviewedTurnsFinalThreeProviders`).\n2385: - FR-MCP-HVPIPE-013 Self-review independence. Sources S-28, R-21. UC-HV-03, UC-HV-05. TR: HvAdmissionEligibility, TurnSnapshotBuilder, HvFinalVerification.\n2386:   - AC001 Given one turn with no agent review, one with `Unstarted`, one with `Running`, one with `Pass` at 1.0, one with `Fail` at 0.1, and one with `Other`, all otherwise equal, when each is submitted, then admission, assignment, and the brief bytes are identical (`SelfReviewVariedAdmissionAssignmentAndBriefIdentical`).\n2387:   - AC002 Given those turns reviewed with the same reviewer output, when finalized, then the stored hostile reviews and verdicts are identical (`SelfReviewVariedVerdictIdentical`).\n2388:   - AC003 Given the HostileValidation assemblies, when scanned, then no HV unit, policy, or process reads an `agentReview` field (architecture test `HostileValidationNeverReadsAgentReview`).\n2389: - FR-MCP-HVPIPE-014 Verdict only: no TODO automation. Sources S-25, R-22. UC-HV-05, UC-HV-12. TR: FinalizeHvRequestCommand.\n2390:   - AC001 Given member turns naming TODOs, when an HV finalizes AGREE or DISAGREE, then every TODO is byte-for-byte unchanged (`FinalizeNeverChangesTodos`).\n2391:   - AC002 Given the HostileValidation assemblies, when scanned, then none references the TODO write services (architecture test `HostileValidationHasNoTodoWriteDependency`).\n2392: - FR-MCP-HVPIPE-015 Results, evidence retrieval, and the standard result document. Sources S-13, S-18, S-21. UC-HV-06, UC-HV-10. TR: GetHvRequestQuery, QueryHvRequestsQuery, GetHvResultQuery, GetHvEvidenceQuery, HvResultDocument.\n2393:   - AC001 Given a completed request, when its result is read, then it holds the complete accepted request, every log record in order, every requested turn with its score, the holistic evaluation, and every FAIL and UNKNOWN with remediation (`ResultDocumentCompleteAndDelineated`).\n2394:   - AC002 Given a request not completed, when its result is read, then 409 `hv_result_not_ready` (`ResultBeforeCompletion409`).\n2395:   - AC003 Given running requests, when queried with `status` `Running`, then each has its reviewer, progress, ETA status, and, when read singly, its last 20 lines (`RunningRequestsQueryAndLastOutput`).\n2396:   - AC004 Given the REST, MCP, client, REPL, and Director surfaces, when each submits, reads, queries, cancels, and retrieves, then each returns the same shapes and codes (`HvSurfacesParityGoldenContract`).\n2397: - FR-MCP-HVPIPE-016 Live output stream, progress, and honest ETA. Sources S-18, S-22, P-03, R-12, R-18. UC-HV-06. TR: StreamHvRunOutputQuery, OrderedEventReplay.\n2398:   - AC001 Given a stream attached mid-run, when the caller reconnects with its last event id, then it receives exactly the missed chunks and then live chunks (`OutputStreamReconnectExactlyMissedEvents`).\n2399:   - AC002 Given a progress record with a percentage and an ETA, when read, then `etaStatus` is `Reported` with those values; given none, then `Unknown` with no number (`EtaReportedOrUnknownNeverEstimated`).\n2400:   - AC003 Given a second attempt, when streamed, then the stream continues with the new run's events (`OutputStreamContinuesAcrossAttempts`).\n2401:   - AC004 Given a malformed `Last-Event-ID`, when attaching, then 400 `validation_error` (`OutputStreamMalformedLastEventId400`).\n2402: - FR-MCP-HVPIPE-017 Completion notification stream. Sources S-19, R-16, R-30. UC-HV-07. TR: NotificationOutbox, StreamHvNotificationsQuery, QueryHvNotificationsQuery, WatchHvNotifications.\n2403:   - AC001 Given a state change and its notification in one transaction, when the transaction rolls back, then no notification is visible; when it commits, the notification is visible with the next sequence and no gap (`NotificationOutboxCommittedWithChangeGapFree`).\n2404:   - AC002 Given a notification stream that drops, or a server that stops after a commit and before any stream delivered its notification (W-07), when the stream reconnects with its last sequence, then it receives every later notification exactly once (`NotificationStreamReconnectNoLossNoDuplicate`).\n2405:   - AC003 Given the plugin watcher and a completion of a request its host session submitted, when the next prompt arrives, then the model's context holds the completion once (`HvWatcherDeliversOwnCompletionOnce`, Pester).\n2406:   - AC004 Given a completion of another host session's request, when the watcher receives it, then it records the sequence and inboxes nothing (`HvWatcherIgnoresOtherSessionsRequests`, Pester).\n2407: - FR-MCP-HVPIPE-018 Audit participation and hard stop. Sources S-29, R-19. Every UC. TR: AuditLedgerGuard, the HV entities' `IsDeleted`.\n2408:   - AC001 Given every HV command, when it commits, then a ledger row exists for each entity it changed (`EveryHvMutationHasLedgerRows`).\n2409:   - AC002 Given the ledger unwritable, when any HV command runs, then 503 `audit_unavailable` and nothing is written (`AuditUnavailableEveryHvCommandRefusedNothingWritten`).\n2410:   - AC003 Given an evidence read (result, evidence, output stream, last output), when it returns bytes, then a `read` ledger row exists, and with the ledger unwritable the read is refused (`EvidenceReadsAuditedOrRefused`).\n2411:   - AC004 Given the ledger unwritable during a run (W-12), when the worker appends, then it stops the reviewer and writes nothing, and the lease expiry recovers the request later (`AuditFailureDuringRunHardStop`).\n2412:   - AC005 Given evidence written (an appended chunk and a stored evidence item) and then removed, when the removal commits, then every ledger row written before it is byte-for-byte unchanged, the ledger still holds the history of those writes, the removal adds its own rows, and an architecture scan finds no HV unit or process that updates or deletes a ledger row (I-13, `EvidenceRemovalLeavesAuditLedgerUnchanged`).\n2413: - FR-MCP-HVPIPE-019 Retention until explicit removal. Sources S-29, R-20. UC-HV-11. TR: RemoveHvEvidenceCommand.\n2414:   - AC001 Given evidence of any age, when any unit or process other than RemoveHvEvidenceCommand runs, then no evidence or chunk payload is removed (`NoAutomaticEvidenceRemoval`, with an architecture scan for payload writes).\n2415:   - AC002 Given a terminal request, when its evidence is removed with a reason and a name, then the payloads in the evidence tables are null, every audit ledger row is unchanged (I-13), the hashes, sizes, result rows, findings, and turn reviews stay, and the removal is audited (`RemoveEvidenceKeepsResultAndHashes`).\n2416:   - AC003 Given an active request, when removal is asked, then 409 `hv_request_active` (`RemoveEvidenceActiveRequest409`).\n2417:   - AC004 Given removed evidence, when read, then 410 `hv_evidence_removed` with the kept hashes and sizes (`RemovedEvidenceRead410WithHashes`).\n2418: - FR-MCP-HVPIPE-020 Surface parity: REST, MCP, client, REPL, Director, and plugin. Sources S-02, S-16, S-19, R-29, R-30. Every UC. TR: HostileValidationController, FwhMcpTools.HostileValidation, HostileValidationClient, HostileValidationWorkflow, HostileValidationDirectorCommands, the plugin verbs and watcher.\n2419:   - AC001 Given the golden contract of the public units, when each surface runs it, then the shapes, statuses, and codes match (`HvSurfacesParityGoldenContract`, shared with FR-MCP-HVPIPE-015-AC004).\n2420:   - AC002 Given the internal units, when the routes, tools, client, and REPL are scanned, then none exposes them (`HvInternalUnitsHaveNoPublicSurface`).\n2421:   - AC003 Given the plugin's submit verb, when it runs, then it binds the submitting turn and builds a stable idempotency key for the same call (`HvSubmitVerbBindsTurnStableKey`, Pester).\n2422:   - AC004 Given a retryable answer to the plugin's submit verb, when it returns, then it reports `retryable: true` with exit 1 and writes no failsafe record (`HvSubmitVerbRetryableNotQueued`, Pester).\n2423:   - AC005 Given the REPL client mutation policy, when it classifies `hostileValidation`, then writes are service-gated and reads are allowed (`ReplPolicyHostileValidationClassification`).\n2424: - FR-MCP-HVPIPE-021 Response grading and trust through finalization. Sources the foundation's Phase C, R-02, R-03, A-04, A-05. UC-HV-05. TR: HvRequestResponse, FinalizeHvRequestCommand, RecordModelGradeCommand (amended).\n2425:   - AC001 Given member turns with agent responses and Mode not `Off`, when finalized, then each pending response gets one model grade from the run's reviewer and its trust decision, in the finalization transaction (`FinalizeGradesLinkedResponsesInSameTransaction`).\n2426:   - AC002 Given Mode `Off` at finalization, when finalized, then the linked responses are `NotGraded` with `agent_context_disabled` and the turns are finalized (`FinalizeModeOffResponsesNotGraded`).\n2427:   - AC003 Given a response rejected or superseded while pending, when the transition commits, then its item is `Closed` with that reason and the request's state is unchanged (`ResponseTransitionClosesHvItemOnly`).\n2428:   - AC004 Given the public