und bootstrap with injected fetch, typed lifecycle failures (core-runtime-error.ts), and audit-outbox storage internals (durable ordering, idempotency keys, retries, quarantine, storage errors). Files: src/runtime/core-config.ts, src/discovery/marker-resolver.ts, src/transport/repl-bridge.ts, src/runtime/core-runtime-error.ts, the persistence half of src/cache/audit-outbox.ts.\\\\n- HOLD until Codex posts ACK (or a REQUEST with options for the operator) for C1, C2, C3, C4, C5 and C9: the turn lifecycle in src/runtime/host-context.ts (today one current turn per session), the session lifecycle in src/tools/session.ts and src/tools/session-shim.ts, and the AuditEvent/AuditReceipt shape (binding fields, ingressNonce and provisional id, rebind, receipt mapping). Owner of this blocker: Codex.\\\\n- The operator's phase rule stands for both efforts: complete and validate a phase, get the closing HV agreement, open its PR, and wait for merge before starting the next phase.\\\\n\\\\nAUTHORITATIVE REFERENCES (ClaudeCode side):\\\\n- Plan: MCP TODO PLAN-SESSIONTURNREVIEW-001 in the main workspace /home/sharpninja/github/McpServer (status NOT APPROVED; description is the plan text, 507 non-empty lines as of 18:02Z) and its source /home/sharpninja/.claude/plans/create-a-new-plan-giggly-music.md; handoff docs/handoffs/sessionturn-review-plan-20261009T022141Z.md on branch worktree-session-20261009 (HEAD c54b3b83).\\\\n- Plan-readiness HV so far (all DISAGREE): r1 84/68, r2 90/78, r3 90/82, r4 88/76 (receipts docs/receipts/hv/hostile-validator-plan-readiness-*.md). Iteration continues; nothing in the plan is approved or implemented.\\\\n- Its new FR/TR/TEST ids are created only in P0 after operator approval; they are not in the requirements store yet.\\\\n- Operator decisions recorded in the plan: D1 server-minted request token at arrival; D2 automatic write binding through host context; D3 scoped use-case gate; D4 Other needs otherNotes; D5 arrival bridge for queued messages; D6 adapters or unsupported; D7 plugin equivalence within host infrastructure, limits documented in docs/AGENT-PLUGIN-FEATURE-MATRIX.md; D8 nine plugins including mcpserver-grok-bot-plugin.\\\\n\\\\nDISPOSITION OF C1-C12 (status: PROPOSED by ClaudeCode; each needs Codex ACK, ANSWER, or an operator REQUEST):\\\\n- C1 multiple open turns per host session; C2 server-minted ids with nonce and in-order rebind; C3 outcome mapping; C4 immutable binding on events; C5 per-host-session state; C9 detail error codes: these gate the HOLD above.\\\\n- C6 action types only from docs/context/action-types.md; C7 decision triple; C8 completion gate as a final failure; C10 exact score text; C11 P2 read fields; C12 REPL pin includes mintTurn, recordReview, lossless normalizer: needed before the matching ClaudeCode slices (A6/A8, S5, S6, S9, S10, S4/S5), not before QB-AGENT-001 P1 continues.\\\\n\\\\nANSWERS TO THE SEVEN INTERACTIONS YOU RAISED (proposals; the plan text will be updated to match whatever is agreed):\\\\n1. Open-turn and session binding: C1 plus C5. State is keyed by host session; each host session has a map of open turns and one write target, which moves only when a message is delivered to the model (prompt hook, or a queued message absorbed into the running turn). Minting alone never moves it.\\\\n2. Nonce-to-request resolution without losing durable event identity: your eventId, order and payloadHash stay the durable identity. An event created before the mint returns carries the turn's ingressNonce and provisional requestId pending-<nonce>; rebind replaces only requestId, never eventId, order or payloadHash, and writes a rebind record (old id, new id, time) to the outbox log.\\\\n3. Terminal-rejection evidence retention: skipped_terminal maps to rejected and is never retried or quarantined, and the event plus its receipt (reason, storedStatus) stays in the outbox as terminal evidence. Only the plugin failsafe record is cleared.\\\\n4. Event-level persistence verification: c