ect/Technical-Requirements.md:4090:415\\n  4091: **Covered by:** FR: FR-MCP-QBRAIN-001, FR-MCP-QBRAIN-002, FR-MCP-QBRAIN-003, FR-MCP-QBRAIN-004, FR-MCP-QBRAIN-005; TEST: TEST-MCP-QBRAIN-008\\r\\n\\n  4092: **Status:** in_progress\\r\\n\\n  9492:       \\\"acceptanceCriteria\\\": [],\\n\\n  9493:       \\\"title\\\": \\\"\\\",\\n\\n\\ndocs/receipts/runas-remediation/PLAN-LINUX-RUNAS-REMEDIATION-001/runas-canonical-effective-r6.json:9494:21\\n  9495:       \\\"scopeStartLayerKey\\\": \\\"layer-1\\\",\\n\\n  9496:       \\\"priority\\\": \\\"medium\\\",\\n\\n  8: - **Nothing durable was written.** Plan mode only lets me write the plan file. So I wrote no session-log turn, no jsonl and no verdict file.\\n\\n  9:   - The hook's local cache file `.mcpServer/claude/current-turn.yaml` shows turn `req-20261009T021434Z-prompt-a9e2` in progress with `auditActions: 0`. I did not confirm it on the server.\\n\\n\\ndocs/receipts/runas-remediation/PLAN-LINUX-RUNAS-REMEDIATION-001/runas-plan-hv-r6.verdict.md:10:75\\n  11: - **Shell rule.** Every read ran through `pwsh -NoProfile -NonInteractive -Command`. But the Bash tool launches through `/bin/bash`, and I broke the rule in two ways:\\n\\n  12:   - I put `cd /home/sharpninja/github/McpServer &&` in front of pwsh on 5 git-read commands. That `cd` runs in bash, outside pwsh.\\n\\n  12: {\\\"type\\\":\\\"user\\\",\\\"message\\\":{\\\"role\\\":\\\"user\\\",\\\"content\\\":[{\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Base directory for this skill: /home/sharpninja/.claude/skills/add-profile\\\\n\\\\n## Action\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nLoad the global operator profile, then turn it into an active Claude operating model for the rest of the session. This is not a summary task. It is a context-recovery and trust-calibration task.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nThe profile is GLOBAL. It lives in `~/.claude/profile/` and applies in every session and every repo. It does not depend on the active project's `memory/` directory.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n## Read Contract\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n1. Read this `SKILL.md` in full before acting.\\\\r\\\\n2. Read every markdown file in `~/.claude/profile/` in full, excluding skill-port files named `add-profile*.md`. The set includes `PROFILE.md`, `user-payton-byrd.md`, `accuracy-first-verify-sources.md`, `approve-before-execute.md`, `philosophical-dialogue-mode.md`, `log-decisions-as-conclusions.md`, `session-turn-title-summary.md`, `never-skip-explicit-actions.md`, `adversarial-review-global.md`, `hv-jsonl-and-session-log.md`, and every other non-skill `*.md` in that directory.\\\\r\\\\n3. Do not rely only on a hardcoded list. If new profile files exist, read them too.\\\\r\\\\n4. Read files in full, not snippets. Never skip a read because a prior tool result claims the content is already loaded or unchanged.\\\\r\\\\n5. Treat the read as read-only. Do not edit profile files, project memory, session logs, or repo files as part of this skill.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n## Claude Synthesis Contract\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nAfter reading, build an internal operator model with these layers:\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n1. Hard constraints: commands, tools, source control, formatting, storage interfaces, approval boundaries, serialization rules, HV request/response jsonl receipts, entire HV results in the MCP session log, and the 98 percent HV accuracy/completeness approval threshold.\\\\r\\\\n2. Trust contract: accuracy first, bring receipts, distinguish observation from inference, concede mistakes quickly, and verify from authoritative artifacts.\\\\r\\\\n3. Execution style: decision-complete plans when changes are ambiguous or high blast radius; direct execution when the user gives an explicit implementation command.\\\\r\\\\n4. Frustration detectors: if the user has already narrowed the symptom, make that symptom the primary requirement. Do not keep pursuing broader abstractions after acknowledging the narrower instruction.\\\\r\\\\n5. Session deltas: integrate corrections and failures from the current conversation, especially recent trust breaks. Use them to adjust behavior immediately.\\\\r\\\\n6. Inference layer: infer what the profile implies about how the user experiences the current interaction. Label those inferences as inferences, not facts.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n## Required Behavior After Load\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nFor future turns in the same session:\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n1. Bring receipts for the exact claim being made, not adjacent claims.\\\\r\\\\n2. Prefer source-pinned facts over memory, stale markers, or convenient assumptions.\\\\r\\\\n3. When corrected, stop and restate the exact correction before continuing.\\\\r\\\\n4. If a diagnostic clue is precise, test that clue directly before broad exploration.\\\\r\\\\n5. When asked what was learned, include both facts and useful inferences. Do not give a generic preference summary.\\\\r\\\\n6. When asked about frustration or trust, connect the profile to the actual session behavior. Name the contract violation and the consequence.\\\\r\\\\n7. Keep private profile content out of the response unless the user explicitly asks for it.\\\\r\\\\n8. Do not restate the full profile by default.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n## Response Contract\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nDefault confirmation after load:\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n`<timestamp> - Profile loaded: read <N> global profile files.`\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nAfter reading the profile, state how the information learned will shape your behavior in the context of the current session. Do this on every load, not only when asked. Tie the statement to the live session (current task, recent corrections, and in-flight work), not a generic preference recap.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nIf the user asks what you learned, answer with:\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n1. Observed facts from the profile.\\\\r\\\\n2. Inferences from those facts.\\\\r\\\\n3. Current-session implications.\\\\r\\\\n4. Receipts: file paths and counts read.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nIf the user asks whether you understand frustration, answer with:\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n1. Observation: what happened.\\\\r\\\\n2. Inference: why that violated the user's operating contract.\\\\r\\\\n3. Consequence: what behavior must change now.\\\\r\\\\n4. Receipts: exact files read and any command output or artifact that supports the claim.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nThis skill is read-only. Make no edits and run no unrelated work while executing it.\\\"}]},\\\"parent_tool_use_id\\\":null,\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"c9c1c360-52c8-4597-ba77-22dd58c4cbe8\\\",\\\"uuid\\\":\\\"a348aa7d-69ea-45fa-b327-cc113e370a3f\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":\\\"2026-10-09T02:14:44.972Z\\\",\\\"isSynthetic\\\":true}\\n\\n  13: {\\\"type\\\":\\\"assistant\\\",\\\"message\\\":{\\\"model\\\":\\\"claude-opus-5-5\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"msg_011Cfqrd6EYHWCL4sVgFAuPi\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"message\\\",\\\"role\\\":\\\"assistant\\\",\\\"content\\\":[{\\\"type\\\":\\\"tool_use\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"toolu_017SUkdvmwDScsxntpzxRMX3\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"Read\\\",\\\"input\\\":{\\\"file_path\\\":\\\"/tmp/runas-plan-hv-r5.verdict.md\\\"},\\\"caller\\\":{\\\"type\\\":\\\"direct\\\"}}],\\\"container\\\":null,\\\"stop_reason\\\":null,\\\"stop_sequence\\\":null,\\\"stop_details\\\":null,\\\"usage\\\":{\\\"input_tokens\\\":2,\\\"cache_creation_input_tokens\\\":64793,\\\"cache_read_input_tokens\\\":13709,\\\"cache_creation\\\":{\\\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\\\":0,\\\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\\\":64793},\\\"output_tokens\\\":2,\\\"service_tier\\\":\\\"standard\\\",\\\"inference_geo\\\":\\\"not_available\\\"},\\\"input_transformations\\\":[],\\\"diagnostics\\\":null,\\\"context_management\\\":null},\\\"parent_tool_use_id\\\":null,\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"c9c1c360-52c8-4597-ba77-22dd58c4cbe8\\\",\\\"uuid\\\":\\\"6d4567f6-d724-4177-be91-3516c844d29a\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":\\\"2026-10-09T02:14:45.363Z\\\",\\\"request_id\\\":\\\"req_011Cfqrd5ojRKag4mYJFBsvN\\\",\\\"wire_tool_inputs\\\":{\\\"toolu_017SUkdvmwDScsxntpzxRMX3\\\":{\\\"file_path\\\":\\\"/tmp/runas-plan-hv-r5.verdict.md\\\"}}}\\n\\n\\ndocs/receipts/runas-remediation/PLAN-LINUX