lable. If approved recovery cannot establish both C10 contexts, Full G1 remains externally blocked regardless of independent Windows progress.\\\\r\\\\n  56: \\\\r\\\\n  57: ## Candidate authority and complete source\\\\r\\\\n  58: \\\\r\\\\n  59: The operator's G1-Repair rule supersedes only the historical caller SHA/tree assignments in completion-plan lines 276, 280, 312, and 316 for repaired execution. All behavioral gates and inventories remain required. W18 has already changed source, so `808ec049d56daf214c391beccd6b9d69bb9867c6` / `5091b64a8d9dade0bfb0b2b0295b93d464e60e1c` is historical baseline evidence, never the final repaired caller.\\\\r\\\\n  60: \\\\r\\\\n  61: Preserve `F:\\\\\\\\GitHub\\\\\\\\McpServer`, its index, untracked work, existing worktrees, and QuadBrain CLI/QBAgent changes. Record a recoverable snapshot with full HEAD, staged and unstaged binary diffs, and a hash-verified copy/manifest of relevant untracked source. Do not reset, clean, stash away, overwrite, or revert unrelated work.\\\\r\\\\n  62: \\\\r\\\\n  63: ## Blocking rule and execution dependencies\\\\r\\\\n  64: \\\\r\\\\n  65: After plan execution approval, run the bounded Phase 0 probes first. A failed Linux preflight blocks native runs and Full G1 completion, not source preparation, Windows sixteenth tasks 3/5/6, provider diagnosis, or Build.Tests diagnosis. Continue independent authorized work in the isolated repair checkout. Each Windows sub-slice exits only after its entire applicable current-plus-prior suite is green and its Sol extra-high HV passes. Native-dependent tasks and the enclosing Full G1 phase remain open; this is not a Windows-only closeout.\\\\r\\\\n  66: \\\\r\\\\n  67: The parent launches all execution through its existing PowerShell.Mcp Baltic console `#69712` using `execute_command`. Do not call `start_console` with `reason` or allocate a replacement console. While Baltic reports Busy, call `wait_for_completion` for the active command until terminal state; do not submit another command or use `Start-Sleep`. Reviewer processes do not drive Baltic.\\\\r\\\\n  68: \\\\r\\\\n  69: ## Phase 0: C10 executor preflight (read-only, no product edit)\\\\r\\\\n  70: \\\\r\\\\n  71: Tests: none. This is ops preflight, not FR implementation. Receipt required.\\\\r\\\\n  72: \\\\r\\\\n  73: Commands (PowerShell.Mcp `execute_command` on Baltic `#69712`):\\\\r\\\\n  74: \\\\r\\\\n  75: 1. `wsl.exe --version` with a 10-second process deadline; preserve exit, duration, stdout, and stderr.\\\\r\\\\n  76: 2. `wsl.exe --list --verbose` with a 10-second process deadline; record empty vs hang.\\\\r\\\\n  77: 3. `Get-Service WslService, vmcompute, hns`.\\\\r\\\\n  78: 4. Terminate only task-owned expired probes. Do not restart services unless Payton already approved it in this slice.\\\\r\\\\n  79: \\\\r\\\\n  80: A responsive version/list is insufficient: Phase 4 capability and identity probes must pass through both exact executor routes.\\\\r\\\\n  81: \\\\r\\\\n  82: If the observed WSL enumeration failure recurs, request explicit approval for one `Restart-Service -Name WslService -Force` and continue independent work while approval is pending. Execution-plan approval, administrator access, and disabled tool approval checks do not authorize that restart. After explicit restart approval, perform only that restart and rerun the bounded list. If still blocked, stop native recovery and report the exact boundary. VHD inspection/repair, package installation, default-user changes, `vmcompute` restart, and privilege grants require separately authorized actions. Do not keep retrying unchanged probes.\\\\r\\\\n  83: \\\\r\\\\n  84: Pass: recorded distro, user, native-ext4 checkout path, `dotnet`/`git` executable path/version, non-root identity, and a harmless probe through that exact route.\\\\r\\\\n  85: \\\\r\\\\n  86: ## Phase 1: complete isolated G1 repair source\\\\r\\\\n  87: \\\\r\\\\n  88: Requirements: sixteenth work uses existing `FR-MCP-U