link verification, contract reconciliation, and plan persistence are agent responsibilities, not questions the user still needs to answer.\n25: \n26: ## 2. Exact state of work\n27: \n28: ### Completed or available\n29: \n30: - The previous conversation recovered the HV draft and displayed a consolidated H0-H7 plan. The user then corrected several incorrectly presented open decisions; those corrections are incorporated below.\n31: - The original architecture source, foundation plan, previous handoff, requirements matrix, and conversation-history file were confirmed to exist during this handoff.\n32: - This agent inspected the foundation architecture's introductory conventions. It has NOT comprehensively reviewed the entire architecture or reconciled all contracts and requirement links.\n33: - This agent independently verified the mandatory-plugin policy and both disabled plugin settings, as described in section 3.\n34: \n35: ### Not completed\n36: \n37: - No HV architecture amendment has been created.\n38: - No corrected HV plan has been persisted as a canonical TODO. There is no saved TODO ID to report.\n39: - No successful canonical database audit was obtained for this work.\n40: - No complete requirements/task-link verification has been performed.\n41: - No HV implementation, implementation worktree, builds, tests, or commits have been performed by this agent.\n42: - No existing architecture, foundation plan, requirements file, or TODO storage file was modified by this agent.\n43: \n44: This handoff is the only new workspace file created for the handoff request. It is a local diagnostic/continuity artifact, not a workaround for canonical persistence or mandatory auditing.\n45: \n46: ## 3. Verified blocker and safety boundaries\n47: \n48: The runtime instructions at `/home/sharpninja/github/McpServer/AGENTS-README-FIRST.yaml` currently require the matching agent plugin:\n49: \n50: - Line 204 prohibits substituting raw REST, generic `mcpserver-repl`, helper modules,