oHighestEffortAndCliDefaultModel`).\",\n20:         \"isSatisfied\": false\n21:       },\n22:       {\n23:         \"id\": \"AC004\",\n24:         \"text\": \"Given an update with a stale `expectedStateVersion`, when it is applied, then 409 `conflict` with `retryable: false` and `details.field` `expectedStateVersion` and nothing changes (`UpdateReviewerStaleStateVersion409NothingChanged`).\",\n25:         \"isSatisfied\": false\n26:       },\n27:       {\n28:         \"id\": \"AC005\",\n29:         \"text\": \"Given an update that changes the strategy, agent path, model, or effort, when it commits, then the reviewer is `Unverified` with reason `configuration_changed` and `reviewer_unverified` is appended (`UpdateReviewerLaunchChangeMakesUnverifiedAndNotifies`).\",\n30:         \"isSatisfied\": false\n31:       },\n32:       {\n33:         \"id\": \"AC006\",\n34:         \"text\": \"Given the REST, MCP, client, REPL, and Director surfaces, when each lists, gets, and updates a reviewer, then each returns the same record and the same error codes (`ReviewerSurfacesParityGoldenContract`).\",\n35:         \"isSatisfied\": false\n36:       }\n37:     ],\n38:     \"description\": \"Reviewer pool configuration and real-time management. Sources: S-02, R-08. Use cases: UC-HV-01.\",\n39:     \"id\": \"FR-MCP-HVPIPE-001\",\n40:     \"title\": \"Reviewer pool configuration and real-time management\",\n41:     \"area\": \"MCP\",\n42:     \"createdAt\": \"2026-10-17T14:25:08.8543231+00:00\",\n43:     \"updatedAt\": \"2026-10-17T14:25:08.8543604+00:00\",\n44:     \"scopeStartLayerKey\": \"layer-1\"\n45:   },\n46:   {\n47:     \"priority\": \"high\",\n48:     \"notes\": \"Proposed in architecture Amendment 1 (docs/architecture/SessionTurn-Review-AgentContext-Architecture-Amendment-1-Durable-HV.md, section 19.1); plan PLAN-HVPIPELINE-001, not approved; created 2026-10-16 so the requirement is captured as it emerges.\",\n49:     \"status\": \"pending\",\n50:     \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n51:       {\n52:         \"id\": \"AC001\",\n53:         \"text\": \"Given each alias of the alias table in any case and with any separators, when normalized, then it maps to its reviewer id, in C# and in PowerShell from one golden contract (`AgentIdentityGoldenContractTests`, C# and Pester).\",\n54:         \"isSatisfied\": false\n55:       },\n56:       {\n57:         \"id\": \"AC002\",\n58:         \"text\": \"Given a submitting turn whose agent is `ClaudeCode` (or `ClaudeCowork`, `claude-code`, `cowork`), when a request is admitted, then Claude is never assigned, and V-5 refuses a run whose reviewer is Claude (`SubmitterAliasesNeverAssignedClaudeFamily`, `FinalVerificationSubmitterReviewerRefusedNotIndependent`).\",\n59:         \"isSatisfied\": false\n60:       },\n61:       {\n62:         \"id\": \"AC003\",\n63:         \"text\": \"Given a free-text submitter name that differs from the submitting turn's agent, when a request is admitted, then exclusion uses the turn's agent (`SubmitterExclusionUsesTurnAgentNeverFreeText`).\",\n64:         \"isSatisfied\": false\n65:       },\n66:       {\n67:         \"id\": \"AC004\",\n68:         \"text\": \"Given the cursor at Copilot, every reviewer enabled and `Online`, and three requests that Cline submits over Cline sessions (so only Cline is excluded), when they are admitted one after another, then Claude, Codex, and Grok are assigned and the cursor ends at Grok (`RoundRobinAssignsInPoolOrderAfterCursor`).\",\n69:         \"isSatisfied\": false\n70:       },\n71:       {\n72:         \"id\": \"AC005\",\n73:         \"text\": \"Given the server restarts between two submissions, when the second is admitted, then it takes the reviewer after the cursor stored before the restart (`RoundRobinCursorSurvivesRestart`).\",\n74:         \"isSatisfied\": false\n75:       },\nEXIT_CODE=0\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
