en any HV command runs, then 503 `audit_unavailable` and nothing is written (`AuditUnavailableEveryHvCommandRefusedNothingWritten`).\\n  - AC003 Given an evidence read (result, evidence, output stream, last output), when it returns bytes, then a `read` ledger row exists, and with the ledger unwritable the read is refused (`EvidenceReadsAuditedOrRefused`).\\n  - AC004 Given the ledger unwritable during a run (W-12), when the worker appends, then it stops the reviewer and writes nothing, and the lease expiry recovers the request later (`AuditFailureDuringRunHardStop`).\\n  - AC005 Given evidence written (an appended chunk and a stored evidence item) and then removed, when the removal commits, then every ledger row written before it is byte-for-byte unchanged, the ledger still holds the history of those writes, the removal adds its own rows, and an architecture scan finds no HV unit or process that updates or deletes a ledger row (I-13, `EvidenceRemovalLeavesAuditLedgerUnchanged`).\\n- FR-MCP-HVPIPE-019 Retention until explicit removal. Sources S-29, R-20. Use cases: UC-HV-11.\"\n25:     },\n26:     {\n27:       \"Actual\": \"Implementation contract of FR-MCP-HVPIPE-018: AuditLedgerGuard, the HV entities' `IsDeleted`. Each named unit, policy, process, component, and entity is specified in docs/architecture/SessionTurn-Review-AgentContext-Architecture-Amendment-1-Durable-HV.md (sections 10 to 16).\",\n28:       \"Id\": \"FR-MCP-HVPIPE-018\",\n29:       \"Field\": \"TR.description\",\n30:       \"Expected\": \"Implementation contract of FR-MCP-HVPIPE-018: RemoveHvEvidenceCommand. Each named unit, policy, process, component, and entity is specified in docs/architecture/SessionTurn-Review-AgentContext-Architecture-Amendment-1-Durable-HV.md (sections 10 to 16).\"\n31:     },\n32:     {\n33:       \"Actual\": \"The units, policies, processes, components, and entities named in this contract satisfy every acceptance criterion of FR-MCP-HVPIPE-018 (5 criteria), proven by TEST-M