0:       \"Expected\": \"Named tests exist and prove FR-MCP-HVPIPE-018-AC002: RemoveEvidenceKeepsResultAndHashes.\"\n61:     },\n62:     {\n63:       \"Actual\": \"Given an evidence read (result, evidence, output stream, last output), when it returns bytes, then a `read` ledger row exists, and with the ledger unwritable the read is refused (`EvidenceReadsAuditedOrRefused`).\",\n64:       \"Id\": \"FR-MCP-HVPIPE-018\",\n65:       \"Field\": \"FR.AC003\",\n66:       \"Expected\": \"Given an active request, when removal is asked, then 409 `hv_request_active` (`RemoveEvidenceActiveRequest409`).\"\n67:     },\n68:     {\n69:       \"Actual\": \"Named tests exist and prove FR-MCP-HVPIPE-018-AC003: EvidenceReadsAuditedOrRefused.\",\n70:       \"Id\": \"FR-MCP-HVPIPE-018\",\n71:       \"Field\": \"TEST.AC003\",\n72:       \"Expected\": \"Named tests exist and prove FR-MCP-HVPIPE-018-AC003: RemoveEvidenceActiveRequest409.\"\n73:     },\n74:     {\n75:       \"Actual\": \"Given the ledger unwritable during a run (W-12), when the worker appends, then it stops the reviewer and writes nothing, and the lease expiry recovers the request later (`AuditFailureDuringRunHardStop`).\",\n76:       \"Id\": \"FR-MCP-HVPIPE-018\",\n77:       \"Field\": \"FR.AC004\",\n78:       \"Expected\": \"Given removed evidence, when read, then 410 `hv_evidence_removed` with the kept hashes and sizes (`RemovedEvidenceRead410WithHashes`).\"\n79:     },\n80:     {\n81:       \"Actual\": \"Named tests exist and prove FR-MCP-HVPIPE-018-AC004: AuditFailureDuringRunHardStop.\",\n82:       \"Id\": \"FR-MCP-HVPIPE-018\",\n83:       \"Field\": \"TEST.AC004\",\n84:       \"Expected\": \"Named tests exist and prove FR-MCP-HVPIPE-018-AC004: RemovedEvidenceRead410WithHashes.\"\n85:     },\n86:     {\n87:       \"Actual\": \"Named tests of FR-MCP-HVPIPE-018: EveryHvMutationHasLedgerRows; AuditUnavailableEveryHvCommandRefusedNothingWritten; EvidenceReadsAuditedOrRefused; AuditFailureDuringRunHardStop; EvidenceRemovalLeavesAuditLedgerUnchanged.\",\n88:       \"Id\": \"FR-MCP-HVPIPE-018\",\n89:       \"Field\": \"TEST.description\",\n90:       \"Expected\": \"Named tests of FR-MCP-HVPIPE-018: NoAutomaticEvidenceRemoval; RemoveEvidenceKeepsResultAndHashes; RemoveEvidenceActiveRequest409; RemovedEvidenceRead410WithHashes.\"\n91:     },\n92:     {\n93:       \"Actual\": \"Surface parity: REST, MCP, client, REPL, Director, and plugin. Sources: S-02, S-16, S-19, R-29, R-30. Use cases: Every UC.\",\n94:       \"Id\": \"FR-MCP-HVPIPE-020\",\n95:       \"Field\": \"FR.description\",\n96:       \"Expected\": \"Surface parity: REST, MCP, client, REPL, Director, and plugin. Sources: S-02, S-16, S-19, R-29, R-30. Every UC. TR: HostileValidationController, FwhMcpTools.HostileValidation, HostileValidationClient, HostileValidationWorkflow, HostileValidationDirectorCommands, the plugin verbs and watcher.\\n  - AC001 Given the golden contract of the public units, when each surface runs it, then the shapes, statuses, and codes match (`HvSurfacesParityGoldenContract`, shared with FR-MCP-HVPIPE-015-AC004).\\n  - AC002 Given the internal units, when the routes, tools, client, and REPL are scanned, then none exposes them (`HvInternalUnitsHaveNoPublicSurface`).\\n  - AC003 Given the plugin's submit verb, when it runs, then it binds the submitting turn and builds a stable idempotency key for the same call (`HvSubmitVerbBindsTurnStableKey`, Pester).\\n  - AC004 Given a retryable answer to the plugin's submit verb, when it returns, then it reports `retryable: true` with exit 1 and writes no failsafe record (`HvSubmitVerbRetryableNotQueued`, Pester).\\n  - AC005 Given the REPL client mutation policy, when it classifies `hostileValidation`, then writes are service-gated and reads are allowed (`ReplPolicyHostileValidationClassification`).\\n- FR-MCP-HVPIPE-021 Response grading and trust through finalization. Sources the foundation's Phase C, R-02, R-03, A-04, A-05. Use cases: UC-HV-05.\"\n97:     },\n98:     