{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_133","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/pwsh -NoProfile -Command \"pwsh.exe -NoProfile -NonInteractive -File './docs/receipts/hv/hv-r1-verify.ps1' -Task EvidenceSummary\"","aggregated_output":"{\n  \"Number\": 81,\n  \"Url\": \"https://github.com/sharpninja/McpServer/pull/81\",\n  \"MergedAt\": \"2026-10-16T22:41:48Z\",\n  \"MergeCommit\": {\n    \"oid\": \"a2cbd57897c588f178da3a191186726b8adab1b1\"\n  },\n  \"Findings\": [\n    {\n      \"Id\": 4300020822,\n      \"ReviewId\": 5554472359,\n      \"CreatedUtc\": \"2026-10-16T22:48:12Z\",\n      \"Path\": \"src/QBrainAi.Storage/WorkspaceKeyConversion.cs\",\n      \"Line\": 26,\n      \"Commit\": \"6dbc384323c036a57c37fd9eaf2259879c1d956f\",\n      \"Body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Migrate legacy workspace keys before canonical queries**\\n\\nOn an upgraded Windows installation, existing rows contain the previous `Q:\\\\workspace` spelling, while this converter canonicalizes new writes and query parameters to `Q:/workspace` but leaves values read from storage unchanged. Because this commit includes no data migration, SQLite/PostgreSQL comparisons against the canonical discriminator no longer match those legacy rows, so tenant-filtered data becomes invisible and workspace bootstrap can create parallel rows. Add a provider migration that rewrites every affected key and foreign key before enabling this converter.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\\n\\n<!-- codex-code-review-finding:v1 -->\",\n      \"Url\": \"https://github.com/sharpninja/McpServer/pull/81#discussion_r4300020822\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"Id\": 4300020832,\n      \"ReviewId\": 5554472359,\n      \"CreatedUtc\": \"2026-10-16T22:48:12Z\",\n      \"Path\": \"plugins/core/lib-ps/plugin-hook.ps1\",\n      \"Line\": 1065,\n      \"Commit\": \"6dbc384323c036a57c37fd9eaf2259879c1d956f\",\n      \"Body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Return a proof shape that the stop hook can consume**\\n\\nWhen a cached session is stale, this production REPL call cannot produce the proof consumed below: the added client method returns `Task<UnifiedSessionLogDto>`, which is absent from `GenericClientPassthrough.AwaitTaskResultAsync` and therefore raises `Unsupported task result type`; even after adding that case, `UnifiedSessionLogDto` contains `status` and `turns`, not the expected `workspacePath`, `requestId`, `outcome`, or `serverStatus`. The catch consequently treats completed persisted turns as active, leaving the stop gate blocked indefinitely; expose a matching proof DTO or derive the requested turn outcome from the returned session DTO.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\\n\\n<!-- codex-code-review-finding:v1 -->\",\n      \"Url\": \"https://github.com/sharpninja/McpServer/pull/81#discussion_r4300020832\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"Id\": 4300020839,\n      \"ReviewId\": 5554472359,\n      \"CreatedUtc\": \"2026-10-16T22:48:12Z\",\n      \"Path\": \"src/QBrainAi.Client/WorkspacePathNormalizer.cs\",\n      \"Line\": 130,\n      \"Commit\": \"6dbc384323c036a57c37fd9eaf2259879c1d956f\",\n      \"Body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Treat root-relative Windows segments as rooted**\\n\\nOn a Windows host, a segment such as `\\\\repo` is rooted and must replace the path after retaining the current drive, but `IsWindowsRooted` recognizes only drive-qualified and UNC paths. `Combine(\\\"C:/content\\\", \\\"\\\\\\\\repo\\\")` therefore returns `C:/content/repo` instead of `C:/repo`; in particular, `ResolveRepoRootWorkspacePath` now resolves a root-relative `RepoRoot` under the content directory and selects the wrong workspace and tenant. Handle a leading backslash as Windows-root-relative using the root drive.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\\n\\n<!-- codex-code-review-finding:v1 -->\",\n      \"Url\": \"https://github.com/sharpninja/McpServer/pull/81#discussion_r4300020839\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"Id\": 4300020846,\n      \"ReviewId\": 5554472359,\n      \"CreatedUtc\": \"2026-10-16T22:48:12Z\",\n      \"Path\": \"src/QBrainAi.Services/Services/FileGitHubWorkspaceTokenStore.cs\",\n      \"Line\": 326,\n      \"Commit\": \"6dbc384323c036a57c37fd9eaf2259879c1d956f\",\n      \"Body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Preserve access to legacy GitHub token entries**\\n\\nAfter upgrading on Windows, this changes the persistent token-store lookup key from the prior `C:\\\\repo` form to `C:/repo`, but entries already stored in the JSON document are never canonicalized on read. The `OrdinalIgnoreCase` comparisons in `GetAsync`, `UpsertAsync`, and `DeleteAsync` do not equate different separators, so existing GitHub credentials become inaccessible, an upsert creates a duplicate entry, and deletion leaves the legacy secret behind. Normalize loaded entry paths or migrate the token document before using the new key format.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\\n\\n<!-- codex-code-review-finding:v1 -->\",\n      \"Url\": \"https://github.com/sharpninja/McpServer/pull/81#discussion_r4300020846\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"Id\": 4300020851,\n      \"ReviewId\": 5554472359,\n      \"CreatedUtc\": \"2026-10-16T22:48:12Z\",\n      \"Path\": \"plugins/core/lib-ps/repl-invoke.ps1\",\n      \"Line\": 738,\n      \"Commit\": \"6dbc384323c036a57c37fd9eaf2259879c1d956f\",\n      \"Body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Keep descendants killable after the root process exits**\\n\\nWhen the REPL wrapper starts a background descendant and then exits before the deadline, `HasExited` is already true here, so `Kill(true)` is skipped even if the descendant still owns stdout/stderr or continues running detached. The subsequent loop can only time out—or can report success once the pipes close—while leaving that descendant alive, defeating the bounded-child guarantee. Start the child in an owned process group/job and terminate that group independently of the root process's exit state.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\\n\\n<!-- codex-code-review-finding:v1 -->\",\n      \"Url\": \"https://github.com/sharpninja/McpServer/pull/81#discussion_r4300020851\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"Id\": 4300020859,\n      \"ReviewId\": 5554472359,\n      \"CreatedUtc\": \"2026-10-16T22:48:12Z\",\n      \"Path\": \"plugins/core/lib-ps/plugin-hook.ps1\",\n      \"Line\": 1174,\n      \"Commit\": \"6dbc384323c036a57c37fd9eaf2259879c1d956f\",\n      \"Body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Complete the turn after consuming a stop override**\\n\\nFor an `in_progress` code-edit turn with a failed build or incomplete audit, consuming the corresponding acceptance marker returns immediately here, before the later `workflow.sessionlog.completeTurn` branch runs. The stop is therefore allowed while both the cache and authoritative session remain in progress, unlike the previous ordering where completion happened before enforcement; this leaves an unaudited stale turn for the next session. Treat the override as bypassing only its specific gate, then continue through turn completion.\\n\\nAGENTS.md reference: [AGENTS.md:L17-L19](https://github.com/sharpninja/McpServer/blob/6dbc384323c036a57c37fd9eaf2259879c1d956f/AGENTS.md#L17-L19)\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\\n\\n<!-- codex-code-review-finding:v1 -->\",\n      \"Url\": \"https://github.com/sharpninja/McpServer/pull/81#discussion_r4300020859\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n{\n  \"Cli\": \"codex\",\n  \"Version\": \"WARNING: proceeding, even though we could not create PATH aliases: Read-only file system (os error 30)\\ncodex-cli 0.162.1\\n\",\n  \"HelpEvidence\": [\n    {\n      \"Line\": 1,\n      \"Text\": \"WARNING: proceeding, even though we could not create PATH aliases: Read-only file system (os err