{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_161","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/pwsh -NoProfile -Command \"pwsh.exe -NoProfile -NonInteractive -File './docs/receipts/hv/hv-r1-inspect.ps1' -Task Read -Path './docs/architecture/SessionTurn-Review-AgentContext-Architecture-Amendment-1-Durable-HV.md' -Start 453 -Count 58\"","aggregated_output":"SOURCE ./docs/architecture/SessionTurn-Review-AgentContext-Architecture-Amendment-1-Durable-HV.md totalLines=2785\n453: Every entity is new, in `src/QBrainAi.Storage/Entities/HostileValidation/`, keyed by `WorkspaceId` first (every read is workspace-scoped and no read crosses workspaces, foundation section 3), soft-deleted through `IsDeleted` so that `McpDbContext` writes its audit ledger rows for it (R-19), and carries the root ids of every parent it hangs from (foundation section 3.1, \"Root ids\"). Lengths are the foundation's: an agent 64, a session id or request id 256, a readable key 128. Scores are `decimal` with precision 29 and scale 28, written and read as exact lexemes (ScoreLexeme). Every timestamp is UTC with offset, and the identifiers that carry a time use the UTC form `yyyyMMddTHHmmssZ` (D-08). Diagrams are in Addendum B.\n454: \n455: `HvWorkspaceState` (table `HvWorkspaceStates`, key `WorkspaceId`): one row per workspace, created on first use. `LastAssignedReviewerId` (16, null before the first assignment; the round-robin cursor, R-07), `NextNotificationSequence` (long, starts at 1, R-16), `StateVersion` (int).\n456: \n457: `HvReviewer` (table `HvReviewers`, key (`WorkspaceId`, `ReviewerId`)):\n458: \n459: - `ReviewerId` (16): `Cline`, `Copilot`, `Claude`, `Codex`, or `Grok`.\n460: - `Enabled` (bool), `ExecutionStrategy` (32), `AgentPath` (512), `ConfiguredModel` (128, null means the CLI default), `ConfiguredEffort` (32, null means the highest effort of section 10), `MaxConcurrentRuns` (int).\n461: - `ResolvedModel` (128) and `ResolvedEffort` (32): the runtime model and effort the last passing NONCE recorded from the reviewer's own provenance (P-04); null until a NONCE passes.\n462: - `Readiness` (16: `Unverified`, `Online`, `Offline`), `ReadinessReason` (64: the failure code that made it `Offline`, or the change that made it `Unverified`), `ReadinessChangedUtc`, `LastProbeRunId` (128), `OpenIncidentId` (128, the incident that made it `Offline`).\n463: - `ProbeRequestedUtc`: set when a NONCE is requested and cleared when ClaimHvRunCommand creates its probe run; a requested probe waits here, so a NONCE survives a restart before it is claimed.\n464: - `StateVersion` (int: optimistic concurrency for UpdateHvReviewerCommand), `CreatedUtc`, `UpdatedUtc`.\n465: \n466: `HvRequest` (table `HvRequests`, key (`WorkspaceId`, `HvRequestId`), `HvRequestId` = `hvr-<sessionId>-<yyyyMMddTHHmmssZ>`, `-<nn>` from the second key of one second, ReadableKeyAllocator):\n467: \n468: - Scope: `ScopeKind` (16: `Turn`, `Range`, `Session`), `Agent` (64) and `SessionId` (256) of the reviewed MCP session, `FromRequestId` and `ToRequestId` (256; equal for `Turn`, null for `Session`), `ExcludedSubmittingTurn` (bool: a session scope left the submitting turn out, R-05).\n469: - Submitter: `SubmitterKind` (16: `Agent`, `Operator`), the submitting turn key `SubmitterAgent` (64), `SubmitterSessionId` (256), `SubmitterRequestId` (256) (null for `Operator`), `SubmitterReviewerId` (16, AgentIdentity of `SubmitterAgent`, `Unknown` allowed), `OperatorName` (128, `Operator` only), `AuthorReviewerId` (16, AgentIdentity of the reviewed session's `Agent`, `Unknown` allowed; R-08).\n470: - Context: `Context` (text, as submitted; read surfaces redact it through SecretRedactor), `ContextFormat` (16: `Markdown`, `Yaml`, `Text`).\n471: - Idempotency: `IdempotencyKey` (128, unique with `WorkspaceId`), `PayloadSha256` (64, PayloadFingerprint of the client inputs: scope, submitter, context, context format).\n472: - State: `Status` (16: `Queued`, `Running`, `CancelRequested`, `Finalizing`, `Completed`, `Failed`