{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_166","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/pwsh -NoProfile -Command \"pwsh.exe -NoProfile -NonInteractive -File './docs/receipts/hv/hv-r1-inspect.ps1' -Task Read -Path './docs/architecture/SessionTurn-Review-AgentContext-Architecture-Amendment-1-Durable-HV.md' -Start 322 -Count 60\"","aggregated_output":"SOURCE ./docs/architecture/SessionTurn-Review-AgentContext-Architecture-Amendment-1-Durable-HV.md totalLines=2785\n322: \n323: ## 11. Shared components (new, each defined once)\n324: \n325: The foundation's shared components (foundation section 3.5) are reused unchanged: SerializableWrite, IdempotentCreate with PayloadFingerprint, ReadableKeyAllocator, PagedQuery with PageBounds, ClassifiedErrorException with ErrorCodes, SecretRedactor, ContentHasher, TurnLocator, TurnWritePipeline, ScoreLexeme, ScoreVerdict, and WorkspaceResolutionBehavior. The components below are new; each has one implementation, one test class named for it, and one diagram here, and every unit that uses one draws it as a single call node.\n326: \n327: ### 11.1 FencedLease (namespace `QBrainAi.Support.Mcp.Storage.Leases`)\n328: \n329: Claims, renews, and takes over the lease of one row, and guards every fenced write, following develop's handoff-ingestion pattern (`HandoffIngestionService.cs:724-735,782-807`). Operations: `Claim(row, owner, duration)` (only when the row has no lease or an expired one; the fence token increments), `Renew(row, owner, fence, duration)`, `Guard(row, owner, fence)` (the precondition of every fenced write), `Release(row, owner, fence)`. Each runs inside the caller's SerializableWrite. Used by ClaimHvRunCommand, RecordHvRunHeartbeatCommand, AppendHvRunOutputCommand, CloseHvRunOutputCommand, FailHvRunCommand, and ExpireHvRunLeasesCommand.\n330: \n331: ```mermaid\n332: flowchart TD\n333:     S([\"FencedLease: operation, row, owner, fence\"]) --> OP{\"Operation?\"}\n334:     OP -->|Claim| CL{\"Lease absent or expired?\"}\n335:     CL -->|no| E1([\"held: another owner holds a live lease\"])\n336:     CL -->|yes| CT[\"Set owner and expiry, increment the fence token\"]\n337:     CT --> OK1([\"claimed: the new fence token\"])\n338:     OP -->|\"Renew, Guard, or Release\"| G{\"Owner and fence equal the stored ones?\"}\n339:     G -->|no| E2([\"stale_fence: nothing changed\"])\n340:     G -->|yes| W{\"Operation?\"}\n341:     W -->|Renew| RN[\"Extend the expiry\"]\n342:     RN --> OK2([\"renewed\"])\n343:     W -->|Guard| OK3([\"guarded: the caller's write proceeds\"])\n344:     W -->|Release| RL[\"Clear owner and expiry\"]\n345:     RL --> OK4([\"released\"])\n346: ```\n347: \n348: ### 11.2 GzipCodec (namespace `QBrainAi.Support.Mcp.Storage.Compression`)\n349: \n350: `Compress(bytes)` returns one GZIP member; `Decompress(bytes)` returns the original bytes; `RoundTrip(original, compressed)` decompresses and compares length and SHA-256 (through ContentHasher's hex form over raw bytes) and fails with `evidence_corrupt` on any difference, so no compressed blob is stored unverified. It follows `DataAuditLogEntity`'s encode and decode (`DataAuditLogEntity.cs:119-147`); that entity's private copy is context, not work. Used by SubmitHvRequestCommand (request evidence), AppendHvRunOutputCommand (chunks), FinalizeHvRequestCommand (result document, chunk verification), and GetHvEvidenceQuery and OrderedEventReplay (reads).\n351: \n352: ```mermaid\n353: flowchart TD\n354:     S([\"GzipCodec: operation, bytes\"]) --> OP{\"Operation?\"}\n355:     OP -->|Compress| C[\"Write one GZIP member at the configured level\"]\n356:     C --> RT[[\"GzipCodec RoundTrip on the result\"]]\n357:     RT -->|equal| OK1([\"compressed bytes\"])\n358:     RT -->|different| E1([\"evidence_corrupt\"])\n359:     OP -->|Decompress| D{\"Valid GZIP member?\"}\n360:     D -->|no| E2([\"evidence_corrupt\"])\n361:     D -->|yes| OK2([\"original bytes\"])\n362:     OP -->|RoundTrip| R[\"Decompress, compare length and SHA-256 with the original\"]\n363:     R -->|equal| OK3([\"equal\"])\n364:     R -->|different| E3([\"evidence_corrupt\"])\n365: ```\n366: \n367: ### 11.3 AuditLedgerGuard (namespace `QBrainAi.Support.Mcp.Storage.Auditing`)\n368: \n369: `EnsureAvailable()` checks, inside the caller's transaction, that the `DataAuditLogs` table is writable and refuses with 503 `audit_unavailable` (`retryable: true`) when it is not, closing for HV the skip of `McpDbContext.AppendAuditRows` (`McpDbContext.cs:1507-1538`); `RecordRead(entityKind, entityKey, actor)` adds one ledger row with action `read` for an evidence access (R-19). Every HV unit calls `EnsureAvailable()` before any other step that writes; GetHvEvidenceQuery, GetHvResultQuery, and the output stream call `RecordRead` before returning bytes.\n370: \n371: ```mermaid\n372: flowchart TD\n373:     S([\"AuditLedgerGuard: operation\"]) --> A{\"DataAuditLogs writable in this transaction?\"}\n374:     A -->|no| E([\"503 audit_unavailable, retryable: nothing written\"])\n375:     A -->|yes| OP{\"Operation?\"}\n376:     OP -->|EnsureAvailable| OK1([\"available\"])\n377:     OP -->|RecordRead| R[\"Add one ledger row: action read, entity kind and key, actor, request id\"]\n378:     R --> OK2([\"read recorded with the caller's commit\"])\n379: ```\n380: \n381: ### 11.4 AgentIdentity (namespace `QBrainAi.Client.Agents`)\nEXIT_CODE=0\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_167","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/pwsh -NoProfile -Command \"pwsh.exe -NoProfile -NonInteractive -File './docs/receipts/hv/hv-r1-inspect.ps1' -Task Native -CommandName rg -ArgumentText 'StartedUtc|ProcessId|LastProbeRunId|StateVersion|exactly.once:::docs/architecture/SessionTurn-Review-AgentContext-Architecture-Amendment-1-Durable-HV.md:::-n'\"","aggregated_output":"154:- R-12 True live output (S-22, P8). Each reviewer adapter delivers every output line as the process writes it, through a line callback, never after the process ends; the worker appends lines in batches (at most `OutputFlushInterval`, default 250 ms, or `OutputFlushBytes`, default 64 KiB, whichever comes first) through AppendHvRunOutputCommand, which stores each batch as one GZIP chunk and wakes the streams. The output stream replays stored chunks and then follows new ones (shared component OrderedEventReplay). Develop's one-shot strategy yields its output only after completion (`src/QBrainAi.Services/Services/OneShotCliAgentExecutionStrategy.cs:57-75`), so the adapters need a real line path (section 21, P8). Acceptance criterion FR-MCP-HVPIPE-008-AC003 makes the difference testable: a line is observable on the stream while the reviewer process is still running. The reviewer's records are read from each agent message's complete text, assembled from the CLI's native events (Grok's `streaming-json` sends message text one token per event, and Copilot sends deltas and then the whole message, as the probe runs of 2026-10-16 show), by one extraction function that the worker runs as lines arrive and finalization runs over the stored log (section 16.3), so a record split across events is read exactly once and both read the same records (FR-MCP-HVPIPE-010-AC006).\n155:- R-13 Leases and fences (handoff requirement 10). A run is owned through a lease (owner, expiry) and a fence token that increases on every claim and takeover, the pattern develop already uses for handoff ingestion (owner and expiry with a `StateVersion` takeover, `src/QBrainAi.Services/Services/HandoffIngestionService.cs:724-735`, and a fenced terminal write that matches owner and version, `:782-807`). Every worker write carries the fence; a write with a stale fence changes nothing and returns `stale_fence`, and the worker that receives it stops its process. Expired leases are swept (ExpireHvRunLeasesCommand): the attempt becomes `Abandoned` and the request is queued again until `MaxAttemptsPerRequest` (default 3) is spent, then `Failed`, or `Canceled` when a cancel was requested; policy HvRetryDecision writes that outcome, with its turn release and its notification, for the sweep exactly as for FailHvRunCommand. Rejected: the unused lease options of the HostileReview subsystem (`HostileReviewWorkerOptions.cs:30-46`), which no code reads (section 21, P1).\n455:`HvWorkspaceState` (table `HvWorkspaceStates`, key `WorkspaceId`): one row per workspace, created on first use. `LastAssignedReviewerId` (16, null before the first assignment; the round-robin cursor, R-07), `NextNotificationSequence` (long, starts at 1, R-16), `StateVersion` (int).\n462:- `Readiness` (16: `Unverified`, `Online`, `Offline`), `ReadinessReason` (64: the failure code that made it `Offline`, or the change that made it `Unverified`), `ReadinessChangedUtc`, `LastProbeRunId` (128), `OpenIncidentId` (128, the incident that made it `Offline`).\n464:- `StateVersion` (int: optimistic concurrency for UpdateHvReviewerCommand), `CreatedUtc`, `UpdatedUtc`.\n472:- State: `Status` (16: `Queued`, `Running`, `CancelRequested`, `Finalizing`, `Completed`, `Failed`, `Canceled`), `AssignedReviewerId` (16), `AttemptCount` (int), `FailureCode` (64), `CancelRequestedUtc`, `CreatedUtc`, `StartedUtc`, `CompletedUtc`, `StateVersion` (int).\n486:- `Status` (16: `Claimed`, `Running`, `OutputClosed`, `Succeeded`, `Failed`, `Abandoned`, `Canceled`), `ProcessId`, `ClaimedUtc`, `StartedUtc`, `LastHeartbeatUtc`, `LastOutputUtc`, `EndedUtc`, `ExitCode`, `FailureCode` (64), `FailureDetail` (text, sanitized).\n490:- `StateVersion` (int). Unique filtered (`WorkspaceId`, `HvRequestId`) where `Status` is `Claimed`, `Running`, or `OutputClosed`: one live run per request.\n530:- `UpdateHvReviewerRequest { enabled, executionStrategy, agentPath, model, effort, maxConcurrentRuns, expectedStateVersion }`: every field but `expectedStateVersion` optional; `model` and `effort` accept an empty string to return to the default.\n591:- `conflict` 409: `retryable: false` for an idempotency key reused with other inputs or a reviewer update whose `expectedStateVersion` is stale (`details.field` `expectedStateVersion`), `retryable: true` when SerializableWrite or ReadableKeyAllocator is exhausted.\n631:- Validation before the transaction: `expectedStateVersion` required; `executionStrategy`, when present, a supported strategy name; `maxConcurrentRuns` in 1..8; `model` at most 128 and `effort` at most 32 characters; any violation is 400 `validation_error` naming the field.\n632:- Delegate: AuditLedgerGuard; the reviewer row (404 when absent); `StateVersion` equal to `expectedStateVersion`, otherwise 409 `conflict` with `retryable: false` and `details.field` `expectedStateVersion`; apply the fields; when the strategy, agent path, model, or effort changed, set `Readiness` `Unverified` with reason `configuration_changed` and append `reviewer_unverified` (NotificationOutbox); increment `StateVersion`. After the commit the worker is woken, and it NONCEs an enabled `Unverified` reviewer (R-10).\n638:    S([\"Handler runs: PATCH reviewers/{reviewerId}\"]) --> V{\"Fields valid and expectedStateVersion present?\"}\n645:    SW -->|attempt| VER{\"StateVersion equals expectedStateVersion?\"}\n646:    VER -->|no| E5([\"409 conflict, retryable false, details.field expectedStateVersion\"])\n651:    NO --> INC[\"Increment StateVersion\"]\n941:- Delegate: AuditLedgerGuard; then, in this order: (1) a probe: the first enabled reviewer, in pool order, with `ProbeRequestedUtc` set and fewer active runs than its `MaxConcurrentRuns`: insert its `Probe` run (`hvprobe-` key, a fresh 32-byte random `ProbeNonce` in lower-case hex), FencedLease `Claim`, clear `ProbeRequestedUtc`; (2) otherwise a review: the oldest `Queued` request (by `CreatedUtc`, then `HvRequestId`) whose assignee is eligible with capacity, or whose assignee is no longer eligible and for which policy RoundRobinAssignment finds an eligible reviewer with capacity (the reassignment is recorded on the request); insert its `Review` run (`hvrun-<hvRequestId>-<nn>`, `Attempt` = `AttemptCount` + 1), FencedLease `Claim`, set the request `Running` (with `StartedUtc` on the first attempt) and `AttemptCount` + 1, and append `hv_started`. With nothing claimable it returns null and writes nothing; a request whose turns are all frozen stays `Queued` while no reviewer is eligible (ETA `Unknown`, R-18).\n963:    L2 --> RS[\"Request Running, AttemptCount plus 1, StartedUtc on the first attempt\"]\n1283:- V-6 Reviewer turn (`reviewer_turn_unverified`): the `hv_reviewer_turn` record names a turn TurnLocator finds, whose agent AgentIdentity maps to the run's reviewer, whose session is neither the reviewed session nor the submitter's, created at or after the run's `StartedUtc`, whose stored result (its response, then its dialog parts in order with each part's header line removed, as foundation check 6 reads it) contains the `hv_verdict` record byte for byte in its stored normal form (P-06, R-24).\n1533:    Caller->>API: PATCH reviewers/{reviewerId} with expectedStateVersion\n1539:        alt invalid field or no expectedStateVersion\n1548:            else stale expectedStateVersion\n1549:                H-->>Caller: 409 conflict, retryable false, details.field expectedStateVersion\n2200:Actors: the plugin's watcher and the model, Director, any client. Trigger: an HV completes, fails, or is canceled (S-19). Main flow: the plugin's watcher follows the notification stream from its last sequence (WatchHvNotifications, StreamHvNotificationsQuery); a terminal notification for a request its host session submitted goes to the host session's inbox; at the next prompt the plugin adds it to the model's context once, with the overall verdict and how to read the result. Alternates: the stream drops and the watcher reconnects from its recorded sequence, missing nothing; the server restarts and the outbox rows are still there; a client without streams polls (QueryHvNotificationsQuery); a notification arrives twice (at least once) and the sequence deduplicates it. Postconditions: every terminal outcome of a request the host session submitted reaches that session's model exactly once. Invariants: I-12.\n2298:  - AC004 Given an update with a stale `expectedStateVersion`, when it is applied, then 409 `conflict` with `retryable: false` and `details.field` `expectedStateVersion` and nothing changes (`UpdateReviewerStaleStateVersion409NothingChanged`).\n2369:  - AC006 Given native streams of each CLI, recorded from the probe runs of 2026-10-16, in which a record is split across events (Grok's per-token text), repeated in a delta and in the whole message (Copilot), inside a fenced block, or beside other text on its line, when the records are extracted as the lines arrive and again over the stored log, then each record is extracted exactly once, the line with other text is free text, and both extractions return the same records (`ReviewerRecordsExtractedOnceFromAssembledMessagesPerCli`).\n2404:  - AC002 Given a notification stream that drops, or a server that stops after a commit and before any stream delivered its notification (W-07), when the stream reconnects with its last sequence, then it receives every later notification exactly once (`NotificationStreamReconnectNoLossNoDuplicate`).\n2573:Not drawn: `HvReviewer` `ExecutionStrategy`, `AgentPath`, `ConfiguredModel`, `ConfiguredEffort`, `ResolvedModel`, `ResolvedEffort`, `ReadinessReason`, `ReadinessChangedUtc`, `LastProbeRunId`, `OpenIncidentId`, `ProbeRequestedUtc`, `MaxConcurrentRuns`, `CreatedUtc`, `UpdatedUtc`.\n2581:        int StateVersion\n2588:        int StateVersion\n2647:Not drawn: `HvRun` timestamps, `ProcessId`, `ExitCode`, `FailureDetail`, `ExpectedModel`, `ExpectedEffort`, `ProbeNonce`, the output manifest, progress, and provenance columns of section 12; the unique filtered (`WorkspaceId`, `HvRequestId`) where `Status` is live. `HvRunOutputChunk`: unique (`WorkspaceId`, `RunId`, `Sequence`); `LineCount`, `ByteCount`, `FenceToken`, `CreatedUtc`, `RemovedUtc`.\nEXIT_CODE=0\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
