241:       JWT authentication implemented:\n242:       - TokenService generates HS256-signed tokens\n243:       - JwtValidator validates and extracts claims\n244:       - Services registered in Startup.cs\n245:       - All unit tests passing\n246: ```\n247: \n248: ### Failing a Turn\n249: \n250: To mark a turn as failed with an error description:\n251: \n252: ```yaml\n253: type: request\n254: payload:\n255:   requestId: req-20260409T120007Z-fail-001\n256:   method: workflow.sessionlog.failTurn\n257:   params:\n258:     errorMessage: Unable to complete - missing System.IdentityModel.Tokens.Jwt package\n259:     errorCode: dependency_missing\n260: ```\n261: \n262: Both `completeTurn` and `failTurn` produce an immutable terminal state. No further `updateTurn`, `appendDialog`, or `appendActions` calls are allowed on a completed or failed turn.\n263: \n264: ## Querying Session History\n265: \n266: To browse previous sessions for context continuity:\nEXIT_CODE=0\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
