e review: the HV runner launches the reviewer (`codex exec -m <RequiredModel> -c model_reasoning_effort=\"<RequiredEffort>\" --json -`), which reviews the turns of an HV request (CreateAgentContextHvRequestCommand), emits its `=== VERDICT JSON ===`, and stores its entire result on its own session-log turn; when the run completes the runner freezes the request, response, and rollout jsonl receipts (section 6.3). Step 2, the grade-only continuation: the runner resumes the same thread (`codex exec resume <reviewerThreadId> -m <RequiredModel> -c model_reasoning_effort=\"<RequiredEffort>\" --json -`) with a prompt naming the frozen receipt paths, and the HV agent submits one grade per item through `New-McpAgentContextRecordModelGradeParams`, copied from its own verdict; the continuation reviews nothing and changes no receipt. A continuation that fails or is interrupted is resumed again with the same prompt: a resubmitted grade equal to the stored one returns it (200), so retries are safe (`ModelGradeTwoStepProtocolReviewThenContinuationSubmits`, `ModelGradeRetrySameSubmission200Existing`). There is no grading worker or HV pipeline in this effort (operator, 2026-10-11): the runner is the existing HV runner and both steps run the configured grader.\n3380: - REST `POST /qbrainai/agent-context/responses/{responseId}/grades/model`; MCP `agent_context_record_model_grade(string workspacePath, string responseId, string gradeJson)`; client `RecordModelGradeAsync(responseId, RecordModelGradeRequest)`; REPL `client.AgentContext.RecordModelGradeAsync`; PowerShell `New-McpAgentContextRecordModelGradeParams` (also builds the request from the reviewer's verdict: the scores and findings of its `grades` entry for the response copied exactly, the reviewer's own session-log turn ids, its thread id, and the request, response, and rollout jsonl paths); tool descriptor `agent_context_record_model_grade`.\n3381: - Response 201 `AgentResponseGradeResult` with `hvRequestStatus` (`Completed` once