in the bound of four attempts, `ModelGradeHvRequestCompletedDuringReadsReadsAgain409Closed`), inserts the grade, marks the item `Graded` and the HV request `Completed` with `CompletedUtc` when no item stays `Pending`, and dispatches the trust decision in the same transaction.\n3384: - Errors: 400 `validation_error` (`details.field` `workspacePath`, WorkspaceResolutionBehavior; malformed findings, or a finding whose claimId the response does not have), `review_score_format`, `review_score_precision`, `review_score_out_of_range`, `agent_context_receipt_paths_required` (`ModelGradeMissingReceiptPathsOrReviewerIds400ReceiptPathsRequired`); 403 `agent_context_grader_not_allowed` (`ModelGradeOtherGrader403GraderNotAllowed`); 404 `not_found` (`response`, `hv_request`); 409 `agent_context_disabled`, `conflict` with `retryable: false` (a different grade already stored for this response and HV request), `agent_context_response_not_gradable` (`GradeRejectedOrSupersededResponse409ResponseNotGradable`), `agent_context_grade_not_in_hv_request` (`ModelGradeResponseNotItemOfHvRequest409GradeNotInHvRequest`), `agent_context_hv_request_closed` (`ModelGradeCompletedHvRequest409HvRequestClosed`), `conflict` with `retryable: true` (SerializableWrite or ReadableKeyAllocator exhausted after four attempts, or the dispatched EvaluateStalenessCommand exhausted); 422 `agent_context_receipt_unverified`; REPL only (ClientMutationPolicy, before any server call): `transaction_degraded`, `mutation_not_transactional`.\n3385: \n3386: The handler's validation checks that `hvRequestId`, the request, response, and rollout jsonl paths, `reviewerSessionId`, `reviewerRequestId`, and `reviewerThreadId` are present (otherwise `agent_context_receipt_paths_required`), that every finding has a claimId and a check with outcome PASS, FAIL, or UNKNOWN (otherwise `validation_error`), and that the grader agent, model, and effort equal the configured grader. The insert takes a `grd-` key from ReadableKeyAllocator through IdempotentCreate and stores the grade with `hvRequestId`, its findings, the receipt paths and hashes, the thresholds in force, and `RecordedUtc`. The 200 is a retry of the continuation; the 422 names the failed check. One decision holds the three request checks (receipt fields, findings, and the configured grader agent, model, and effort), each refusal on its own edge. The reads are drawn as one call of the nested activity ReadModelGradeInputs and the SerializableWrite with its delegate as one call of the nested activity SaveModelGrade, both below, whose edges are their returns. One 409 `conflict` terminal stands for both conflict answers: `retryable: false` for a different grade already stored for this response and HV request, and `retryable: true` when SerializableWrite or ReadableKeyAllocator is exhausted after four attempts.\n3387: \n3388: ```mermaid\n3389: flowchart TD\n3390:     S([\"Body deserialized: POST grades/model\"]) --> LX[[\"ScoreLexemeJsonConverter: both scores\"]]\n3391:     LX -->|invalid lexeme| E2([\"400 review_score_format, precision, or out_of_range\"])\n3392:     LX -->|\"valid: pipeline, then the handler\"| V{\"Receipt fields, findings, and grader valid?\"}\n3393:     V -->|\"a receipt field missing\"| E5([\"400 agent_context_receipt_paths_required\"])\n3394:     V -->|\"a finding malformed\"| E6([\"400 validation_error\"])\n3395:     V -->|\"not the configured grader\"| E7([\"403 agent_context_grader_not_allowed\"])\n3396:     V -->|yes| ICR[[\"IdempotentCreate lookup, read-only\"]]\n3397:     ICR -->|\"stored, equal submission\"| EXR([\"200 the stored grade\"])\n3398:     ICR -->|\"another grade stored\"| E14([\"409 conflict, retryable only when exhausted\"])\n3399:     ICR -->|absent| RM[[\"ReadModelGradeInputs, no transaction open\"]]\n3400:     RM -->|refused| ER([\"Refusal of ReadModelGradeInputs, drawn there\"])\n3401:     RM -->|\"checks passed, verdict derived\"| SM[[\"SaveModelGrade\"]]\n3402:     SM -->|\"stored, equal submission\"| EXR\n3403:     SM -->|\"another grade stored, or retries exhausted\"| E14\n3404:     SM -->|\"changed: read again\"| ICR\n3405:     SM -->|committed| R([\"201 grade, response status, hvRequestStatus\"])\n3406: ```\n3407: \n3408: ##### Nested activity: ReadModelGradeInputs (reads of RecordModelGradeCommand, before its SerializableWrite)\n3409: \n3410: No transaction is open. The gradable check runs in this order: the response is neither `Rejected` nor `Superseded`, the HV request is `Open`, and the response is an item of it. The eight checks are `receipt_path`, `request_meta`, `verdict_block`, `verdict_binding`, `verdict_match`, `reviewer_turn`, `reviewer_independent`, and `runtime_identity` (section 6.3); they read the frozen receipt files and the reviewer's own session-log turn and compare normal forms (ContentHasher, `ModelGradeVerdictWithEmDashReviewerTurnMatchesInNormalForm`). After every read-only check, the receipt, reviewer, and runtime-identity checks included (section 3.1, Database-only delegates), the dispatched EvaluateStalenessCommand persists `Stale` when a dependency changed; a `Stale` response stays gradable and DecideAgentResponseTrustCommand leaves it `Stale`. ScoreVerdict counts the PASS, FAIL, and UNKNOWN findings at `max(configured, 0.98)`. The diagram draws the response, claim, HV request, and item checks as one call of the nested activity CheckGradeTarget below.\n3411: \n3412: ```mermaid\n3413: flowchart TD\n3414:     S([\"ReadModelGradeInputs: no transaction open\"]) --> CT[[\"CheckGradeTarget\"]]\n3415:     CT -->|refused| ERT([\"Refusal of CheckGradeTarget, drawn there\"])\n3416:     CT -->|\"an item of an Open HV request\"| RV{\"The eight receipt checks pass?\"}\n3417:     RV -->|\"a check fails\"| E13([\"422 agent_context_receipt_unverified\"])\n3418:     RV -->|\"all eight pass\"| EV[\"Dispatch EvaluateStalenessCommand for it\"]\n3419:     EV -->|\"409 conflict, retryable true\"| EC([\"409 conflict, retryable true\"])\n3420:     EV -->|evaluated| VD[[\"ScoreVerdict over the findings\"]]\n3421:     VD --> R([\"Checks passed, verdict derived\"])\n3422: ```\n3423: \n3424: ##### Nested activity: CheckGradeTarget (response, claim, HV request, and item checks of ReadModelGradeInputs)\n3425: \n3426: No transaction is open. The checks run in this order: the response exists in the workspace, every finding's claimId names a claim of the response, the HV request exists in the workspace, and the response is gradable in it (neither `Rejected` nor `Superseded`, the HV request `Open`, and the response an item of it).\n3427: \n3428: ```mermaid\n3429: flowchart TD\n3430:     S([\"CheckGradeTarget: no transaction open\"]) --> F{\"Response in the workspace?\"}\n3431:     F -->|no| E8([\"404 not_found response\"])\n3432:     F -->|yes| CK{\"Each claimId a claim of it?\"}\n3433:     CK -->|no| E6([\"400 validation_error\"])\n3434:     CK -->|yes| HR{\"HV request in the workspace?\"}\n3435:     HR -->|no| E10([\"404 not_found hv_request\"])\n3436:     HR -->|yes| GQ{\"Gradable in that HV request?\"}\n3437:     GQ -->|\"Rejected or Superseded\"| E9([\"409 agent_context_response_not_gradable\"])\n3438:     GQ -->|\"HV request Completed\"| E11([\"409 agent_context_hv_request_closed\"])\n3439:     GQ -->|\"not an item\"| E12([\"409 agent_context_grade_not_in_hv_request\"])\n3440:     GQ -->|yes| R([\"Gradable: an item of an Open HV request\"])\n3441: ```\n3442: \n3443: ##### Nested activity: SaveModelGrade (SerializableWrite of RecordModelGradeCommand, after ReadModelGradeInputs)\n3444: \n3445: The SerializableWrite locks the response. Its delegate reads and writes only the database: it runs the key lookup again, re-checks that the response's status and `StatusVersion` (read after the staleness dispatch), the HV request's status, and the item's disposition are those the reads saw (a change ends the attempt and the unit reads again, within the bound of four attempts), inserts the grade with a `grd-` key from ReadableKeyAllocator, marks the item `Graded` and the HV request `Completed` with `CompletedUtc` when no item stays `Pending`, and dispatches DecideAgentResponseTrustCommand in the same transaction.\n3446: \n3447: ```mermaid\nEXIT_CODE=0\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
