{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_256","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/pwsh -NoProfile -Command \"& './docs/receipts/hv/hv-r1-audit.ps1' -ContentPath './docs/receipts/hv/hv-r1-findings-second-pass.md' -Category decision -WhatIf\"","aggregated_output":"What if: Performing the operation \"Append review dialog\" on target \"Own reviewer turn req-20261017T142304Z-hv-amendment1-r1\".\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_259","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/pwsh -NoProfile -Command \"& './docs/receipts/hv/hv-r1-inspect.ps1' -Task Read -Path './docs/architecture/SessionTurn-Review-AgentContext-Architecture-Amendment-1-Durable-HV.md' -Start 935 -Count 52\"","aggregated_output":"SOURCE ./docs/architecture/SessionTurn-Review-AgentContext-Architecture-Amendment-1-Durable-HV.md totalLines=2785\n935: \n936: Every unit here is internal (R-29): its caller is process HvWorkerHost (section 16.1) or another unit of this section, never a route, tool, or client. Each returns a typed result to its caller; the codes in its list are those results, and none reaches a public surface.\n937: \n938: #### ClaimHvRunCommand: claim the next probe or review [FR-MCP-HVPIPE-003, -007]\n939: \n940: - Handler: `ClaimHvRunCommand(string WorkspacePath, string WorkerId) : ICommand<HvRunClaim?>`; `HvRunClaim { runId, kind, reviewerId, attempt, fenceToken, leaseExpiresUtc, hvRequestId, expectedModel, expectedEffort, probeNonce }`.\n941: - Delegate: AuditLedgerGuard; then, in this order: (1) a probe: the first enabled reviewer, in pool order, with `ProbeRequestedUtc` set and fewer active runs than its `MaxConcurrentRuns`: insert its `Probe` run (`hvprobe-` key, a fresh 32-byte random `ProbeNonce` in lower-case hex), FencedLease `Claim`, clear `ProbeRequestedUtc`; (2) otherwise a review: the oldest `Queued` request (by `CreatedUtc`, then `HvRequestId`) whose assignee is eligible with capacity, or whose assignee is no longer eligible and for which policy RoundRobinAssignment finds an eligible reviewer with capacity (the reassignment is recorded on the request); insert its `Review` run (`hvrun-<hvRequestId>-<nn>`, `Attempt` = `AttemptCount` + 1), FencedLease `Claim`, set the request `Running` (with `StartedUtc` on the first attempt) and `AttemptCount` + 1, and append `hv_started`. With nothing claimable it returns null and writes nothing; a request whose turns are all frozen stays `Queued` while no reviewer is eligible (ETA `Unknown`, R-18).\n942: - Concurrency: the request's state, version, and the one-live-run index are checked and written in the delegate, so two workers never claim one request (W-11).\n943: - Results: a claim; null; 409 `conflict` (`retryable: true`, the worker tries again at its next poll); 503 `audit_unavailable`.\n944: \n945: ```mermaid\n946: flowchart TD\n947:     S([\"ClaimHvRunCommand: workerId\"]) --> SW[[\"SerializableWrite with AuditLedgerGuard\"]]\n948:     SW -->|\"audit unavailable\"| E1([\"503 audit_unavailable\"])\n949:     SW -->|\"attempts exhausted\"| E2([\"409 conflict, retryable true\"])\n950:     SW -->|attempt| P{\"An enabled reviewer with a requested probe and free capacity?\"}\n951:     P -->|yes| PR[\"Insert the Probe run with a fresh nonce; clear ProbeRequestedUtc\"]\n952:     PR --> L1[[\"FencedLease Claim\"]]\n953:     L1 --> R1([\"probe claim\"])\n954:     P -->|no| Q{\"Oldest Queued request whose assignee is eligible with capacity?\"}\n955:     Q -->|yes| RV\n956:     Q -->|\"no, assignee no longer eligible\"| RR[[\"Policy RoundRobinAssignment\"]]\n957:     RR -->|\"no eligible reviewer with capacity\"| NX{\"Another Queued request?\"}\n958:     NX -->|yes| Q\n959:     NX -->|no| R0([\"null: nothing claimable\"])\n960:     RR -->|\"reviewer, reassignment recorded\"| RV[\"Insert the Review run, attempt AttemptCount plus 1\"]\n961:     Q -->|\"no Queued request\"| R0\n962:     RV --> L2[[\"FencedLease Claim\"]]\n963:     L2 --> RS[\"Request Running, AttemptCount plus 1, StartedUtc on the first attempt\"]\n964:     RS --> N[[\"NotificationOutbox: hv_started\"]]\n965:     N --> R2([\"review claim\"])\n966: ```\n967: \n968: #### RecordHvRunHeartbeatCommand: renew the lease and read cancellation [FR-MCP-HVPIPE-007, -008]\n969: \n970: - Handler: `RecordHvRunHeartbeatCommand(string WorkspacePath, string RunId, string WorkerId, long FenceToken) : ICommand<HvHeartbeatResult>`; `HvHeartbeatResult { leaseExpiresUtc, cancelRequested }`.\n971: - Delegate: AuditLedgerGuard; FencedLease `Renew`; `LastHeartbeatUtc`; `cancelRequested` is true when the request is `CancelRequested` (a probe run is never canceled this way).\n972: - Results: renewed; `stale_fence` (the worker stops its process, section 16.2); 409 `conflict` (`retryable: true`); 503 `audit_unavailable`.\n973: \n974: ```mermaid\n975: flowchart TD\n976:     S([\"RecordHvRunHeartbeatCommand: run, worker, fence\"]) --> SW[[\"SerializableWrite with AuditLedgerGuard\"]]\n977:     SW -->|\"audit unavailable\"| E1([\"503 audit_unavailable\"])\n978:     SW -->|\"attempts exhausted\"| E2([\"409 conflict, retryable true\"])\n979:     SW -->|attempt| L[[\"FencedLease Renew\"]]\n980:     L -->|stale_fence| E3([\"stale_fence: nothing changed\"])\n981:     L -->|renewed| H[\"Set LastHeartbeatUtc; read whether the request is CancelRequested\"]\n982:     H --> R([\"renewed: leaseExpiresUtc, cancelRequested\"])\n983: ```\n984: \n985: #### AppendHvRunOutputCommand: persist live output [FR-MCP-HVPIPE-008, -011, -016]\n986: \nEXIT_CODE=0\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_258","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/pwsh -NoProfile -Command \"& './docs/receipts/hv/hv-r1-inspect.ps1' -Task Read -Path './docs/architecture/SessionTurn-Review-AgentContext-Architecture-Amendment-1-Durable-HV.md' -Start 2328 -Count 31\"","aggregated_output":"SOURCE ./docs/architecture/SessionTurn-Review-AgentContext-Architecture-Amendment-1-Durable-HV.md totalLines=2785\n2328:   - AC004 Given that refusal through the plugin verb, when the model receives it, then the report carries the reviewer statuses, the open incidents, and the NONCE remedy text (`HvSubmitVerbNoReviewerAddsContext`, Pester).\n2329:   - AC005 Given the same idempotency key and inputs, when submitted twice, then the second returns 200 with the stored request; with other inputs, 409 `conflict` with `retryable: false` (`SubmitIdempotencyKeyReplayAndReuse`).\n2330:   - AC006 Given any submission surface, when a caller asks to re-review, then no force or re-review parameter exists in any request shape (`SubmitRequestShapeHasNoForceFlag`).\n2331: - FR-MCP-HVPIPE-006 Request context and requirement references. Sources S-14, R-23. UC-HV-03. TR: RequirementReferenceExtractor, HvRequestRequirementRef.\n2332:   - AC001 Given a Markdown or YAML context naming FR, TR, and TEST ids, acceptance-criterion forms, and a use case, when admitted, then each reference is stored in order of first appearance without duplicates, resolved against the effective requirements and use cases, and listed in the brief (`RequirementReferenceExtractorFindsResolvesAndOrders`).\n2333:   - AC002 Given a reference that resolves to nothing, when admitted, then it is listed unresolved and the request is admitted (`RequirementReferenceUnresolvedListedNeverRefused`).\n2334:   - AC003 Given a context over 65536 characters or an unknown format, when submitted, then 400 `validation_error` naming the field (`SubmitContextTooLongOrUnknownFormat400`).\n2335:   - AC004 Given a context holding a secret, when the brief is built, then the secret is redacted in the brief and the stored context is returned redacted on every read surface (`ContextSecretRedactedInBriefAndReads`).\n2336: - FR-MCP-HVPIPE-007 Durable scheduling: queue, leases, fences, and restart safety. Sources S-17, S-24, handoff requirement 10, R-07, R-13. UC-HV-04, UC-HV-09. TR: ClaimHvRunCommand, RecordHvRunHeartbeatCommand, ExpireHvRunLeasesCommand, FencedLease, HvRetryDecision, HvWorkerHost.\n2337:   - AC001 Given a submission, when it commits, then the worker is woken and claims it without a manual trigger, and when the wake-up is lost (a crash after the commit, W-01) the next poll claims it (`SubmitWakesWorkerAutoStart`).\n2338:   - AC002 Given two workers claiming at once, when both run, then exactly one run is claimed per request, on three providers (W-11, `ClaimConcurrentWorkersOneRunPerRequestThreeProviders`).\n2339:   - AC003 Given a run whose lease expired before its process started, while it ran, or after its process exited but before its close committed (W-02, W-03, W-04), when the sweep runs, then the run is `Abandoned`, its fence token is incremented, its output stays stored as evidence (L-02), and the request is `Queued` with attempts left; on its last counted attempt it is `Failed`, and with a cancel requested it is `Canceled`, each ended request with its turns `None`, its `Pending` responses `Closed` with `request_ended`, and `hv_failed` or `hv_canceled` appended, exactly as after FailHvRunCommand (`LeaseExpiryAbandonsFencesAndRequeues`, `LeaseExpiryEndsRequestLikeFailedRun`).\n2340:   - AC004 Given a worker whose lease was taken over, when it appends, heartbeats, closes, or fails, then each answers `stale_fence` and nothing changes (`StaleFenceEveryWorkerWriteRefusedNothingChanged`).\n2341:   - AC005 Given a request `Finalizing` when the server restarted (W-05), when the sweep runs, then FinalizeHvRequestCommand finalizes it once (`SweepFinalizesFinalizingRequestOnce`).\n2342:   - AC006 Given a graceful shutdown during a run, when the worker stops, then the run ends `worker_shutdown`, no incident exists, the reviewer is unchanged, and the attempt is not counted (`GracefulShutdownNotCountedNoIncident`).\n2343:   - AC007 Given two registered workspaces, each with queued requests, when each workspace's worker claims, then no run or request crosses workspaces (`WorkerClaimsOnlyItsWorkspace`).\n2344: - FR-MCP-HVPIPE-008 Execution lifecycle: true live output, heartbeats, no time limit, cancellation. Sources S-18, S-22, P-02, R-11, R-12, R-28. UC-HV-04, UC-HV-08. TR: RunReviewerProcess, StreamReviewerOutput, IHvReviewerAdapter live lines and launch barrier, AppendHvRunOutputCommand, CancelHvRequestCommand.\n2345:   - AC001 Given a reviewer that writes lines over time, when it runs, then every line is appended within `OutputFlushInterval` of being written, in order (`OutputLinesAppendedWithinFlushIntervalInOrder`).\n2346:   - AC002 Given a buffer reaching `OutputFlushBytes`, when the next line arrives, then the buffer is appended at once (`OutputFlushedAtByteThreshold`).\n2347:   - AC003 Given a scripted fake reviewer that writes one line and then blocks on a gate the test controls, when the test reads the run's output stream, then the line arrives while the gate is closed and the process is still running (operator-confirmed P8, `LiveOutputLineObservableBeforeReviewerExits`).\n2348:   - AC004 Given a reviewer running longer than any interval the configuration names, when nothing else happens, then no unit or process ends it (`ReviewerRunHasNoTimeLimit`).\n2349:   - AC005 Given a `Queued` request, when canceled, then it is `Canceled`, its turns are `None`, and `hv_canceled` is appended; given a `Running` request, then it becomes `CancelRequested`, and at the next heartbeat the process is stopped and the request is `Canceled` (`CancelQueuedImmediateRunningAtNextHeartbeat`).\n2350:   - AC006 Given a cancel racing a finalization, a claim, or a close of one request (W-10), when both run, then exactly one commits and the other sees its state, on three providers (`CancelVersusFinalizeOneCommitsThreeProviders`).\n2351:   - AC007 Given a `Finalizing`, `Completed`, or `Failed` request, when canceled, then 409 `hv_request_not_cancelable` (`CancelTerminalOrFinalizing409`).\n2352:   - AC008 Given an interactive session of a reviewer's agent live in the workspace, when a review run and a probe run of that reviewer start and end, then the interactive session's plugin state files and its session-log session are byte-for-byte unchanged, and the reviewer's turn is in a session of its own (H1 Pester per plugin host, and the live check: `ReviewerRunLeavesSameAgentLiveSessionUnchanged`).\n2353:   - AC009 Given each adapter's launch and a reviewer told to create or change a workspace file, when the run ends, then the attempt was refused or the tool was never offered, and the workspace tree outside the plugin's own host-session state is unchanged (H1, per adapter, with the probe streams of 2026-10-16 as fixtures: `ReviewerRunCannotChangeWorkspaceFilesPerAdapter`).\n2354:   - AC010 Given a server-launched reviewer whose host enforces the foundation's Stop gate, when it has emitted its verdict record, then its own `Chore` turn is closed through the completion gate and the process exits on its own, never held open by the gate (H1 Pester per host and the live check: `ReviewerClosesOwnTurnAndExitsUnderStopGate`).\n2355:   - AC011 Given a scripted fake reviewer that starts a child process which keeps the reviewer's output pipes open, when its run is canceled, its fence goes stale, or the ledger fails, and also when the reviewer's root process exits on its own first, then the reviewer and every descendant are ended, the output is read to its end, and the attempt ends with no process left running (H3: `ReviewerStopEndsWholeProcessTree`).\n2356: - FR-MCP-HVPIPE-009 Execution failures: incidents through triage, offline, retry bound. Sources S-15, S-26, R-17. UC-HV-09. TR: FailHvRunCommand, FileHvIncidentCommand, HvIncident, HvRetryDecision.\n2357:   - AC001 Given a reviewer-attributable failure, when recorded, then the reviewer is `Offline` with the code and incident, and an incident is `Pending` with `dedupeKey` `hv-reviewer-<reviewerId>-<code>` (`ReviewerFailureOfflineWithIncident`).\n2358:   - AC002 Given a pending incident, when filed, then the triage service receives its `dedupeKey` and the incident records the report and group ids (`IncidentFiledThroughTriageWithDedupeKey`).\nEXIT_CODE=0\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_257","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/pwsh -NoProfile -Command \"& './docs/receipts/hv/hv-r1-inspect.ps1' -Task Read -Path './docs/architecture/SessionTurn-Review-AgentContext-Architecture-Amendment-1-Durable-HV.md' -Start 290 -Count 61\"","aggregated_output":"SOURCE ./docs/architecture/SessionTurn-Review-AgentContext-Architecture-Amendment-1-Durable-HV.md totalLines=2785\n290: - L-04 A reviewer CLI that cannot report its runtime model and effort cannot pass a NONCE, so it stays `Unverified` or `Offline` (R-10, P-04). Verified on 2026-10-16 (VI-01): Codex, Claude, Grok, and Copilot record both in their own run records; Cline records the model and only whether thinking was on, never the effort level, so Cline cannot pass a NONCE until it records the effort of a run (D-06, settled: P-04 fails closed).\n291: \n292: ## 9. Crash windows and recovery\n293: \n294: Each window names what is durable at the crash and what recovers it. \"Sweep\" is the worker host's periodic pass (process HvWorkerHost).\n295: \n296: - W-01 Crash after the submit commit, before the worker wakes: the request is `Queued` in the store; the next poll claims it.\n297: - W-02 Crash after a claim, before the process starts: the run's lease expires; the sweep marks the attempt `Abandoned` and the request `Queued`, or `Failed` or `Canceled` with its turns released when its attempts are spent or a cancel was requested (ExpireHvRunLeasesCommand, policy HvRetryDecision).\n298: - W-03 Worker crash while the reviewer runs: the reviewer's output pipe closes with the worker; the output already appended is durable; the lease expires and the sweep queues a new attempt. A worker that is alive but lost its lease (a pause longer than the lease) gets `stale_fence` on its next write and stops its process (I-05).\n299: - W-04 Crash after the reviewer exits, before CloseHvRunOutputCommand commits: as W-03, a new attempt runs (L-02).\n300: - W-05 Crash after CloseHvRunOutputCommand commits (request `Finalizing`), before finalization: the sweep dispatches FinalizeHvRequestCommand for every `Finalizing` request (idempotent, I-03).\n301: - W-06 Crash or failure inside the finalization transaction: it rolls back; the request stays `Finalizing` and the sweep runs finalization again.\n302: - W-07 Crash after the finalization commit, before any stream delivers its notification: the notification row is durable; streams and pollers replay it by sequence (R-16).\n303: - W-08 Crash after an incident row commits, before triage filing: the incident stays `Pending`; the sweep files it (FileHvIncidentCommand).\n304: - W-09 Crash after triage accepts a filing, before the report id is recorded: the retry files again under the same `dedupeKey`, which joins the same triage group (L-03).\n305: - W-10 Cancel racing finalization, claim, or close: all of them change the request row inside SerializableWrite, so one commits first and the other sees the committed state (R-28).\n306: - W-11 Two workers claiming one request: the claim is a conditional update on the request's state and version inside SerializableWrite; exactly one claim commits.\n307: - W-12 The audit ledger becomes unavailable during a run: AppendHvRunOutputCommand refuses with 503 `audit_unavailable` and writes nothing; the worker stops the reviewer process (a hard stop, S-29), cannot record the failure while the ledger is down, and the lease expiry later queues a new attempt; nothing is ever reported complete without its audit rows.\n308: \n309: ## 10. Configuration: `HostileValidationOptions`\n310: \n311: Section `Mcp:HostileValidation`, declared under the canonical root as `QBrainAi: HostileValidation:` in `appsettings.yaml` and projected onto `Mcp:` by `CanonicalSectionProjectionProvider`, as foundation section 6.2 declares `AgentContext`; class `HostileValidationOptions` in `src/QBrainAi.Services/HostileValidation/HostileValidationOptions.cs` with `SectionName = \"Mcp:HostileValidation\"`, `Validate()`, and `ValidateOnStart()`; per instance through `McpInstanceResolver`.\n312: \n313: - `Reviewers` (list): exactly one entry for each of `Cline`, `Copilot`, `Claude`, `Codex`, and `Grok` (S-02); each entry has `Enabled` (default true), `ExecutionStrategy` (an existing strategy name, `src/QBrainAi.Services/Services/IAgentExecutionStrategy.cs:6-46`), `AgentPath` (the CLI to launch), `Model` (null means the CLI's default model, recorded from the runtime provenance; Copilot needs a configured model, because its default `auto` routes each prompt to a model of its own choosing, which two probe prompts of 2026-10-16 showed by landing on `mai-code-1.1-flash` and `gpt-6-luna`, and it refuses `--reasoning-effort` without an explicit model, so V-7 could not hold, VI-02), `Effort` (null means the highest effort the reviewer's CLI accepts, verified on 2026-10-16 (VI-08): Codex `max` (its rollout recorded `effort` `max`), Claude `max` (its transcript recorded `effort` `max`), Cline `xhigh` (the highest `--thinking` level), Grok `xhigh` (Grok 1.0.60 refuses `max`: \"unknown effort level 'max'; use one of: xhigh, high, medium, low\"), and Copilot `max` (the highest `--reasoning-effort` value, which the configured model's NONCE proves); develop's one-shot constants at `OneShotCliAgentExecutionStrategy.cs:23-26` differ for Codex (`xhigh`) and Grok (`max`, which Grok refuses), problem P9), and `MaxConcurrentRuns` (default 1, 1..8).\n314: - `MaxTurnsPerRequest` (default 200, 1..2000).\n315: - `MaxAttemptsPerRequest` (default 3, 1..10).\n316: - `LeaseDuration` (default 5 minutes) and `HeartbeatInterval` (default 60 seconds; must be less than half of `LeaseDuration`).\n317: - `OutputFlushInterval` (default 250 milliseconds, 50..5000) and `OutputFlushBytes` (default 65536, 1024..4194304); the default interval is kept only after its storage cost is measured (VI-05).\n318: - `PollInterval` (default 2 seconds) and `WorkerEnabled` (default true).\n319: - There is no execution timeout and no output size limit (R-11, S-22: \"Output should be captured live and streamed\").\n320: - Startup validation fails on an unknown or duplicate reviewer id, a missing one of the five, an unknown execution strategy, an enabled Copilot entry without a configured `Model`, or a value outside its range.\n321: - Seeding: at startup each reviewer entry is inserted as an `HvReviewer` row when the workspace has none for its id (readiness `Unverified`); an existing row is never overwritten, because UpdateHvReviewerCommand is the real-time management surface (S-02), the pattern develop uses for agent definitions seeded per workspace (`SeedWorkspaceAgentsAsync`, `src/QBrainAi.Services/Services/IAgentPoolService.cs:83`).\n322: \n323: ## 11. Shared components (new, each defined once)\n324: \n325: The foundation's shared components (foundation section 3.5) are reused unchanged: SerializableWrite, IdempotentCreate with PayloadFingerprint, ReadableKeyAllocator, PagedQuery with PageBounds, ClassifiedErrorException with ErrorCodes, SecretRedactor, ContentHasher, TurnLocator, TurnWritePipeline, ScoreLexeme, ScoreVerdict, and WorkspaceResolutionBehavior. The components below are new; each has one implementation, one test class named for it, and one diagram here, and every unit that uses one draws it as a single call node.\n326: \n327: ### 11.1 FencedLease (namespace `QBrainAi.Support.Mcp.Storage.Leases`)\n328: \n329: Claims, renews, and takes over the lease of one row, and guards every fenced write, following develop's handoff-ingestion pattern (`HandoffIngestionService.cs:724-735,782-807`). Operations: `Claim(row, owner, duration)` (only when the row has no lease or an expired one; the fence token increments), `Renew(row, owner, fence, duration)`, `Guard(row, owner, fence)` (the precondition of every fenced write), `Release(row, owner, fence)`. Each runs inside the caller's SerializableWrite. Used by ClaimHvRunCommand, RecordHvRunHeartbeatCommand, AppendHvRunOutputCommand, CloseHvRunOutputCommand, FailHvRunCommand, and ExpireHvRunLeasesCommand.\n330: \n331: ```mermaid\n332: flowchart TD\n333:     S([\"FencedLease: operation, row, owner, fence\"]) --> OP{\"Operation?\"}\n334:     OP -->|Claim| CL{\"Lease absent or expired?\"}\n335:     CL -->|no| E1([\"held: another owner holds a live lease\"])\n336:     CL -->|yes| CT[\"Set owner and expiry, increment the fence token\"]\n337:     CT --> OK1([\"claimed: the new fence token\"])\n338:     OP -->|\"Renew, Guard, or Release\"| G{\"Owner and fence equal the stored ones?\"}\n339:     G -->|no| E2([\"stale_fence: nothing changed\"])\n340:     G -->|yes| W{\"Operation?\"}\n341:     W -->|Renew| RN[\"Extend the expiry\"]\n342:     RN --> OK2([\"renewed\"])\n343:     W -->|Guard| OK3([\"guarded: the caller's write proceeds\"])\n344:     W -->|Release| RL[\"Clear owner and expiry\"]\n345:     RL --> OK4([\"released\"])\n346: ```\n347: \n348: ### 11.2 GzipCodec (namespace `QBrainAi.Support.Mcp.Storage.Compression`)\n349: \n350: `Compress(bytes)` returns one GZIP member; `Decompress(bytes)` returns the original bytes; `RoundTrip(original, compressed)` decompresses and compares length and SHA-256 (through ContentHasher's hex form over raw bytes) and fails with `evidence_corrupt` on any difference, so no compressed blob is stored unverified. It follows `DataAuditLogEntity`'s encode and decode (`DataAuditLogEntity.cs:119-147`); that entity's private copy is context, not work. Used by SubmitHvRequestCommand (request evidence), AppendHvRunOutputCommand (chunks), FinalizeHvRequestCommand (result document, chunk verification), and GetHvEvidenceQuery and OrderedEventReplay (reads).\nEXIT_CODE=0\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
