-MCP-SESSIONREVIEW-008, TEST-MCP-SESSIONCLASS-002'\n390:    - \"- TR-MCP-PLUGIN-011 (TR:1625) \\\"Stop gate no-ops phantom turns and counts commits\\\". Changes: AC1 (system-event or zero-work in_progress turns are no-op'd) is replaced, because system events never open turns (TR-MCP-PLUGIN-013) and the stop gate now blocks on any real in_progress request turn and never calls completeTurn; AC2 (commits count) kept. New ACs: TR-MCP-PLUGIN-011-AC001 blocks on in_progress request turns [A7]; -AC002 never calls completeTurn/failTurn and the auto-close at `plugin-hook.ps1:1017` is removed [A7]; -AC003 commits count toward model evidence (former AC2) [A7].\"\n391:    - '- TEST-MCP-PLUGIN-011 (TEST:769). The \"no-ops a task-notification phantom turn\" case becomes \"the prompt hook never opens it\" (A3) and new cases \"blocks a real in_progress turn\" and \"never completeTurn\" (A7). New ACs: TEST-MCP-PLUGIN-011-AC001 [A3], -AC002 [A7].'\n395:    - \"- TEST-MCP-SESSIONLIFE-002 (TEST:1142). Changes: AC001's supersession case becomes the no-cancel case; AC002's exit list adds `skipped_terminal` (A5), and its \\\"Stop ordering\\\" becomes no-auto-close (A7). New ACs: TEST-MCP-SESSIONLIFE-002-AC005 no-cancel [A4]; -AC006 skipped_terminal exit [A5]; -AC007 stop gate blocks and never closes [A7].\"\n408:    - '- FR-MCP-SESSIONLIFE-005 (FR:2118). Changes: AC001 drops \"auto-close\"; statement \"the active turn\" becomes \"every open request turn\". New ACs: FR-MCP-SESSIONLIFE-005-AC006 the stop gate never closes a turn [A7]; -AC007 it blocks while a delivered request (the stop ledger, FR-MCP-SESSIONTURN-003-AC004) is in_progress, blocks a withdrawn request still in_progress with `turn_withdrawn_unclosed`, and only warns for a minted request still `queued` although its server turn is in_progress (D5) [A7].'\n409:    - '- TR-MCP-SESSIONLIFE-005 (TR:2730). Changes: `Close-PluginTurnIfNeeded` blocks instead of closing; \"exact-turn proof\" applies to every open turn. New AC: TR-MCP-SESSIONLIFE-005-AC005 findings function is pure and IO is separated [A7].'\n417:    - \"- FR-MCP-CLEARSESSION-001 (FR:1268), TR-MCP-CLEARSESSION-001 (TR:661). Changes: inline AC1 \\\"finalizing the open turn via workflow.sessionlog.completeTurn\\\" becomes \\\"finalizing each open request turn per the clear-session selection rule (TR-MCP-CLEARSESSION-001-AC001: completeTurn, failTurn, or left in progress)\\\" [S8 coordinator +S9 Node coordinator and skill text], and \\\"byte-identical in all 8 agent plugin repositories\\\" becomes all 9 (grok-bot added, D8) [S9]. Phasing: S8 ships the PowerShell clear-session coordinator runtime in the synced plugin core with its PowerShell RED cases and edits no skill text; because `SyncAgentPlugins` does not copy this skill, S9, after the Node equivalent exists, edits the clear-session skill text in all nine plugin repos at once (the six PowerShell hosts and cline, cline-v2, opencode) and owns the nine-repo byte-parity and gate-step test, hosted in McpServer `tests/Build.Tests` and run in S9's Build.Tests infrastructure step (`dotnet test tests/Build.Tests/Build.Tests.csproj -c Debug`) against the nine repos under the plugin parent `/home/sharpninja/github`, which the S9 and S11 gate commands pass through `MCP_AGENT_PLUGIN_PARENT`, read by the cases and passed to `ResolveAgentPluginParentDirectory` (`build/Build.SyncAgentPlugins.cs:157`, which reads no environment variable itself; the cases fail, never skip, when the variable is unset or fewer than nine repos are found) as `pluginParent` (`ClearSessionSkill_NineReposByteIdentical_ListsSelectionSteps`, `ClearSessionSkill_ListsGateSteps`), not in a per-repo G6 suite. New ACs: TR-MCP-CLEARSESSION-001-AC001 clear-session selects with the shared completion policy before any close, so it holds before S10, for each open request turn addressed by its original (`sessionId`, `requestId`) pair, in this precedence: a withdrawn turn is failed (reason \\\"withdrawn before delivery\\\"); else a turn marked blocked is failed with its blocker reason (blocked takes precedence over a ready completion); else a turn whose completion gate and model-evidence check (FR-MCP-SESSIONTURN-005-AC002) are met is completed; else it stays in progress, reported by requestId with its exact missing items; `failed` requires `requestClass` only, and no review is ever fabricated. \\\"Marked blocked\\\" means the turn's `blockers` section (the existing decision-list field, FR-MCP-SESSIONTURN-006-AC001) holds at least one nonblank model-authored entry, read by the coordinator for that turn by its original pair; the first entry is the fail reason (operator option A, 2026-10-10). Before failing a withdrawn or blocked turn, the coordinator checks its close prerequisites in the Stop gate remedy order (FR-MCP-SESSIONTURN-005-AC009): model evidence (FR-MCP-SESSIONTURN-005-AC002) and a `requestClass` that is neither missing nor `Unclassified`. A turn that lacks one is not sent to `failTurn`: the coordinator reports it by requestId with its `queryText`, the reason it will be failed with, and each missing prerequisite; within the same clear-session run, before its session-end step, the model writes them by the original pair (a designDecision, then the class, Code, Docs, or Chore, judged from that `queryText`), and the coordinator runs again, reads them back by that pair, and fails the turn with its reason, so neither the plugin's evidence check nor the server gate refuses a clear-session fail [S8 +S9 +S10]; TR-MCP-CLEARSESSION-001-AC002 the clear-session skill text is byte-identical in all nine plugin repos and lists the selection and gate steps, with evidence `ClearSessionSkill_NineReposByteIdentical_ListsSelectionSteps` and `ClearSessionSkill_ListsGateSteps` in the Build.Tests infrastructure step, not a TEST record [S9; S11 re-runs it].\"\n422:    - \"UC-3 Close every request turn before stopping. Actors: model, host Stop hook. Basic flow: model records actions/decisions (incl. via `designDecisions`) and closes each turn; Stop hook finds all closed with evidence and passes, clearing the ledger. Alternate: a turn is open (including one whose close the plugin refused for missing model evidence) or its most recent close was refused by the server's completion gate, the Stop hook blocks with the reason and the accepted remedy; a turn closed without evidence by another surface is only warned and never closes turns itself. Alternate: the host session failed closed under D6 (`unsupportedSince`) while a turn was open; the Stop hook blocks with the reduced remedy (only the missing model evidence, the missing `requestClass` from S8/S9, and the close call; the terminal reviews are judged at the drain), the model's evidence and close for that turn are captured in the plugin failsafe (reviews are refused and recorded after the drain through the original pair), the next Stop warns instead of blocking, and the next SessionStart drains the captured records with the turn's original pair through the trusted recovery flow. Realizes FR-MCP-SESSIONTURN-005, -006; updated FR-MCP-SESSIONLIFE-005, FR-MCP-CLEARSESSION-001.\"\n439:    - '  - A7: SESSIONTURN-003-003; SESSIONTURN-005-001, -002, -004..009; extensions of SESSIONTURN-003-004, -007-004, -007-007 (Stop side).'\n461:    - '  - A7: TR-MCP-PLUGIN-011-AC001..AC003; TEST-MCP-PLUGIN-011-AC002; TEST-MCP-SESSIONLIFE-002-AC007; FR-MCP-SESSIONLIFE-005-AC006, -AC007; TR-MCP-SESSIONLIFE-005-AC005.'\n470:    - '  - Changed existing ACs (text edits; RED first in the slice shown): A3: FR-MCP-SESSIONLIFE-001-AC002; A4: FR-MCP-SESSIONLIFE-001-AC005, FR-MCP-SESSIONLIFE-002-AC004, FR-MCP-SESSIONLIFE-003-AC003, TR-MCP-SESSIONLIFE-002-AC002, -AC003, TEST-MCP-SESSIONLIFE-002-AC001, FR-MCP-TRIAGESTORE-001 ac-1; A5: FR-MCP-SESSIONLIFE-003-AC001, -AC002 (the per-turn `turns[]` outcome fields of the A5 mapping), TR-MCP-SESSIONLIFE-003-AC001, -AC002, TEST-MCP-SESSIONLIFE-002-AC002 (its wrapper-exit list with `skipped_terminal`); A7: FR-MCP-SES