cking again while turns are open and recording `stop_gate_overridden_by_host` if the host stops anyway; passes with `{}` and clears closed entries. Auto-close removed. Block text: `session_turn_stop_gate: <n> turn(s) are not closed correctly:` then one line per turn `<id> (<code>): <remedy>`, then `The stop gate never closes turns for you.`; each turn's remedy accumulates every unmet prerequisite of that turn, in this order: for a turn whose most recent close the server refused with `session_turn_completion_gate`, the server's missing items first (in place of the locally computed `requestClass` and review items); at least one model-authored action, designDecision, or commit (FR-MCP-SESSIONTURN-005-AC002); `requestClass` (from S8/S9, when the plugin's requestClass and recordReview verbs ship); the terminal reviews the completion gate names (from S8/S9, when the plugin's requestClass and recordReview verbs ship, gate order; before S10 the server accepts those writes, so following the remedy literally still passes); then the single close call valid for its status: `workflow.sessionlog.failTurn` with reason 'withdrawn before delivery' for a withdrawn request, otherwise `workflow.sessionlog.completeTurn` (or `failTurn` if the work failed), passing requestId <id>. Following a turn's remedy literally makes the next Stop pass for that turn, including a Code turn that lacks both model evidence and terminal reviews (`StopGate_EachRemedyFollowedLiterally_NextStopPasses`, `StopGate_CodeTurn_MissingEvidenceAndReviews_AccumulatedRemedy_NextStopPasses`).\"\n504:    - \"A3 MCP-SESSIONTURN-003 Ingress mint and system-event classifier (plugin). Reqs SESSIONTURN-001 (plugin mint ACs), -002. Contract: the atomic `turn-state.yaml` queue, delivery, and write-target writer used by the bridge and by the prompt hook on hosts without a bridge (a prompt-hook mint is delivered at once and becomes the host session's write target, TR-MCP-SESSIONTURN-001 AC-005 and AC-006; A4 adds the invocation 