uginTurnReview`, `-RequestClass`. `repl-invoke.ps1`: `Protect-ReplLosslessScalars` in `Convert-ReplParamsYamlToObject` (414-434) for `correctness`, `completeness`, `reviewedAt` (block, flow, JSON); `Invoke-WorkflowRecordReview` (targets the D2 invocation binding or the `requestId` override (required under D9 while two or more delivered requests are open), or for a turn of an earlier MCP session its original (`sessionId`, `requestId`) pair (FR-MCP-SESSIONREVIEW-002-AC002, C5), which is how a turn that is no longer its session's write target is reviewed; works on terminal turns; no failsafe so an older queued review never overwrites a newer one, including in a host session with `unsupportedSince`, where a review is refused and recorded after the drain through the original pair (`UnsupportedSession_ReviewRefused_NotCaptured`), the gate-rejected drain being an S10 case); requestClass on update/complete/fail; advisory local completion pre-check (reports the missing items with the exact gate message as a warning before the close is sent and never refuses a close; for an already open turn of a host session with `unsupportedSince`, the close goes to the failsafe per FR-MCP-SESSIONTURN-005-AC001, FR-MCP-SESSIONCLASS-004-AC002); server gate rejection is reported with the server's message and missing items, keeps turn in_progress, and clears failsafe, including for a drained `unsupported_session` close; stop gate adds `session_turn_completion_gate` for a turn whose most recent close the server refused with that code. RED: new `SessionTurnReviewGate.Tests.ps1` (unsupported-session cases against a server double: a Code turn missing reviews is open, `unsupportedSince` is recorded, the advisory pre-check warns and the close goes into the failsafe with no server write, and Stop warns (`Precheck_UnsupportedSession_CodeTurnMissingReviews_CloseCaptured_NoServerWrite`); a review in that session is refused and not captured (`UnsupportedSession_ReviewRefused_NotCaptured`); the pre-check 