{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_283","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/pwsh -NoProfile -Command \"& './docs/receipts/hv/hv-r1-inspect.ps1' -Task Read -Path './docs/architecture/SessionTurn-Review-AgentContext-Architecture-Amendment-1-Durable-HV.md' -Start 2360 -Count 39\"","aggregated_output":"SOURCE ./docs/architecture/SessionTurn-Review-AgentContext-Architecture-Amendment-1-Durable-HV.md totalLines=2785\n2360:   - AC004 Given triage unreachable, or a crash after the incident committed and before its filing (W-08), when filing, then the incident stays `Pending` with the error and the next sweep files it (`IncidentFilingRetriedUntilFiled`).\n2361:   - AC005 Given attempts spent, when the last attempt fails, then the request is `Failed` with `attempts_exhausted`, its turns are `None`, and `hv_failed` is appended (`AttemptsExhaustedRequestFailedTurnsReleased`).\n2362:   - AC006 Given a server-attributable failure (`evidence_corrupt`, `snapshot_changed`, `reviewer_not_independent`), when recorded, then an incident with `hv-server-<code>` exists and the reviewer is unchanged (`ServerFailureIncidentReviewerUnchanged`).\n2363: - FR-MCP-HVPIPE-010 Reviewer output contract, per-turn and holistic evaluation. Sources S-03, S-10, S-13, S-21, R-31. UC-HV-05. TR: reviewer contract v1, IHvReviewerAdapter ExtractReviewerRecords, HvFinalVerification V-4 and V-8, HvTurnAssessment, HvFinding.\n2364:   - AC001 Given a log with one assessment per member, one holistic record, and one verdict record last, when finalized, then each requested turn has its score and the holistic evaluation is stored separately (`FinalizeStoresPerTurnScoresAndSeparateHolistic`).\n2365:   - AC002 Given a log missing an assessment, with two verdict records, without a holistic record, or with a finding without remediation, when finalized, then `reviewer_output_invalid` and nothing is committed (`FinalizeIncompleteOutputRefusedNothingCommitted`).\n2366:   - AC003 Given a holistic correctness of 0.97 with every turn AGREE, when finalized, then the overall verdict is DISAGREE (`OverallVerdictHolisticBelow098Disagree`); given an AGREE verdict with a FAIL finding, then `reviewer_output_invalid` (`VerdictAgreeWithFailFindingRefused`).\n2367:   - AC004 Given turn scores whose mean differs from the holistic scores, when finalized, then the stored holistic scores are the reviewer's own, never recomputed (`HolisticScoresNeverComputedFromTurnScores`).\n2368:   - AC005 Given a record the reviewer forged as `hv_provenance` or `hv_brief` inside its message text, when the log is read, then it is not accepted as a worker record (`ForgedWorkerRecordInMessageTextIgnored`).\n2369:   - AC006 Given native streams of each CLI, recorded from the probe runs of 2026-10-16, in which a record is split across events (Grok's per-token text), repeated in a delta and in the whole message (Copilot), inside a fenced block, or beside other text on its line, when the records are extracted as the lines arrive and again over the stored log, then each record is extracted exactly once, the line with other text is free text, and both extractions return the same records (`ReviewerRecordsExtractedOnceFromAssembledMessagesPerCli`).\n2370:   - AC007 Given a run that exits with code 0 and holds no reviewer records (an empty output, or a stream its CLI ended `cancelled`), when it closes, then a review fails with `reviewer_output_invalid`, the reviewer is `Offline` with an incident, and a probe fails with `probe_nonce_mismatch`; an exit code never stands in for a verdict (`ExitZeroWithoutReviewerRecordsIsNotAReview`).\n2371: - FR-MCP-HVPIPE-011 Evidence completeness, GZIP at rest, round-trip verification. Sources S-13, S-30, R-12, R-14. UC-HV-04, UC-HV-05, UC-HV-10. TR: GzipCodec, HvEvidence, HvRunOutputChunk, V-1.\n2372:   - AC001 Given an accepted request and a run's lines, when stored, then every payload is a GZIP member that decompresses to the exact bytes, and no uncompressed copy is stored (`EvidenceStoredGzipOnlyRoundTripExact`).\n2373:   - AC002 Given a chunk whose bytes, SHA-256, or chain hash was altered, or a missing sequence, when finalized, then `evidence_corrupt` and nothing is committed (`FinalizeCorruptOrTruncatedLogRefused`).\n2374:   - AC003 Given a compression whose round trip fails, when admitted or appended, then 500 `evidence_corrupt` and nothing is saved (`CompressionRoundTripFailureNothingSaved`).\n2375:   - AC004 Given a finalized run, when the response log is downloaded compressed and read back as one GZIP stream (VI-07), then decompression yields every stored line in order and its SHA-256 chain equals the run's (`ResponseLogDownloadMultiMemberGzipMatchesChain`).\n2376:   - AC005 Given a reviewer output of any size, when appended, then no limit truncates it (`OutputHasNoSizeLimitNeverTruncated`).\n2377: - FR-MCP-HVPIPE-012 Atomic finalization and turn finality. Sources S-06, S-07, S-23, R-04, R-15. UC-HV-05, UC-HV-12. TR: FinalizeHvRequestCommand, CommitFinalResult, HvTurnFreeze, A-07, A-08, A-11.\n2378:   - AC001 Given a fault injected after each write of CommitFinalResult (W-06), when finalization runs, then nothing of the result is visible after the rollback, the request stays `Finalizing`, and the next sweep finalizes it, on three providers (`FinalizeFaultAfterEachWriteNothingVisibleThreeProviders`).\n2379:   - AC002 Given an admitted turn, when any turn write, review write, review reset, section write, dialog append, title change, or session replace or delete targets it from any origin but `HvFinalization`, then 409 `turn_immutable` with `hv_pending`, and after finalization with `hv_final` (`FrozenTurnEveryWritePathRefused`).\n2380:   - AC003 Given a canceled or failed request, when it ends, then its turns are writable again (`EndedRequestReleasesTurns`).\n2381:   - AC004 Given a request finalized, when FinalizeHvRequestCommand runs again, then it returns the stored outcome and writes nothing (`FinalizeTwiceSecondReturnsStoredNothingWritten`).\n2382:   - AC005 Given a member turn changed by a path that bypasses the guard (a fixture writing the store directly), when finalized, then V-2 refuses with `snapshot_changed` (`FinalizeSnapshotChangedRefused`).\n2383:   - AC006 Given a `Code` turn completed with hostile review `Other` \"HV requested\", when its HV finalizes, then its hostile review holds the HV result and its status stays `completed` (`FinalizeReplacesOtherPendingHvReviewKeepsStatus`).\n2384:   - AC007 Given turns whose hostile review is `Pass` or `Fail`, `Other`, or absent when the A-11 migration adds the HV columns, when the migration runs, then exactly the `Pass` and `Fail` turns are `Final` with no request id, every write to them is refused with 409 `turn_immutable` `hv_final`, and an HV over them is refused with 409 `hv_turns_already_reviewed`, on three providers (HvStorageSchema: `MigrationMarksHvReviewedTurnsFinalThreeProviders`).\n2385: - FR-MCP-HVPIPE-013 Self-review independence. Sources S-28, R-21. UC-HV-03, UC-HV-05. TR: HvAdmissionEligibility, TurnSnapshotBuilder, HvFinalVerification.\n2386:   - AC001 Given one turn with no agent review, one with `Unstarted`, one with `Running`, one with `Pass` at 1.0, one with `Fail` at 0.1, and one with `Other`, all otherwise equal, when each is submitted, then admission, assignment, and the brief bytes are identical (`SelfReviewVariedAdmissionAssignmentAndBriefIdentical`).\n2387:   - AC002 Given those turns reviewed with the same reviewer output, when finalized, then the stored hostile reviews and verdicts are identical (`SelfReviewVariedVerdictIdentical`).\n2388:   - AC003 Given the HostileValidation assemblies, when scanned, then no HV unit, policy, or process reads an `agentReview` field (architecture test `HostileValidationNeverReadsAgentReview`).\n2389: - FR-MCP-HVPIPE-014 Verdict only: no TODO automation. Sources S-25, R-22. UC-HV-05, UC-HV-12. TR: FinalizeHvRequestCommand.\n2390:   - AC001 Given member turns naming TODOs, when an HV finalizes AGREE or DISAGREE, then every TODO is byte-for-byte unchanged (`FinalizeNeverChangesTodos`).\n2391:   - AC002 Given the HostileValidation assemblies, when scanned, then none references the TODO write services (architecture test `HostileValidationHasNoTodoWriteDependency`).\n2392: - FR-MCP-HVPIPE-015 Results, evidence retrieval, and the standard result document. Sources S-13, S-18, S-21. UC-HV-06, UC-HV-10. TR: GetHvRequestQuery, QueryHvRequestsQuery, GetHvResultQuery, GetHvEvidenceQuery, HvResultDocument.\n2393:   - AC001 Given a completed request, when its result is read, then it holds the complete accepted request, every log record in order, every requested turn with its score, the holistic evaluation, and every FAIL and UNKNOWN with remediation (`ResultDocumentCompleteAndDelineated`).\n2394:   - AC002 Given a request not completed, when its result is read, then 409 `hv_result_not_ready` (`ResultBeforeCompletion409`).\n2395:   - AC003 Given running requests, when queried with `status` `Running`, then each has its reviewer, progress, ETA status, and, when read singly, its last 20 lines (`RunningRequestsQueryAndLastOutput`).\n2396:   - AC004 Given the REST, MCP, client, REPL, and Director surfaces, when each submits, reads, queries, cancels, and retrieves, then each returns the same shapes and codes (`HvSurfacesParityGoldenContract`).\n2397: - FR-MCP-HVPIPE-016 Live output stream, progress, and honest ETA. Sources S-18, S-22, P-03, R-12, R-18. UC-HV-06. TR: StreamHvRunOutputQuery, OrderedEventReplay.\n2398:   - AC001 Given a stream attached mid-run, when the caller reconnects with its last event id, then it receives exactly the missed chunks and then live chunks (`OutputStreamReconnectExactlyMissedEvents`).\nEXIT_CODE=0\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
